window.IELTS_DATA={"masters":[{"id":"M01","title":"同事Adam","keywords":"认识同事 → 做事有条理 → 我遇到困难 → 他教方法 → 我的变化。","script":["I'd like to talk about a colleague of mine called Adam. We met at work about two years ago, and we gradually became friends. He's a few years older than me, and he's someone I often turn to when I need advice.","What stands out about him is how organised he is. Before starting a task, he writes down the main steps and decides what needs to be done first. He doesn't make things complicated. In fact, he's usually the person who makes a confusing situation easier to understand.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Since then, I've tried to follow his approach. Whenever a task feels overwhelming, I break it into smaller steps. So he's had a positive influence on the way I work."],"variants":[{"name":"教我表达技能","answer_script":["The person I'd like to describe is my colleague Adam, who taught me how to present a complicated idea clearly. We met at work about two years ago, and he is a few years older than me. Before he helped me, I often included too many details when explaining something.","What stands out about him is how organised he is. Before starting a task, he writes down the main steps and decides what needs to be done first. He doesn't make things complicated. In fact, he's usually the person who makes a confusing situation easier to understand.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Since then, I've tried to follow his approach. Whenever a task feels overwhelming, I break it into smaller steps. So he's had a positive influence on the way I work."],"module":"The person I'd like to describe is my colleague Adam, who taught me how to present a complicated idea clearly. We met at work about two years ago, and he is a few years older than me. Before he helped me, I often included too many details when explaining something.","omit":""},{"name":"性格乐观","answer_script":["A happy person I know is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and gradually became friends. He isn't excited all the time, but he usually seems comfortable with himself and finds something positive in an ordinary day.","He enjoys small things, like having a good conversation or helping someone finish a task. When a plan goes wrong, he tends to focus on what we can try next rather than complain about the whole situation. That makes it pleasant to work with him.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","I think he is a happy person because he doesn't expect everything to be perfect. He puts effort into things he can change and doesn't spend the whole day worrying about things he can't control. Being around him often improves my mood."],"module":"A happy person I know is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and gradually became friends. He isn't excited all the time, but he usually seems comfortable with himself and finds something positive in an ordinary day. He enjoys small things, like having a good conversation or helping someone finish a task. When a plan goes wrong, he tends to focus on what we can try next rather than complain about the whole situation. That makes it pleasant to work with him. I think he is a happy person because he doesn't expect everything to be perfect. He puts effort into things he can change and doesn't spend the whole day worrying about things he can't control. Being around him often improves my mood.","omit":""},{"name":"爱拍照","answer_script":["A person I know who really enjoys photography is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and became friends. Outside work, he often takes photos of ordinary streets, small shops and interesting patterns in buildings.","He usually uses his phone rather than carrying a lot of equipment. What I like about his photos is that he notices details other people walk past. He might photograph the reflection in a window or the shadow of a tree instead of a famous landmark.","Last month, we went for a walk near Dubai Creek. I took a quick photo and thought the scene looked rather ordinary. Adam suggested moving a few steps to the side and waiting until fewer people were in the picture. The result looked much clearer.","He also explained that good light matters more than simply having an expensive camera. I enjoyed learning something practical without having to study a long list of technical terms. We compared our pictures afterwards and talked about why they looked different.","I appreciate his hobby because it encourages him to pay attention to his surroundings. His example has made me look more carefully when I go for a walk. I still don't take photos as seriously as he does, but I understand why he enjoys it."],"module":"A person I know who really enjoys photography is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and became friends. Outside work, he often takes photos of ordinary streets, small shops and interesting patterns in buildings. He usually uses his phone rather than carrying a lot of equipment. What I like about his photos is that he notices details other people walk past. He might photograph the reflection in a window or the shadow of a tree instead of a famous landmark. Last month, we went for a walk near Dubai Creek. I took a quick photo and thought the scene looked rather ordinary. Adam suggested moving a few steps to the side and waiting until fewer people were in the picture. The result looked much clearer. He also explained that good light matters more than simply having an expensive camera. I enjoyed learning something practical without having to study a long list of technical terms. We compared our pictures afterwards and talked about why they looked different. I appreciate his hobby because it encourages him to pay attention to his surroundings. His example has made me look more carefully when I go for a walk. I still don't take photos as seriously as he does, but I understand why he enjoys it.","omit":""},{"name":"只见过一次","answer_script":["A person I only met once but would like to know better is a man called Adam. I met him at a small photography workshop last month. We spoke for about twenty minutes while practising how to take pictures of the street outside.","I noticed him because he was using a basic phone but still taking interesting photos. He didn't seem concerned about having the most expensive equipment. Instead, he paid attention to the light, the background and the position of the people in the picture.","When I asked how he made an ordinary scene look so good, he showed me a simple example. He moved a little to one side, waited for a person to walk past and then took the photo. That small change made the picture much more balanced.","He explained the idea patiently and asked me to try it myself. I liked the fact that he was willing to share what he knew without making me feel inexperienced. Before we left, he mentioned that he enjoyed photographing different cities.","I'd like to know more about his travels and see some of those photographs. He seemed observant, friendly and easy to talk to. Although our conversation was short, I came away with a useful idea and the feeling that we could have an interesting conversation again."],"module":"A person I only met once but would like to know better is a man called Adam. I met him at a small photography workshop last month. We spoke for about twenty minutes while practising how to take pictures of the street outside. I noticed him because he was using a basic phone but still taking interesting photos. He didn't seem concerned about having the most expensive equipment. Instead, he paid attention to the light, the background and the position of the people in the picture. When I asked how he made an ordinary scene look so good, he showed me a simple example. He moved a little to one side, waited for a person to walk past and then took the photo. That small change made the picture much more balanced. He explained the idea patiently and asked me to try it myself. I liked the fact that he was willing to share what he knew without making me feel inexperienced. Before we left, he mentioned that he enjoyed photographing different cities. I'd like to know more about his travels and see some of those photographs. He seemed observant, friendly and easy to talk to. Although our conversation was short, I came away with a useful idea and the feeling that we could have an interesting conversation again.","omit":"这是初次见面版本；不保留认识两年的同事关系。"},{"name":"成功企业员工","answer_script":["I'd like to talk about Adam, a colleague who works for a successful software company. I've known him for about two years. The company has developed a practical product that helps its customers handle repeated tasks, and Adam works on making the product easier to use.","I think the company has done well because it understands what its customers actually need. It doesn't try to add every possible feature at once. Adam follows the same approach in his own work: he sets a clear goal and keeps the solution simple.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Talking to Adam has helped me understand that a successful company needs useful products and people who communicate clearly. I admire his contribution because he pays attention to the person using the product. That is a quality I'd like to develop in my own work."],"module":"I'd like to talk about Adam, a colleague who works for a successful software company. I've known him for about two years. The company has developed a practical product that helps its customers handle repeated tasks, and Adam works on making the product easier to use. I think the company has done well because it understands what its customers actually need. It doesn't try to add every possible feature at once. Adam follows the same approach in his own work: he sets a clear goal and keeps the solution simple. Talking to Adam has helped me understand that a successful company needs useful products and people who communicate clearly. I admire his contribution because he pays attention to the person using the product. That is a quality I'd like to develop in my own work.","omit":""},{"name":"聪明解题","answer_script":["I'd like to describe my colleague Adam, who helped solve a problem in a simple but clever way. We met at work about two years ago. I often ask him for advice because he can identify what is actually making a task difficult.","The problem was that I had too much information in a presentation. My first reaction was to add even more explanation. Adam suggested doing the opposite: remove the unnecessary details and show one example that people could easily understand.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Since then, I've tried to follow his approach. Whenever a task feels overwhelming, I break it into smaller steps. So he's had a positive influence on the way I work."],"module":"I'd like to describe my colleague Adam, who helped solve a problem in a simple but clever way. We met at work about two years ago. I often ask him for advice because he can identify what is actually making a task difficult. The problem was that I had too much information in a presentation. My first reaction was to add even more explanation. Adam suggested doing the opposite: remove the unnecessary details and show one example that people could easily understand.","omit":""},{"name":"受欢迎的人","answer_script":["A popular person I know is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and gradually became friends. Many people in our team enjoy working with him because he is approachable and takes other people's questions seriously.","He remembers small things about people and is willing to help without making a big show of it. For example, if someone is new to the team, he explains the basic information and checks whether they are comfortable asking questions. That makes people feel included.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","I think he is popular because people feel respected around him. He doesn't need to dominate a conversation or impress everyone. His friendliness and willingness to help are enough. I enjoy his company for the same reasons, and I try to learn from the way he treats others."],"module":"A popular person I know is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and gradually became friends. Many people in our team enjoy working with him because he is approachable and takes other people's questions seriously. He remembers small things about people and is willing to help without making a big show of it. For example, if someone is new to the team, he explains the basic information and checks whether they are comfortable asking questions. That makes people feel included. I think he is popular because people feel respected around him. He doesn't need to dominate a conversation or impress everyone. His friendliness and willingness to help are enough. I enjoy his company for the same reasons, and I try to learn from the way he treats others.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M01","name":"open_minded","keywords":"Adam → 不同意见 → 小原型 → 试验 → 接受结果","note":"Adam、认识方式、团队讨论及原型结果全部为样例。主体是他如何认真听取不同观点，并用具体行为证明思想开放；不只是夸他聪明或乐观。","answer_script":["An open-minded person I know is my colleague Adam. We've worked together for two years, and I appreciate the way he listens when people suggest a different approach. He doesn't seem to feel that he needs to defend his first idea immediately.","One example was a discussion about a small tool our team wanted to build. I was in favour of creating a complete system, while another colleague suggested testing a simple version first. At the beginning, Adam also seemed interested in planning more features in advance.","However, he asked the colleague to explain what we could learn from a small prototype. He listened carefully and asked practical questions about the time involved and how we would check the result. He also made sure that I had a chance to explain my concerns.","After the discussion, he supported trying the smaller version. We agreed on one basic task, tested it with a few examples and used the results to decide what to do next. The approach gave us useful information before we committed more time to the project.","What impressed me was that Adam changed his view after considering the explanation. He didn't simply agree to avoid an argument. His questions showed that he was thinking seriously about the idea. I enjoy working with him because different opinions can become something useful instead of making the conversation uncomfortable."]}],"followups":[{"q":"What skill did he teach you?","a":"He taught me to begin with one clear message and support it with an example. I used to explain every detail at once. Now I check what the listener actually needs to understand before adding more information.","q_zh":"他教会了你什么技能？"},{"q":"Do you still use his advice?","a":"Yes, especially when I explain an unfamiliar idea at work. I write down the main point first and remove information that doesn't support it. That preparation usually makes me less nervous during the conversation.","q_zh":"你现在还会采用他的建议吗？"},{"q":"Could you teach the skill to someone else?","a":"I could share the basic method and help them practise. I wouldn't claim to be an expert, but listening to their explanation and pointing out unclear parts would be a useful starting point.","q_zh":"你能把这项技能教给别人吗？"}],"category":"人物","title_en":"Adam, a helpful and organised colleague","audio":"audio/c00af183d1131772.m4a"},{"id":"M02","title":"小说与电影The Martian","keywords":"推荐 → 被困火星 → 一次解决一个问题 → 紧张但有幽默 → 对我的启发。","script":["I'd like to talk about a novel called The Martian, by Andy Weir. I read it a few months ago after a friend recommended it. I usually prefer stories that feel practical, so the combination of science and adventure appealed to me.","The main character is an astronaut called Mark Watney, who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to find ways to stay alive and contact people on Earth. The situation sounds hopeless, but he doesn't give up. He deals with one problem at a time, using whatever resources he has.","What I enjoyed most was the way he thought through his difficulties. The book made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the story enjoyable as well.","I read a little in the evening, and I often continued longer than I had planned because I wanted to know what would happen next. I felt relieved whenever one of his ideas worked.","The story also gave me a useful reminder: a big problem becomes less frightening when you focus on the next small action. I think that's why it stayed with me. I'd recommend it to someone who enjoys a hopeful story with a clever main character."],"variants":[{"name":"失望电影","answer_script":["The film I'd choose is The Martian. I watched it at home a few months ago after reading the novel by Andy Weir. Because I had enjoyed the book, I expected the film to give me the same sense of involvement, but some parts disappointed me.","The story follows an astronaut called Mark Watney who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to work out how to survive and contact Earth. The main idea is interesting, and I liked the fact that science and practical thinking were important to the story.","My disappointment was mainly about the pace of the problem-solving. In the book, I could spend time following his thoughts and understanding why a particular solution might work. In the film, some of those steps felt rushed, so I was less involved in the decisions.","The visuals were impressive, and the acting was enjoyable, but I sometimes felt that a difficult problem had been solved before I fully understood it. I watched it with a friend, and we discussed that difference afterwards.","I wouldn't describe it as a terrible film. My expectations were simply too closely connected to the book. I learned that an adaptation can tell the same story while creating a different experience. If I watched it again, I'd probably judge it more on its own terms."],"module":"The film I'd choose is The Martian. I watched it at home a few months ago after reading the novel by Andy Weir. Because I had enjoyed the book, I expected the film to give me the same sense of involvement, but some parts disappointed me. The story follows an astronaut called Mark Watney who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to work out how to survive and contact Earth. The main idea is interesting, and I liked the fact that science and practical thinking were important to the story. My disappointment was mainly about the pace of the problem-solving. In the book, I could spend time following his thoughts and understanding why a particular solution might work. In the film, some of those steps felt rushed, so I was less involved in the decisions. The visuals were impressive, and the acting was enjoyable, but I sometimes felt that a difficult problem had been solved before I fully understood it. I watched it with a friend, and we discussed that difference afterwards. I wouldn't describe it as a terrible film. My expectations were simply too closely connected to the book. I learned that an adaptation can tell the same story while creating a different experience. If I watched it again, I'd probably judge it more on its own terms.","omit":""},{"name":"喜欢的电影","answer_script":["I'd like to talk about a film called The Martian. I watched it at home with a friend a few months ago. Matt Damon plays an astronaut who is accidentally left behind on Mars. The mixture of an unusual setting and practical problem-solving appealed to me.","The main character is an astronaut called Mark Watney, who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to find ways to stay alive and contact people on Earth. The situation sounds hopeless, but he doesn't give up. He deals with one problem at a time, using whatever resources he has.","What I enjoyed most was seeing how the character responded to each new difficulty. The film made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the experience enjoyable as well.","I particularly liked the landscape and the way the acting conveyed his loneliness. My friend and I kept wondering how we would behave in that situation. Afterwards, we talked about which part of the story had made us feel most nervous.","The story also gave me a useful reminder: a big problem becomes less frightening when you focus on the next small action. I think that's why it stayed with me. I'd recommend it to someone who enjoys a hopeful story with a clever main character."],"module":"I'd like to talk about a film called The Martian. I watched it at home with a friend a few months ago. Matt Damon plays an astronaut who is accidentally left behind on Mars. The mixture of an unusual setting and practical problem-solving appealed to me. What I enjoyed most was seeing how the character responded to each new difficulty. The film made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the experience enjoyable as well. I particularly liked the landscape and the way the acting conveyed his loneliness. My friend and I kept wondering how we would behave in that situation. Afterwards, we talked about which part of the story had made us feel most nervous.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M02","name":"influential_book","answer_script":["A book that influenced the way I think is The Martian by Andy Weir. It is a science-fiction novel about an astronaut called Mark Watney who is left on Mars and has to find a way to survive. I read it when I wanted something entertaining after work.","The main character is an astronaut called Mark Watney, who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to find ways to stay alive and contact people on Earth. The situation sounds hopeless, but he doesn't give up. He deals with one problem at a time, using whatever resources he has.","What I enjoyed most was the way he thought through his difficulties. The book made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the story enjoyable as well.","I read a little in the evening, and I often continued longer than I had planned because I wanted to know what would happen next. I felt relieved whenever one of his ideas worked.","What influenced me most was his habit of breaking a huge problem into smaller tasks. I sometimes feel overwhelmed by a difficult project, and the story reminds me to work out what I can do next. I don't pretend my problems are as serious as his, but that practical way of thinking has stayed with me."],"keywords":"The Martian → Mark Watney → 生存困境 → 拆小任务 → 工作启发","note":"影响你的书需要讲清个人影响，而不是只复述剧情。","omit":"影响你的书需要讲清个人影响，而不是只复述剧情。"}],"followups":[{"q":"Would you recommend the book?","a":"Yes, particularly to someone who enjoys a practical character solving problems. It has tense moments and humour, so it doesn't feel serious all the time. However, someone who dislikes technical details might prefer the film.","q_zh":"你会推荐这本书吗？"},{"q":"Would you watch the film again?","a":"I might. The first time, I compared it too closely with the novel. Watching it again would let me pay more attention to the acting and visuals instead of expecting every detail from the book.","q_zh":"你会再看一遍这部电影吗？"},{"q":"What did you learn from it?","a":"The main idea I took away was to focus on the next manageable action. When a problem feels too large, listing a few smaller steps helps me begin rather than wait for a perfect solution.","q_zh":"你从中学到了什么？"}],"category":"事物","title_en":"The Martian: the novel and the film","audio":"audio/429b3f4b9218f598.m4a"},{"id":"M03","title":"老迪拜半日游","keywords":"周末朋友 → 老街和市场 → 水边 → 照片与聊天 → 和日常不同。","script":["I'd like to describe an afternoon I spent exploring an older part of Dubai with a friend. We went there on a weekend because we wanted a break from our usual routine. We weren't trying to visit every attraction. We just wanted to walk around and see something different.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","At one point, we walked through a busy market. It was quite crowded, and I could hear people talking and calling out to customers. Later, we moved to a quieter spot by the water and took a few photos. The light was softer by then, which made the area look especially nice.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"variants":[{"name":"市场噪音","answer_script":["A noisy place I remember visiting is a busy market near Dubai Creek. I went there with a friend on a weekend afternoon. We wanted to explore the area, look at the small shops and see something different from our usual surroundings.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","The narrow paths were full of shoppers. I could hear sellers calling to customers, groups talking loudly and carts moving between the shops. The sounds overlapped, so my friend and I sometimes had to repeat ourselves. I found it lively at first, but after a while I wanted a break.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I enjoyed looking around, but I wouldn't want to spend the whole day there. The noise made it difficult to concentrate on a conversation. Moving to the quieter waterfront afterwards helped me appreciate the difference. So it was interesting to visit, even though it wasn't somewhere I could fully relax."],"module":"A noisy place I remember visiting is a busy market near Dubai Creek. I went there with a friend on a weekend afternoon. We wanted to explore the area, look at the small shops and see something different from our usual surroundings. The narrow paths were full of shoppers. I could hear sellers calling to customers, groups talking loudly and carts moving between the shops. The sounds overlapped, so my friend and I sometimes had to repeat ourselves. I found it lively at first, but after a while I wanted a break. I enjoyed looking around, but I wouldn't want to spend the whole day there. The noise made it difficult to concentrate on a conversation. Moving to the quieter waterfront afterwards helped me appreciate the difference. So it was interesting to visit, even though it wasn't somewhere I could fully relax.","omit":""},{"name":"拥挤市场","answer_script":["A crowded place I've visited is a market near Dubai Creek. I went there with a friend on a weekend afternoon. We wanted to explore the small shops and take a few photos, but there were more people than we had expected.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","At some points, the path was so busy that we had to wait before moving forward. People stopped to look at products while others tried to pass them. I kept my bag close and paid attention to where my friend was, because it would have been easy to lose each other.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","The crowd gave the market an energetic atmosphere, but it also made simple things take longer. I was glad we eventually found a quiet place to sit. If I go again, I'll choose a less busy time so that I can enjoy the shops without constantly moving around other people."],"module":"A crowded place I've visited is a market near Dubai Creek. I went there with a friend on a weekend afternoon. We wanted to explore the small shops and take a few photos, but there were more people than we had expected. At some points, the path was so busy that we had to wait before moving forward. People stopped to look at products while others tried to pass them. I kept my bag close and paid attention to where my friend was, because it would have been easy to lose each other. The crowd gave the market an energetic atmosphere, but it also made simple things take longer. I was glad we eventually found a quiet place to sit. If I go again, I'll choose a less busy time so that I can enjoy the shops without constantly moving around other people.","omit":""},{"name":"朋友愉快夜晚","answer_script":["One enjoyable evening was when a friend and I explored an older part of Dubai and then sat down for a drink near the creek. It happened on a weekend a few months ago. Neither of us wanted a big event; we just wanted time to talk.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","As it became darker, the area felt calmer. We walked past the shops, took a few photos and then chose somewhere comfortable to sit. We talked about things that had happened that week, shared a few funny stories and stopped checking our phones for a while.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"module":"One enjoyable evening was when a friend and I explored an older part of Dubai and then sat down for a drink near the creek. It happened on a weekend a few months ago. Neither of us wanted a big event; we just wanted time to talk. As it became darker, the area felt calmer. We walked past the shops, took a few photos and then chose somewhere comfortable to sit. We talked about things that had happened that week, shared a few funny stories and stopped checking our phones for a while.","omit":""},{"name":"省钱外出","answer_script":["A day out that cost me very little was an afternoon exploring an older part of Dubai with a friend. We chose it because we wanted to do something enjoyable without spending much. Most of the plan involved walking around, looking at the shops and taking photos.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","At one point, we walked through a busy market. It was quite crowded, and I could hear people talking and calling out to customers. Later, we moved to a quieter spot by the water and took a few photos. The light was softer by then, which made the area look especially nice.","We only spent money on transport and a simple drink. We didn't book an expensive activity or buy things just because they were available. Sitting by the water and talking was one of the best parts, and that didn't require a large budget.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"module":"A day out that cost me very little was an afternoon exploring an older part of Dubai with a friend. We chose it because we wanted to do something enjoyable without spending much. Most of the plan involved walking around, looking at the shops and taking photos. We only spent money on transport and a simple drink. We didn't book an expensive activity or buy things just because they were available. Sitting by the water and talking was one of the best parts, and that didn't require a large budget.","omit":""},{"name":"公共交通","answer_script":["A journey I made by public transport was a trip to the area around Dubai Creek with a friend. We used a train for part of the journey and walked the final section. During the outing, we also crossed the creek in a small boat.","I enjoyed being a passenger because I could look around rather than concentrate on driving. We checked the direction before getting on and kept the plan fairly simple. Travelling together made the journey feel like part of the outing, instead of just a way to reach the destination.","The boat crossing was the most memorable part. It was a short journey, but being close to the water gave me a different view of the buildings and the people on the shore. I took a few pictures while my friend pointed out places we could explore next.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"module":"A journey I made by public transport was a trip to the area around Dubai Creek with a friend. We used a train for part of the journey and walked the final section. During the outing, we also crossed the creek in a small boat. I enjoyed being a passenger because I could look around rather than concentrate on driving. We checked the direction before getting on and kept the plan fairly simple. Travelling together made the journey feel like part of the outing, instead of just a way to reach the destination. The boat crossing was the most memorable part. It was a short journey, but being close to the water gave me a different view of the buildings and the people on the shore. I took a few pictures while my friend pointed out places we could explore next.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M03","name":"historic_place","answer_script":["A place with a sense of history that I'd like to describe is Al Fahidi Historical Neighbourhood in old Dubai. I visited it with my friend Adam a few months ago. We wanted a quiet walk somewhere that felt different from the city's newer areas.","The narrow lanes and traditional buildings immediately caught my attention. Instead of rushing between large modern buildings, we could walk slowly and look at small courtyards and the details around us. I liked the feeling of discovering a place one corner at a time.","We spent some time looking around and stopped for a drink at a small cafe. Adam took a few photographs, while I was more interested in how the streets connected. Afterwards, we continued towards the creek and watched the boats crossing the water.","What made the visit enjoyable was the contrast within the same city. I usually associate Dubai with busy roads and tall buildings, but that afternoon gave me a different impression. We didn't need a strict schedule, so there was time to notice things we would normally walk past.","I would like to go back and learn more about the area's history before visiting. I don't know every detail about the buildings, but the neighbourhood made me curious. For me, a historical place is interesting when it helps me imagine how everyday life used to be, rather than simply looking old."],"keywords":"Al Fahidi → 窄巷与庭院 → 慢慢散步 → 迪拜另一面 → 想再了解历史","note":"只使用已核实的历史街区身份；个人参观细节为样例。","omit":"只使用已核实的历史街区身份；个人参观细节为样例。"}],"followups":[{"q":"Would you go there again?","a":"Yes, but I would choose a quieter time. I enjoyed the atmosphere and the waterfront, while the crowded market was tiring. A less busy visit would give me more time to notice the small details.","q_zh":"你会再去那里吗？"},{"q":"Who would you take?","a":"I'd take a friend who enjoys walking and looking at everyday places. We wouldn't need to follow a strict schedule. Having someone to share observations with would make the outing more enjoyable.","q_zh":"你会带谁一起去？"},{"q":"What was your favourite part?","a":"The quiet moment by the water was my favourite. After the busy market, it was pleasant to sit down and talk. It made a fairly ordinary afternoon feel like a proper break from work.","q_zh":"你当时最喜欢的是哪个部分？"}],"category":"地点","title_en":"An outing in old Dubai","audio":"audio/5a02bf1371eb47f4.m4a"},{"id":"M04","title":"团队做小原型","keywords":"重复工作 → 大方案 → 同事提议 → 小原型 → 测试成功 → 改变看法。","script":["I'd like to describe a decision I made while working on a small project with my team. We had a repetitive task that involved checking information manually, and I wanted to build a tool to make it easier.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"variants":[{"name":"改变决定","answer_script":["I'd like to describe a time I changed an important decision during a team project. We wanted to make a repeated manual task easier. My original decision was to build a complete system, but I later chose to start with a small version instead.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"module":"I'd like to describe a time I changed an important decision during a team project. We wanted to make a repeated manual task easier. My original decision was to build a complete system, but I later chose to start with a small version instead.","omit":""},{"name":"改变想法","answer_script":["An opinion I changed was my belief that a new idea should be fully developed before anyone tried it. I changed my mind during a small project at work. We wanted to build a tool that would make a repeated manual task easier.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"module":"An opinion I changed was my belief that a new idea should be fully developed before anyone tried it. I changed my mind during a small project at work. We wanted to build a tool that would make a repeated manual task easier.","omit":""},{"name":"团队合作","answer_script":["A time I worked in a group was when a few colleagues and I built a small tool for a repeated task at work. We wanted to reduce the amount of manual checking. Each person understood a different part of the problem, so working together was important.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"module":"A time I worked in a group was when a few colleagues and I built a small tool for a repeated task at work. We wanted to reduce the amount of manual checking. Each person understood a different part of the problem, so working together was important.","omit":""},{"name":"科技困难","answer_script":["A challenging technical problem I faced was getting a small tool to read information correctly. I was working on it with a team at work. The aim was to reduce manual checking, but our first attempt produced results we couldn't rely on.","At first, I thought the main function was wrong. However, after comparing a few examples, we realised that some of the information was written in a different format. The tool was treating those examples as if they followed the same pattern as the others.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"module":"A challenging technical problem I faced was getting a small tool to read information correctly. I was working on it with a team at work. The aim was to reduce manual checking, but our first attempt produced results we couldn't rely on. At first, I thought the main function was wrong. However, after comparing a few examples, we realised that some of the information was written in a different format. The tool was treating those examples as if they followed the same pattern as the others.","omit":""},{"name":"帮助别人","answer_script":["A time I helped someone solve a problem was when a colleague had to check the same information repeatedly. It was taking up too much of his day. I asked which part was most difficult and suggested building a simple tool to handle the repeated steps.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was pleased that I could help with a problem that affected his everyday work. The tool didn't remove the need for all checks, but it made the process easier. I also learned that asking careful questions is useful before deciding what kind of help someone needs."],"module":"A time I helped someone solve a problem was when a colleague had to check the same information repeatedly. It was taking up too much of his day. I asked which part was most difficult and suggested building a simple tool to handle the repeated steps. I was pleased that I could help with a problem that affected his everyday work. The tool didn't remove the need for all checks, but it made the process easier. I also learned that asking careful questions is useful before deciding what kind of help someone needs.","omit":""},{"name":"节约时间","answer_script":["A change that helped save time was using a simple tool for a repeated task at work. Before that, my team checked the information manually each time. We still needed to look at the results, but we wanted to avoid repeating every basic step ourselves.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"module":"A change that helped save time was using a simple tool for a repeated task at work. Before that, my team checked the information manually each time. We still needed to look at the results, but we wanted to avoid repeating every basic step ourselves.","omit":""},{"name":"增加信心","answer_script":["A time I became more confident was when a small tool I helped build finally worked. It happened during a project with a few colleagues. At the beginning, I wasn't sure I could contribute enough because the problem was less straightforward than I had expected.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","Seeing a practical result made me feel more confident about handling unfamiliar problems. I didn't suddenly know everything, but I had evidence that I could learn, ask questions and improve a first attempt. Since then, I've been more willing to take part when a task initially looks difficult."],"module":"A time I became more confident was when a small tool I helped build finally worked. It happened during a project with a few colleagues. At the beginning, I wasn't sure I could contribute enough because the problem was less straightforward than I had expected. Seeing a practical result made me feel more confident about handling unfamiliar problems. I didn't suddenly know everything, but I had evidence that I could learn, ask questions and improve a first attempt. Since then, I've been more willing to take part when a task initially looks difficult.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M04","name":"useful_app","keywords":"内部程序 → 请求列表 → 负责人 → 状态 → 每天使用","note":"团队开发、程序功能和使用效果均为样例。它是目前已在使用的内部程序，不能同时讲成尚未开发或将来想买的App；具体业务功能需与M04实际个人化版本一致。","answer_script":["A useful app I use at work is a small internal program that our team developed. It brings requests into one shared list, so we can see what needs attention without searching through several different conversations. I helped work on an early version of it.","Before we had the program, requests were spread across messages and emails. It was easy to miss an update or forget who was handling something. Even a simple question could involve looking through old conversations before finding the information we needed.","We started with a basic version instead of trying to build a complete system. The main features were a list of requests, the person responsible for each one and its current status. We tested it with a few examples and corrected the parts that were unclear.","I now use it to check my tasks and update their progress. During team discussions, we can look at the same information rather than explain everything again from memory. It doesn't do the work for us, but it helps us keep track of it.","What I like most is that it solves a problem I actually have. The interface is simple, and I don't need a long explanation each time I open it. For me, useful software makes an ordinary task easier to manage, rather than adding features I rarely need."]}],"followups":[{"q":"What was the hardest part?","a":"The hardest part was understanding why the first results were wrong. We had to compare examples carefully instead of change things at random. Once we understood the difference, the solution became much clearer.","q_zh":"当时最困难的是哪个部分？"},{"q":"Did the project work perfectly?","a":"No. It handled the basic task, but we still checked the results and kept a list of improvements. I think that was acceptable for a first version because the main goal was to test whether the idea was useful.","q_zh":"这个项目当时运行得很完美吗？"},{"q":"Would you make the same decision again?","a":"Yes, if the situation were similar. Starting small allowed us to learn without making a large commitment. For a more serious or complex problem, I would spend more time understanding the requirements before testing anything.","q_zh":"如果再来一次，你还会做同样的决定吗？"}],"category":"经历","title_en":"Building a small tool with a team","audio":"audio/23b21937cd25ee34.m4a"},{"id":"M05","title":"散步与减少刷手机","keywords":"下班累 → 刷手机更久 → 十分钟散步 → 和朋友坚持 → 状态变好。","script":["I'd like to talk about a small change I made to my evening routine. I used to come home from work and immediately start looking at my phone. I told myself I was taking a short break, but quite often I ended up scrolling for nearly an hour.","The problem was that I didn't feel rested afterwards. I was still tired, and sometimes I went to bed later than I had planned. So I decided to replace part of that screen time with a short walk.","I started with just ten minutes because I knew I wouldn't stick to an ambitious exercise plan. When the weather was comfortable, I walked outside. On other days, I found somewhere indoors where I could move around. I usually left my phone in my pocket and paid attention to my surroundings.","After a while, a friend began joining me. That made the habit easier to maintain because we could chat and remind each other to go. We weren't trying to become athletes. We just wanted to do something more active after sitting for most of the day.","The walk gives me a clear break between work and the rest of my evening. The change is simple, but it helps me relax and makes me feel more in control of my time."],"variants":[{"name":"浪费时间","answer_script":["An activity I regularly do that I consider a waste of time is scrolling through short posts on my phone. It often happens after work. I tell myself that I'll look for a few minutes, but the activity can take up much more of the evening than I intended.","The problem was that I didn't feel rested afterwards. I was still tired, and sometimes I went to bed later than I had planned. So I decided to replace part of that screen time with a short walk.","I started with just ten minutes because I knew I wouldn't stick to an ambitious exercise plan. When the weather was comfortable, I walked outside. On other days, I found somewhere indoors where I could move around. I usually left my phone in my pocket and paid attention to my surroundings.","After a while, a friend began joining me. That made the habit easier to maintain because we could chat and remind each other to go. We weren't trying to become athletes. We just wanted to do something more active after sitting for most of the day.","I consider it a waste of time because I usually haven't chosen a clear purpose and I remember very little afterwards. A few useful posts do appear, but they don't justify all the time I spend. I'm trying to keep a limit and choose a more deliberate way to relax."],"module":"An activity I regularly do that I consider a waste of time is scrolling through short posts on my phone. It often happens after work. I tell myself that I'll look for a few minutes, but the activity can take up much more of the evening than I intended. I consider it a waste of time because I usually haven't chosen a clear purpose and I remember very little afterwards. A few useful posts do appear, but they don't justify all the time I spend. I'm trying to keep a limit and choose a more deliberate way to relax.","omit":""},{"name":"帮助朋友健康","answer_script":["A person whose fitness I helped improve is a friend called Sam. Like me, he spent most of his working day sitting down. He wanted to be more active, but he found it difficult to start an exercise routine that he could continue.","A few months ago, I suggested that we begin with a short walk after work. I didn't give him complicated fitness advice. I simply thought doing something together would make the first step easier. We agreed to try ten minutes rather than set an ambitious target.","When the weather was comfortable, we walked outside. Otherwise, we found somewhere suitable indoors. I checked in with him before the walk and tried to make the plan convenient. On days when one of us felt tired, we still did a shorter version instead of cancelling everything.","After a few weeks, he said the routine had become easier to maintain. He also enjoyed having a break between work and the rest of the evening. I can't claim that it transformed his health, but it did help him spend more time moving regularly.","The hardest part was getting started and keeping the plan simple. I'm pleased that I could support him without putting pressure on him. Helping with a small habit was more practical than telling him to make a huge change overnight."],"module":"A person whose fitness I helped improve is a friend called Sam. Like me, he spent most of his working day sitting down. He wanted to be more active, but he found it difficult to start an exercise routine that he could continue. A few months ago, I suggested that we begin with a short walk after work. I didn't give him complicated fitness advice. I simply thought doing something together would make the first step easier. We agreed to try ten minutes rather than set an ambitious target. When the weather was comfortable, we walked outside. Otherwise, we found somewhere suitable indoors. I checked in with him before the walk and tried to make the plan convenient. On days when one of us felt tired, we still did a shorter version instead of cancelling everything. After a few weeks, he said the routine had become easier to maintain. He also enjoyed having a break between work and the rest of the evening. I can't claim that it transformed his health, but it did help him spend more time moving regularly. The hardest part was getting started and keeping the plan simple. I'm pleased that I could support him without putting pressure on him. Helping with a small habit was more practical than telling him to make a huge change overnight.","omit":""},{"name":"早起事件","answer_script":["A time I got up earlier than usual was one Saturday when I arranged to meet a friend for a morning walk. We wanted to go out before the day became too hot, so we agreed to meet shortly after sunrise.","I'm not normally someone who wakes up very early on a day off. To make it easier, I prepared my clothes and set an alarm the night before. I also went to bed a little earlier instead of staying on my phone.","When the alarm rang, I wanted to go back to sleep. However, I knew my friend was expecting me, so I got ready and left. Once I was outside, I began to feel more awake. The streets were quieter than usual, and the air felt more comfortable.","We walked for a while and then had breakfast together. I enjoyed having time to talk without feeling rushed. By the time I got home, I had already done something pleasant, and there was still most of the day left.","I was glad I had made the effort. I wouldn't want to wake up at that time every weekend, but it showed me why some people enjoy an early start. Planning one enjoyable activity made getting out of bed much easier."],"module":"A time I got up earlier than usual was one Saturday when I arranged to meet a friend for a morning walk. We wanted to go out before the day became too hot, so we agreed to meet shortly after sunrise. I'm not normally someone who wakes up very early on a day off. To make it easier, I prepared my clothes and set an alarm the night before. I also went to bed a little earlier instead of staying on my phone. When the alarm rang, I wanted to go back to sleep. However, I knew my friend was expecting me, so I got ready and left. Once I was outside, I began to feel more awake. The streets were quieter than usual, and the air felt more comfortable. We walked for a while and then had breakfast together. I enjoyed having time to talk without feeling rushed. By the time I got home, I had already done something pleasant, and there was still most of the day left. I was glad I had made the effort. I wouldn't want to wake up at that time every weekend, but it showed me why some people enjoy an early start. Planning one enjoyable activity made getting out of bed much easier.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M05","name":"sleep_routine","keywords":"刷手机 → 时间过晚 → 提前停 → 早点睡 → 更精神","note":"作息、屏幕时间与第二天状态均为个人感受样例，没有减重、治疗或其他医学断言。它是夜间作息变化，不是把傍晚散步简单改成早起。","answer_script":["A change I made to my evening routine was spending less time on my phone before bed. I used to tell myself I was having a short break, but I often kept scrolling until late. The next morning, I sometimes felt rushed and tired.","I decided to make the change small enough to maintain. I chose a time to stop looking at messages and social media, usually about half an hour before I wanted to sleep. I put my phone away from the bed so that it was less tempting to pick it up again.","During that time, I did a few things, such as preparing my clothes for the next day or reading a few pages of a book. I wasn't trying to follow a complicated routine. I mainly wanted the evening to feel as though it was coming to an end.","After a while, I noticed that I was getting into bed earlier more often. On some mornings, I felt more awake and had enough time for breakfast. Those mornings felt less hurried, which made the change feel worthwhile.","I don't manage it perfectly every night, especially when I have something urgent to finish. Still, having a simple stopping point helps me control my time. I like the routine because it gives me a calmer end to the day and a less hurried start the next morning."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Was the habit difficult to maintain?","a":"At first, yes. After work, doing nothing often felt easier. Keeping the walk short and arranging it with a friend helped. I was more likely to continue when the plan felt convenient rather than demanding.","q_zh":"当时坚持这个习惯困难吗？"},{"q":"Do you still use your phone?","a":"Yes, because it is useful for communication and finding information. I'm trying to reduce the time I spend scrolling without a purpose. The aim is to make a choice, rather than automatically open the same apps.","q_zh":"你现在还使用手机吗？"},{"q":"Would you recommend your routine?","a":"I'd recommend trying a small, manageable activity. The exact routine should suit the person and the weather. Someone doesn't need to copy my walk if another simple habit fits their life better.","q_zh":"你会推荐自己的日常安排吗？"}],"category":"经历","title_en":"Walking more and spending less time on my phone","audio":"audio/31bf46c69725e72d.m4a"},{"id":"M06","title":"耳机与购买服务","keywords":"需要专注 → 攒钱和比较 → 购买 → 出问题 → 店员换货 → 实际价值。","script":["I'd like to talk about a pair of headphones that I saved up to buy. I wanted them because I often needed to concentrate in places where there was background noise. I also thought they would be useful for listening to English recordings.","They were more expensive than the basic headphones I had used before, so I didn't buy them immediately. I compared a few options and put aside a little money each month. I also cut back on a few small purchases that I didn't really need.","When I finally bought them, I was pleased because I had made a deliberate choice rather than buying something on impulse. I started using them regularly for work and language practice.","A few weeks later, one side stopped working properly. I took them back to the shop, expecting a long argument. Instead, the assistant listened carefully, checked the problem and explained the next steps. After confirming the fault, the shop arranged a replacement.","That experience made the purchase more memorable. I appreciated both the product and the way the problem was handled. For me, the value wasn't just the price or the brand. It was having something useful and knowing that I could get help when it didn't work as expected."],"variants":[{"name":"好服务","answer_script":["The good service I'd like to describe was the help I received in a shop when my headphones stopped working. I had bought them a few weeks earlier after saving up. Because I used them often, I was disappointed when one side began to fail.","I brought the headphones and the proof of purchase back to the shop. The assistant asked me to explain what had happened and listened without interrupting. He then checked the problem instead of immediately suggesting that I had caused it.","He explained the next steps in language I could understand and told me what information the shop needed. After confirming the fault, the staff arranged a replacement. I appreciated knowing what was happening, rather than being passed from one person to another.","The assistant also gave me time to ask questions and check the replacement. I had expected the visit to be stressful, but it was straightforward. The most helpful part was his calm attitude, which made me feel that the problem was being taken seriously.","That experience made the purchase more memorable. I appreciated both the product and the way the problem was handled. For me, the value wasn't just the price or the brand. It was having something useful and knowing that I could get help when it didn't work as expected."],"module":"The good service I'd like to describe was the help I received in a shop when my headphones stopped working. I had bought them a few weeks earlier after saving up. Because I used them often, I was disappointed when one side began to fail. I brought the headphones and the proof of purchase back to the shop. The assistant asked me to explain what had happened and listened without interrupting. He then checked the problem instead of immediately suggesting that I had caused it. He explained the next steps in language I could understand and told me what information the shop needed. After confirming the fault, the staff arranged a replacement. I appreciated knowing what was happening, rather than being passed from one person to another. The assistant also gave me time to ask questions and check the replacement. I had expected the visit to be stressful, but it was straightforward. The most helpful part was his calm attitude, which made me feel that the problem was being taken seriously.","omit":""},{"name":"电子故障","answer_script":["A problem I had with an electronic device was when one side of my headphones stopped working. I had bought them a few weeks earlier and was using them regularly for work and English recordings. At first, I thought the recording or connection might be the problem.","I tried a different recording and connected the headphones again. The same side still wasn't working, so I decided to stop guessing and contact the shop. I found the proof of purchase and explained when the fault had started.","The shop assistant checked the headphones and confirmed that they weren't working properly. He explained the replacement process clearly. I was relieved that I didn't have to understand the internal parts of the device in order to get help.","A few weeks later, one side stopped working properly. I took them back to the shop, expecting a long argument. Instead, the assistant listened carefully, checked the problem and explained the next steps. After confirming the fault, the shop arranged a replacement.","That experience made the purchase more memorable. I appreciated both the product and the way the problem was handled. For me, the value wasn't just the price or the brand. It was having something useful and knowing that I could get help when it didn't work as expected."],"module":"A problem I had with an electronic device was when one side of my headphones stopped working. I had bought them a few weeks earlier and was using them regularly for work and English recordings. At first, I thought the recording or connection might be the problem. I tried a different recording and connected the headphones again. The same side still wasn't working, so I decided to stop guessing and contact the shop. I found the proof of purchase and explained when the fault had started. The shop assistant checked the headphones and confirmed that they weren't working properly. He explained the replacement process clearly. I was relieved that I didn't have to understand the internal parts of the device in order to get help.","omit":""},{"name":"必需物品","answer_script":["Something I find difficult to do without is my pair of headphones. They aren't a phone or a computer, but I use them almost every day. They help me concentrate in places with background noise and listen to English recordings without disturbing other people.","I chose a comfortable pair because I knew I would wear them for a while. Before buying them, I compared a few options and saved a little money each month. I wanted something useful, rather than simply buying the most fashionable brand.","When I finally bought them, I was pleased because I had made a deliberate choice rather than buying something on impulse. I started using them regularly for work and language practice.","A few weeks later, one side stopped working properly. I took them back to the shop, expecting a long argument. Instead, the assistant listened carefully, checked the problem and explained the next steps. After confirming the fault, the shop arranged a replacement.","When I couldn't use them, I realised how much they were part of my routine. I could still work and study, but I found it harder to focus and practise listening in a shared space. That's why I think of them as a small but important everyday item."],"module":"Something I find difficult to do without is my pair of headphones. They aren't a phone or a computer, but I use them almost every day. They help me concentrate in places with background noise and listen to English recordings without disturbing other people. I chose a comfortable pair because I knew I would wear them for a while. Before buying them, I compared a few options and saved a little money each month. I wanted something useful, rather than simply buying the most fashionable brand. When I couldn't use them, I realised how much they were part of my routine. I could still work and study, but I found it harder to focus and practise listening in a shared space. That's why I think of them as a small but important everyday item.","omit":""},{"name":"未来礼物","answer_script":["A gift I'd like to buy for a friend is a pair of comfortable headphones. My friend Sam enjoys listening to music and is also trying to improve his English. We've known each other for a few years, so I have a fairly good idea of what he would use.","He sometimes listens through his phone's speaker, which isn't very convenient when other people are nearby. I think headphones would let him enjoy recordings and practise listening without disturbing anyone. They could also be useful when he wants to concentrate.","I wouldn't choose the most expensive pair automatically. I'd compare comfort, sound quality and how easy they are to use. If possible, I'd ask him about his preferences without immediately revealing that I was thinking about a gift.","I'd probably give them to him on his birthday. I would include a short note explaining why I chose them, because I think that personal detail matters. I might also suggest an English podcast we could both listen to and discuss afterwards.","I'd choose this gift because it connects with his actual interests. A useful present can show that someone has paid attention to you. I hope he would enjoy it regularly, rather than put it away after the first day."],"module":"A gift I'd like to buy for a friend is a pair of comfortable headphones. My friend Sam enjoys listening to music and is also trying to improve his English. We've known each other for a few years, so I have a fairly good idea of what he would use. He sometimes listens through his phone's speaker, which isn't very convenient when other people are nearby. I think headphones would let him enjoy recordings and practise listening without disturbing anyone. They could also be useful when he wants to concentrate. I wouldn't choose the most expensive pair automatically. I'd compare comfort, sound quality and how easy they are to use. If possible, I'd ask him about his preferences without immediately revealing that I was thinking about a gift. I'd probably give them to him on his birthday. I would include a short note explaining why I chose them, because I think that personal detail matters. I might also suggest an English podcast we could both listen to and discuss afterwards. I'd choose this gift because it connects with his actual interests. A useful present can show that someone has paid attention to you. I hope he would enjoy it regularly, rather than put it away after the first day.","omit":""},{"name":"想买科技产品","answer_script":["A piece of technology I'd like to buy is a better pair of headphones. I already use a basic pair, but I would like something more comfortable that could reduce distracting background noise. It isn't a phone, and it would serve a clear purpose in my routine.","I often need to concentrate on work or listen to English recordings. When the surroundings are noisy, I find myself repeating the same section because I've missed something. A better pair could make those activities easier, especially in a shared space.","Before buying anything, I would compare a few models and read about their comfort and everyday use. I'd prefer to try them in a shop if possible. The most expensive option wouldn't necessarily be the best one for me.","I plan to save a little money each month instead of buying them immediately. I would also check what help is available if they stop working. My experience with electronic products has taught me that service matters as well as the product itself.","I want them because I expect to use them often, not just because they are new. If they help me work and study with fewer interruptions, I would consider the purchase worthwhile. Until then, I can continue using what I already have."],"module":"A piece of technology I'd like to buy is a better pair of headphones. I already use a basic pair, but I would like something more comfortable that could reduce distracting background noise. It isn't a phone, and it would serve a clear purpose in my routine. I often need to concentrate on work or listen to English recordings. When the surroundings are noisy, I find myself repeating the same section because I've missed something. A better pair could make those activities easier, especially in a shared space. Before buying anything, I would compare a few models and read about their comfort and everyday use. I'd prefer to try them in a shop if possible. The most expensive option wouldn't necessarily be the best one for me. I plan to save a little money each month instead of buying them immediately. I would also check what help is available if they stop working. My experience with electronic products has taught me that service matters as well as the product itself. I want them because I expect to use them often, not just because they are new. If they help me work and study with fewer interruptions, I would consider the purchase worthwhile. Until then, I can continue using what I already have.","omit":""},{"name":"久等回复","answer_script":["A time I waited a long time for a reply was when I contacted a shop about a problem with my headphones. One side had stopped working, and I wanted to know what I needed to bring in for a replacement.","I sent a short message with the purchase details and a description of the fault. I thought I would hear back fairly quickly, but after several days there was still no reply. I checked that I had used the correct contact information before sending a polite follow-up.","The wait was frustrating mainly because I didn't know what to do next. I was unsure whether the message had been received, whether the shop needed more information or whether I should visit in person. I didn't want to make an unnecessary trip.","In the end, I went to the shop with the headphones and the proof of purchase. An assistant checked the problem and explained the process. Once I had that information, I felt much more relaxed.","The experience reminded me that even a brief response can be helpful. It doesn't have to solve a problem immediately, but it should let the customer know what is happening. Since then, I've tried to acknowledge messages when I can't give a complete answer straight away."],"module":"A time I waited a long time for a reply was when I contacted a shop about a problem with my headphones. One side had stopped working, and I wanted to know what I needed to bring in for a replacement. I sent a short message with the purchase details and a description of the fault. I thought I would hear back fairly quickly, but after several days there was still no reply. I checked that I had used the correct contact information before sending a polite follow-up. The wait was frustrating mainly because I didn't know what to do next. I was unsure whether the message had been received, whether the shop needed more information or whether I should visit in person. I didn't want to make an unnecessary trip. In the end, I went to the shop with the headphones and the proof of purchase. An assistant checked the problem and explained the process. Once I had that information, I felt much more relaxed. The experience reminded me that even a brief response can be helpful. It doesn't have to solve a problem immediately, but it should let the customer know what is happening. Since then, I've tried to acknowledge messages when I can't give a complete answer straight away.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M06","name":"lost_item","keywords":"老迪拜市场 → 钥匙不见 → 原路返回 → 店员 → 找回","note":"市场到访、丢钥匙、店员帮忙及找回全部为样例；丢的是钥匙，不是手机。未冒称任何真实商铺的失物流程。","answer_script":["One time I lost something was during a visit to a market in the older part of Dubai. I was there with a friend, looking around the small shops and taking a few photographs. The item I lost was my set of keys.","I noticed they were missing when we were about to leave. At first, I thought they must be in another pocket, so I checked my clothes and bag carefully. When I still couldn't find them, I began feeling worried because I needed them to get into my home.","My friend helped me think through where we had been. I remembered taking the keys out while looking for my wallet in one shop. We walked back along the same route and asked a member of staff whether anyone had found them.","Fortunately, someone had noticed the keys on the counter and kept them safely. I described the key ring before the staff member returned them to me. I felt relieved and thanked him, because a small mistake could have caused a much more inconvenient evening.","Afterwards, I put the keys in one specific pocket instead of moving them between my bag and clothes. I also tried to check them before leaving a place. The experience was stressful at the time, but it reminded me that a simple habit can help me avoid the same problem again."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Was it worth the money?","a":"For me, yes, because I used the headphones regularly. I wouldn't judge the value only by the brand or price. Comfort, usefulness and the help available when something goes wrong all mattered to my decision.","q_zh":"这笔钱花得值吗？"},{"q":"How did the service affect your opinion?","a":"It made me trust the shop more. A fault is disappointing, but a clear explanation and a fair solution can improve the experience. I appreciated being treated as someone with a problem worth understanding.","q_zh":"这次服务如何影响了你的看法？"},{"q":"Would you buy a more expensive pair?","a":"Only if I had a clear reason. I'd compare the features with my actual needs and try them if possible. Spending more doesn't automatically mean that a product will be more comfortable or useful for me.","q_zh":"你会买一副更贵的耳机吗？"}],"category":"事物","title_en":"Headphones, saving up and customer service","audio":"audio/f06e3e348f714cbf.m4a"},{"id":"M07","title":"祖母的花园","keywords":"童年去祖母家 → 种植物 → 我的失败 → 她教耐心 → 现在仍记得。","script":["I'd like to talk about my grandmother and a skill she taught me when I was a child. She enjoyed looking after plants, and whenever I visited her, I liked spending time in the small garden near her home.","When I was about ten, she helped me grow a plant of my own. At first, I thought I only needed to put it in the soil and water it as much as possible. She explained that plants needed the right amount of water and enough light, and that doing more wasn't always doing better.","We checked the plant together every few days. I was impatient because I wanted to see a result immediately. She encouraged me to notice small changes instead of expecting something dramatic overnight.","Eventually, I saw new leaves, and I felt surprisingly proud. It was a small achievement, but it was something I had helped create and look after myself.","What I admire about my grandmother is her patience. She didn't make me feel foolish when I made mistakes. She explained things calmly and let me try again. I still remember that experience because it taught me more than how to care for a plant. It also taught me to be consistent and to give things time."],"variants":[{"name":"手工技能","answer_script":["A person I know who is good at making things by hand is my grandmother. When I was a child, I often visited her home and watched her repair clothes or make small useful items. She enjoyed the process and didn't rush through it.","One summer, when I was about ten, she helped me make a simple cloth bag. We chose some spare material and decided on a size that I could use for a few books. She showed me how to measure it and join the pieces carefully.","My first attempt was uneven, and I wanted to start again. She explained that we could undo one small section and fix it instead. That made the task feel less intimidating. I slowly began to understand that a mistake didn't mean the whole item was ruined.","When we finished, the bag wasn't perfect, but it was useful. I felt proud that I had helped make something rather than just buy it. I used it afterwards, which made the experience more memorable.","I admire her patience and practical skills. She could turn simple materials into something that solved a small everyday problem. I don't make many things by hand now, but the lesson has stayed with me: work carefully, notice mistakes and improve one part at a time."],"module":"A person I know who is good at making things by hand is my grandmother. When I was a child, I often visited her home and watched her repair clothes or make small useful items. She enjoyed the process and didn't rush through it. One summer, when I was about ten, she helped me make a simple cloth bag. We chose some spare material and decided on a size that I could use for a few books. She showed me how to measure it and join the pieces carefully. My first attempt was uneven, and I wanted to start again. She explained that we could undo one small section and fix it instead. That made the task feel less intimidating. I slowly began to understand that a mistake didn't mean the whole item was ruined. When we finished, the bag wasn't perfect, but it was useful. I felt proud that I had helped make something rather than just buy it. I used it afterwards, which made the experience more memorable. I admire her patience and practical skills. She could turn simple materials into something that solved a small everyday problem. I don't make many things by hand now, but the lesson has stayed with me: work carefully, notice mistakes and improve one part at a time.","omit":""},{"name":"耐心倾听","answer_script":["A time I listened to something I wasn't initially interested in was when my grandmother explained how she looked after her plants. I visited her one afternoon, and she was excited to show me a plant that had produced new leaves.","At first, I didn't really care about the details. I thought she would point out the plant quickly, but she began explaining the light, watering and changes she had noticed over several weeks. I was tempted to change the subject.","I kept listening because I knew the hobby mattered to her. She had put time and effort into it, and I didn't want to make her feel that her excitement was unimportant. I put my phone away and asked a couple of simple questions.","As the conversation continued, I became more interested. I could see that she enjoyed noticing small changes and solving practical problems. I also learned why giving a plant too much attention could sometimes be less helpful than being patient.","I felt glad that I had listened properly. The conversation made her happy and helped me understand her hobby rather than just see it as a collection of pots. It reminded me that showing interest in another person's experience can matter even when the subject isn't one of my favourites."],"module":"A time I listened to something I wasn't initially interested in was when my grandmother explained how she looked after her plants. I visited her one afternoon, and she was excited to show me a plant that had produced new leaves. At first, I didn't really care about the details. I thought she would point out the plant quickly, but she began explaining the light, watering and changes she had noticed over several weeks. I was tempted to change the subject. I kept listening because I knew the hobby mattered to her. She had put time and effort into it, and I didn't want to make her feel that her excitement was unimportant. I put my phone away and asked a couple of simple questions. As the conversation continued, I became more interested. I could see that she enjoyed noticing small changes and solving practical problems. I also learned why giving a plant too much attention could sometimes be less helpful than being patient. I felt glad that I had listened properly. The conversation made her happy and helped me understand her hobby rather than just see it as a collection of pots. It reminded me that showing interest in another person's experience can matter even when the subject isn't one of my favourites.","omit":""}],"followups":[{"q":"Do you still practise that skill?","a":"Not as often as I did as a child, but I remember the basic approach. I try to notice what needs attention, make a small change and be patient with the result instead of expect immediate success.","q_zh":"你现在还练习那项技能吗？"},{"q":"Why did you enjoy learning from her?","a":"She explained things calmly and let me try for myself. When I made a mistake, she showed me how to improve it. That made learning feel less like a test and more like doing something together.","q_zh":"你当时为什么喜欢跟她学习？"},{"q":"What other quality do you admire?","a":"I admire how she values useful everyday skills. She enjoys looking after what she has and helping other people. Those qualities aren't dramatic, but they make ordinary life more comfortable and thoughtful.","q_zh":"你还欣赏她的什么品质？"}],"category":"人物","title_en":"My grandmother and her garden","audio":"audio/c3a8b306a2bcd931.m4a"},{"id":"M08","title":"朋友的生日晚餐","keywords":"朋友生日 → 简单安排 → 分工 → 蛋糕惊喜 → 朋友高兴。","script":["I'd like to describe a birthday dinner I helped organise for a friend. It happened a few months ago, and there were just a few of us. We wanted to make the evening special without turning it into a complicated or expensive event.","I checked when everyone was available and chose a place that was easy for us to reach. Another friend arranged the cake, while I made the reservation and confirmed the time. We also asked him what food he liked so that he would enjoy the meal.","On the evening itself, we arrived a little early and made sure everything was ready. The atmosphere was relaxed. We talked about work, shared some funny stories and took a few photos together.","The most memorable moment was when the cake came out. It was quite simple, but it had a small decoration connected to one of his hobbies. He hadn't expected it, and his reaction made the effort feel worthwhile.","I was pleased that the plan worked and that everyone had a good time. It reminded me that a successful celebration doesn't depend on spending a lot of money. Paying attention to the person and making time for each other can be much more important."],"variants":[{"name":"收到蛋糕","answer_script":["A special cake I received was one my friends gave me on my birthday a few months ago. I hadn't planned a large celebration, so I was surprised when they invited me to a simple dinner and brought out the cake afterwards.","It was a chocolate cake with a small decoration connected to one of my hobbies. It wasn't especially large or expensive, but the detail showed that they had thought about me. They had arranged it without telling me, which made the surprise work.","We sat together, talked about things that had happened that week and took a few photos. When the cake arrived, everyone smiled and sang. I felt slightly embarrassed by the attention at first, but it was a very warm moment.","We shared the cake after the meal. What I remember most isn't the exact taste, although I enjoyed it. It's the feeling of spending time with people who had made an effort to celebrate with me. I also kept a photo of the cake as a reminder.","The cake was special because it felt personal. A simple gift can mean a lot when it reflects something about the person receiving it. I'd like to do something similar for a friend rather than assume that a more expensive present is always better."],"module":"A special cake I received was one my friends gave me on my birthday a few months ago. I hadn't planned a large celebration, so I was surprised when they invited me to a simple dinner and brought out the cake afterwards. It was a chocolate cake with a small decoration connected to one of my hobbies. It wasn't especially large or expensive, but the detail showed that they had thought about me. They had arranged it without telling me, which made the surprise work. We sat together, talked about things that had happened that week and took a few photos. When the cake arrived, everyone smiled and sang. I felt slightly embarrassed by the attention at first, but it was a very warm moment. We shared the cake after the meal. What I remember most isn't the exact taste, although I enjoyed it. It's the feeling of spending time with people who had made an effort to celebrate with me. I also kept a photo of the cake as a reminder. The cake was special because it felt personal. A simple gift can mean a lot when it reflects something about the person receiving it. I'd like to do something similar for a friend rather than assume that a more expensive present is always better.","omit":""},{"name":"特殊场合食物","answer_script":["A food that people often eat on a special occasion is birthday cake. In my experience, it is usually brought out near the end of a birthday meal and shared with friends or family. The style depends on what the person likes.","One example I remember is a chocolate cake at a friend's birthday dinner. It had a small decoration connected to his hobby. We had arranged the dinner simply, but the cake made the evening feel more like a celebration.","A basic cake is made by preparing a mixture, baking it and then adding some decoration or a topping. I don't think the recipe has to be complicated. The important thing is that everyone can share it and that it suits the person whose birthday it is.","When we brought out my friend's cake, we gathered around, sang and took a few photos. He hadn't expected the personal decoration, so his reaction was the most memorable part. Afterwards, we cut the cake and continued talking.","I associate this food with making time for other people. It gives a group a small shared moment, rather than just another item to eat. That's why even a simple birthday cake can feel special. If the question required a traditional festival food, I'd choose a different example."],"module":"A food that people often eat on a special occasion is birthday cake. In my experience, it is usually brought out near the end of a birthday meal and shared with friends or family. The style depends on what the person likes. One example I remember is a chocolate cake at a friend's birthday dinner. It had a small decoration connected to his hobby. We had arranged the dinner simply, but the cake made the evening feel more like a celebration. A basic cake is made by preparing a mixture, baking it and then adding some decoration or a topping. I don't think the recipe has to be complicated. The important thing is that everyone can share it and that it suits the person whose birthday it is. When we brought out my friend's cake, we gathered around, sang and took a few photos. He hadn't expected the personal decoration, so his reaction was the most memorable part. Afterwards, we cut the cake and continued talking. I associate this food with making time for other people. It gives a group a small shared moment, rather than just another item to eat. That's why even a simple birthday cake can feel special. If the question required a traditional festival food, I'd choose a different example.","omit":""},{"masterId":"M08","name":"changed_plan","keywords":"朋友生日 → 野餐 → 天气 → 餐厅 → 大家满意","note":"全部生日、天气、餐厅及结果为样例。生日主角是朋友；我负责组织并改变计划。天气只是这次样例经历，没有声称某日确有公共天气事件。","answer_script":["One time I changed a plan was when I was organising a birthday gathering for a friend. My original idea was to have a small picnic outdoors. A few of us would bring food, sit together and keep the afternoon simple and inexpensive.","However, on the morning of the gathering, the weather looked windy, and the forecast suggested that rain was possible. I realised that the food and decorations would be difficult to manage outside. I also didn't want everyone to arrive and then feel uncomfortable.","I checked with the group and suggested meeting at a restaurant instead. I found somewhere within our budget, confirmed that there was room for us and sent everyone the new address and time. Another friend contacted the person bringing the cake so that it went to the right place.","The change meant that we no longer needed to prepare picnic food or carry everything outdoors. We could simply meet, order a meal and enjoy the evening. The birthday friend seemed pleased, and the atmosphere was relaxed because nobody was worrying about the weather.","I was happy with the decision because the important part of the plan was spending time together. Although the setting changed, we still achieved that. The experience taught me to keep the purpose of an event in mind and make a practical adjustment when the original arrangement becomes difficult."]},{"masterId":"M08","name":"very_happy","answer_script":["A moment when I felt extremely happy was near the end of a birthday dinner I organised for my friend Ben. It happened a few months ago at a small restaurant in Dubai. When he saw the cake and heard everyone singing, he looked completely surprised.","I checked when everyone was available and chose a place that was easy for us to reach. Another friend arranged the cake, while I made the reservation and confirmed the time. We also asked him what food he liked so that he would enjoy the meal.","On the evening itself, we arrived a little early and made sure everything was ready. The atmosphere was relaxed. We talked about work, shared some funny stories and took a few photos together.","The most memorable moment was when the cake came out. It was quite simple, but it had a small decoration connected to one of his hobbies. He hadn't expected it, and his reaction made the effort feel worthwhile.","I was pleased that the plan worked and that everyone had a good time. It reminded me that a successful celebration doesn't depend on spending a lot of money. Paying attention to the person and making time for each other can be much more important."],"keywords":"秘密准备 → 朋友生日 → 蛋糕出现 → 大家唱歌 → 看到他的笑容","note":"本题突出开心的具体时刻，其余内容沿用生日主线。","omit":"本题突出开心的具体时刻，其余内容沿用生日主线。"}],"followups":[{"q":"What made the event successful?","a":"We chose a convenient time, shared the tasks and paid attention to what our friend liked. The plan was simple enough to manage. The personal decoration on the cake mattered more than making the evening expensive.","q_zh":"是什么让这次活动取得了成功？"},{"q":"Would you organise another event?","a":"Yes, although I would confirm the main details earlier. Knowing the number of people and the food preferences makes the rest easier. I'd still keep the focus on spending time together rather than add too many activities.","q_zh":"你会再组织一次活动吗？"},{"q":"Was the cake the most important thing?","a":"It created a memorable moment, but the company was more important. Without people making time to be there, the cake would just have been food. I remember the conversation and the thought behind the surprise.","q_zh":"蛋糕是当时最重要的东西吗？"}],"category":"经历","title_en":"A birthday dinner for a friend","audio":"audio/3fab4a86ba272c39.m4a"},{"id":"M09","title":"童年好友 Ben：语言学习、历史兴趣与友谊","keywords":"childhood friend → good at learning languages → English and Chinese → history lover → old photographs → museum","example_notice":"可修改的虚构练习样例。Ben、童年经历、语言能力及相处细节均不是用户已确认的事实；使用前替换为能自然讲述的人和经历。","script":["I'd like to talk about my childhood friend Ben. We grew up in the same neighbourhood and became friends when we were about ten. We used to ride our bikes after school, and although we now live in different cities, we still talk regularly.","One thing I admire about him is the way he learns languages. He studies English by watching short videos with subtitles, noting useful expressions and recording himself using them. He also learns Chinese, and we practise together through voice messages. Rather than memorising long lists, he uses new words in simple conversations. Recently, he managed to order a meal in Chinese and ask the waiter about the ingredients without switching to English.","Ben is also interested in history. He once found a box of his grandfather's old photographs and asked him about the people and places in them. He put the pictures in an album with short descriptions. When we visited a local museum, he explained how an old railway had changed the town.","What makes our friendship special is that he never makes me feel embarrassed when I get something wrong. He corrects me gently and usually adds a funny example. He's curious, patient and easy to talk to, so spending time with him always feels worthwhile."],"variants":[{"name":"擅长学习和说语言的人","module":"What impresses me most is how confidently Ben uses the languages he learns. When we practise Chinese, he asks me to correct one or two mistakes at a time. The following week, those mistakes have usually disappeared. He also records the same English story twice and compares the recordings, so he can hear whether his speech is becoming clearer.","omit":"用此模块替换第3段的历史故事；保留第1、2、4段。题目焦点放在具体学习方法、实际表现和我的评价。","answer_script":["Someone I know who's good at learning languages is my childhood friend Ben. We became friends when we were about ten, and we still practise together through voice messages even though we now live in different cities.","One thing I admire about him is the way he learns languages. He studies English by watching short videos with subtitles, noting useful expressions and recording himself using them. He also learns Chinese, and we practise together through voice messages. Rather than memorising long lists, he uses new words in simple conversations. Recently, he managed to order a meal in Chinese and ask the waiter about the ingredients without switching to English.","What impresses me most is how confidently Ben uses the languages he learns. When we practise Chinese, he asks me to correct one or two mistakes at a time. The following week, those mistakes have usually disappeared. He also records the same English story twice and compares the recordings, so he can hear whether his speech is becoming clearer.","I admire his patience as much as his progress. When I make a mistake, he corrects me gently and adds a funny example, so the conversation doesn't become stressful. He has shown me that improving a language can come from small daily habits, rather than waiting until you feel ready to speak."]},{"name":"学习并喜欢历史的人","module":"The person I'd choose is Ben, a childhood friend who loves history. His interest started with his grandfather's photographs. He wanted to know why the streets looked different, so he compared the pictures with the town today. At the museum, he showed me a railway map and explained how trains had helped local shops grow. He made the subject feel personal.","omit":"用此模块替换第2段的语言学习细节；保留第1、3、4段。第1段开头与模块首句重复时，删第1段首句。","answer_script":["I'd like to talk about Ben, a childhood friend who learns about history in his free time. We grew up in the same neighbourhood, and we still talk regularly. His interest has made me look at familiar places differently.","His interest started with a box of his grandfather's old photographs. Ben wanted to know who the people were and why the streets looked different. He asked his grandfather about them and put the pictures in an album with short descriptions. It became a record of his family's life as well as the town's history.","When we visited a local museum, he showed me an old railway map and explained how trains had helped the town develop. He didn't just repeat dates from the labels. He connected the railway with local shops, jobs and travel, which made the explanation easy to follow.","He also takes photographs of interesting museum displays and looks up unfamiliar details afterwards. I used to think history was mostly about remembering facts for school, but his enthusiasm changed my mind. Through him, I've realised that it can explain ordinary places and help us understand how people lived before us."]},{"name":"童年好友","module":"My clearest memory of Ben is from a school sports day. I fell off my bike on the way home and felt embarrassed because other children were watching. He stayed with me, checked that I was all right and walked his own bike beside mine. It was a small gesture, but it showed me that I could count on him.","omit":"用此模块替换第3段的历史故事；保留第1、2、4段。讲友谊时，把语言兴趣当作我们现在仍有联系的原因。","answer_script":["I'd like to talk about my childhood friend Ben. We grew up in the same neighbourhood and became friends when we were about ten. We used to ride our bikes after school, and although we now live in different cities, we still talk regularly.","My clearest memory of Ben is from a school sports day. I fell off my bike on the way home and felt embarrassed because other children were watching. He stayed with me, checked that I was all right and walked his own bike beside mine. It was a small gesture, but it showed me that I could count on him.","We were both quite curious as children. We built small things from cardboard, borrowed books from the library and argued about which bike route was faster. These days, we have different interests and live in different cities, but we still exchange messages. He sometimes practises Chinese with me, and I ask him about his latest history project.","What makes the friendship valuable is that we can speak honestly without trying to impress each other. He remembers what I was like before I started working, and that makes talking to him feel comfortable. I'm glad we've stayed in touch because a friendship like that has grown through years of ordinary, shared experiences."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do some people learn languages faster than others?","a":"People improve faster when they practise regularly and use the language for a clear purpose. For example, someone who needs Chinese to speak to friends gets immediate feedback. That can be more useful than studying vocabulary without ever using it.","q_zh":"为什么有些人学语言比别人快？"},{"q":"How can teachers make history interesting?","a":"Teachers can connect history with places students already know. They could compare old photographs with today's streets or visit a local museum. These activities give students something concrete to discuss, instead of asking them to remember dates in isolation.","q_zh":"老师如何能让历史课变得有趣？"},{"q":"Why do childhood friendships sometimes last?","a":"Childhood friends often share experiences that later friends cannot fully understand. They remember your family, school and early interests. However, shared memories are not enough by themselves. Keeping in touch and showing interest in each other's lives still matter.","q_zh":"为什么有些童年友谊能长久维持？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"人物","title_en":"Ben, a childhood friend who enjoys languages and history","audio":"audio/8392c3b8e44b8b71.m4a"},{"id":"M10","title":"表妹 Sara：想成为护士的人","keywords":"medical career → nurse → cousin → volunteering → patient communication → future plans","example_notice":"可修改的虚构练习样例。Sara、亲属关系、外婆住院及志愿活动均不是用户事实；志愿者只做非医疗事务，没有进行临床操作。","script":["I'd like to talk about my cousin Sara, who wants to become a nurse. She's a few years younger than me, and we've known each other since childhood. We usually meet at family gatherings, but recently we've also been talking about her future career.","Her interest in nursing began when our grandmother spent several days in hospital. Sara noticed that the nurses did much more than check equipment. They explained what was happening and helped our grandmother feel less anxious. She said she wanted a job where her work could make a practical difference to someone's day.","To explore the idea, she volunteered at a community health event last summer. Her role was simple: welcoming visitors, showing them where to queue and helping them complete basic forms. She didn't provide medical treatment. One older visitor was confused about the registration process, and Sara patiently explained each step. Afterwards, she told me that she had enjoyed helping him feel comfortable.","Her plan is to apply for a nursing course, improve her science knowledge and keep volunteering when she can. She knows the work can involve long shifts and difficult situations, so she doesn't see it as an easy career. I admire her because her ambition is based on real interest and some first-hand experience, rather than just the title."],"variants":[{"name":"想从事医疗行业的人","module":"The person I'd choose is Sara, my cousin, who hopes to become a nurse. What makes her suitable is her patience. At the community event, she didn't rush people who needed extra help. She listened, repeated instructions clearly and checked that they understood. I think these habits would help her communicate well with patients, although she would still need proper professional training.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段和第4段；保留第2、3段。模块放开头，末尾补一句：That's why I think she would find nursing both demanding and meaningful.","answer_script":["I'd like to talk about my cousin Sara, who wants to become a nurse. She's a few years younger than me, and we've known each other since childhood. We usually meet at family gatherings, but recently we've also been talking about her future career.","Her interest in nursing began when our grandmother spent several days in hospital. Sara noticed that the nurses did much more than check equipment. They explained what was happening and helped our grandmother feel less anxious. She said she wanted a job where her work could make a practical difference to someone's day.","To explore the idea, she volunteered at a community health event last summer. Her role was simple: welcoming visitors, showing them where to queue and helping them complete basic forms. She didn't provide medical treatment. One older visitor was confused about the registration process, and Sara patiently explained each step. Afterwards, she told me that she had enjoyed helping him feel comfortable.","Her plan is to apply for a nursing course, improve her science knowledge and keep volunteering when she can. She knows the work can involve long shifts and difficult situations, so she doesn't see it as an easy career. I admire her because her ambition is based on real interest and some first-hand experience, rather than just the title."]},{"name":"想一起学习或工作的人","module":"I'd like to study with Sara because she's reliable and willing to ask questions. We once prepared a short presentation about healthy daily habits together. She checked the sources, organised the slides and noticed when our explanation was confusing. I handled the introduction, and she prepared the examples. Working with her felt calm because we both knew what we needed to do.","omit":"用此模块替换第3段的志愿服务；第1段第二句后加：I'd also be happy to study or work with her. 保留第2、4段，只作认识背景和能力评价。","answer_script":["A person I'd like to study or work with is my cousin Sara. She's a few years younger than me, and we've known each other since childhood. She's interested in becoming a nurse, but what I'd like to describe is how well we cooperate.","We once prepared a short presentation about healthy daily habits together. She checked the sources and organised the slides, while I handled the introduction and examples. When part of our explanation was confusing, she pointed it out politely and suggested a clearer way to say it.","I also saw her volunteer at a community health event. She welcomed visitors, helped with basic forms and explained where people needed to queue. She didn't provide medical treatment. One older visitor needed extra help, and she stayed patient instead of rushing him. That showed me she'd be supportive when a team faced a problem.","I'd enjoy working with her because she completes her part and asks questions when she's unsure. We could divide tasks clearly and check each other's work without turning every disagreement into an argument. For me, a good partner doesn't have to know everything; being reliable and willing to communicate is much more useful."]},{"name":"帮助别人改善健康的人（明确为日常习惯）","module":"Sara helped our grandmother build a healthier daily routine after she returned home. Following the advice our grandmother had already received from her healthcare team, Sara kept her company on short walks and made a simple reminder chart. She didn't change any treatment or give medical advice. What she provided was encouragement, which made our grandmother more willing to stick to the routine.","omit":"用此模块替换第3段；第1段首句改为：I'd like to describe my cousin Sara, who helped our grandmother improve her daily habits. 第4段只保留对Sara的评价，删课程计划句。","answer_script":["I'd like to describe my cousin Sara, who helped our grandmother improve her daily habits. Our grandmother had spent a few days in hospital and was following advice from her healthcare team when she returned home. Sara helped her keep to that routine.","For example, she kept our grandmother company on short walks and made a simple reminder chart. She didn't change any treatment or give medical advice. Her role was to encourage her and make the routine less lonely. At first, our grandmother found it difficult to stay motivated, especially when she felt bored.","Sara responded patiently. Instead of making every conversation about health, she chatted about family news during the walks and let our grandmother describe how she was feeling. She also celebrated small achievements, such as following the routine for a week. Gradually, our grandmother became more willing to take part.","I admire Sara because she understood that support can be practical and emotional at the same time. She now wants to become a nurse and plans to apply for a nursing course. This experience helped her see that caring for someone isn't just about knowing facts; listening and being consistent can matter a great deal."]}],"followups":[{"q":"What qualities are important for medical workers?","a":"Medical workers need sound professional knowledge, but communication also matters. A patient may be frightened or confused, so clear explanations and patience can help. Reliability is essential too, because small mistakes or missed information can affect somebody's care.","q_zh":"医务工作者需要具备哪些重要品质？"},{"q":"Is volunteering a useful way to choose a career?","a":"Yes, it gives people a more realistic picture of a workplace. A volunteer at a community event might discover whether they enjoy helping strangers. However, a short experience cannot show every responsibility, so they should also speak to trained professionals.","q_zh":"做志愿者有助于选择职业吗？"},{"q":"Should people choose a job mainly for the salary?","a":"Salary matters because people need financial security, but it shouldn't be the only consideration. In a demanding profession like nursing, interest in the work and realistic expectations are also important. Otherwise, someone may become dissatisfied even with reasonable pay.","q_zh":"人们应该主要根据薪水来选择工作吗？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"人物","title_en":"Sara, who wants to become a nurse","audio":"audio/ac913d1a1e925fba.m4a"},{"id":"M11","title":"迪拜名人 Huda Kattan：创业人物、真实采访与真实广告","keywords":"Dubai local celebrity → popular person → successful entrepreneur → overcoming difficulty → ForbesWomen interview → FauxFilter campaign","example_notice":"Huda Kattan及公开创业资料是真实对象，来源已核验。第一人称如何认识她、何时阅读/观看、个人感受是可修改样例，不表示用户曾见过她、看过采访或购买产品。采访与广告模块使用各自的真实来源；Global Women's Forum材料只作创业事实来源，不能叫采访。","script":["I'd like to talk about Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. She's a well-known businesswoman associated with Dubai. I first became interested in her after seeing her brand in a shopping mall, although I know about her through public sources rather than personally.","Her business began in Dubai in 2013 with false eyelashes. Before that, she worked as a makeup artist and beauty blogger. What interested me was that she didn't begin with a clear plan for a large company. She developed her idea step by step, and the brand eventually expanded beyond Dubai.","I read an account of her appearance at the Global Women's Forum Dubai in 2024. She discussed self-doubt and the need to keep moving forward. I found that useful because starting something new can feel uncomfortable, even when you have the right skills. Her story made success seem like a process of learning and making decisions.","I'm not especially interested in makeup, but I am interested in how people build businesses. To me, her appeal comes from combining practical knowledge with a way of communicating that people understand. If I had the chance to meet her, I'd ask how she decides which customer suggestions to follow. That's why I find her memorable."],"variants":[{"name":"当地名人","module":"A well-known person in Dubai I'd like to describe is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. I think she's popular because people can connect a recognisable person with the brand. She has shared beauty content as well as built a company, so her public image feels more personal than a business name printed on a shop sign.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段；保留第2、3、4段。当地名人不要求她出生于迪拜；不要把她说成阿联酋籍。","answer_script":["A well-known person in Dubai I'd like to describe is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. I think she's popular because people can connect a recognisable person with the brand. She has shared beauty content as well as built a company, so her public image feels more personal than a business name printed on a shop sign.","Her business began in Dubai in 2013 with false eyelashes. Before that, she worked as a makeup artist and beauty blogger. What interested me was that she didn't begin with a clear plan for a large company. She developed her idea step by step, and the brand eventually expanded beyond Dubai.","I first became interested in her after seeing the brand in a shopping mall. I then read some public articles to learn more. I'm interested in how someone becomes associated with a place through their work, even when the business reaches customers in many other countries.","I'm not especially interested in makeup, but I do enjoy learning how people build businesses. To me, her appeal comes from combining practical knowledge with a way of communicating that people understand. If I had the chance to meet her, I'd ask how she decides which customer suggestions to follow. That's why I find her memorable."]},{"name":"受欢迎的人","module":"A popular person I'd like to describe is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. I think people find her memorable because a recognisable person stands behind the products. For me, that makes the brand easier to relate to. I don't need to be a makeup enthusiast to find the connection between her public image and her business interesting.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段；保留第2、3、4段。题目焦点是人气及原因，不引用未经核验的粉丝数。","answer_script":["A popular person I'd like to describe is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. She's well known in Dubai, and I first became interested in her after seeing the brand in a shopping mall. I know about her through public sources.","Her business began in Dubai in 2013 with false eyelashes. Before that, she worked as a makeup artist and beauty blogger. I think one reason people remember her is that they can connect a recognisable person with the products. The company feels more personal than a name printed on a shop sign.","Another thing I find interesting is the connection between a founder's name and a company's identity. When I see her name on the products, I think about an individual with ideas and responsibilities, rather than just a logo. That personal connection is one reason the brand stays in my memory.","I'm not especially interested in makeup, so my interest isn't about wanting every product she sells. I like seeing how someone turns practical knowledge into a business and communicates with customers. That's what makes her appealing to me. I would be interested in meeting her and asking how she decides which customer suggestions to follow."]},{"name":"克服困难并成功的人","module":"What stands out to me is that Huda has publicly discussed moments of self-doubt. Building something new without a clear path can be difficult, and confidence doesn't necessarily come first. Sometimes you gain it by taking one manageable step and learning from the result. I admire that approach because it sounds more realistic than pretending successful people never feel uncertain.","omit":"用此模块替换第3段；保留第1、2、4段。困难限定为公开谈过的自我怀疑和创业路径不清晰，不编造破产、借款或个人失败。","answer_script":["A person I know about who overcame difficulties and became successful is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. She's associated with Dubai, and I became interested in her through public articles about her business. I've never met her personally.","She launched her brand in Dubai in 2013 with false eyelashes, after working as a makeup artist and beauty blogger. Building a company from an idea is a considerable challenge, especially when there isn't a clear route to follow. It involves decisions as well as practical skills.","In an account of her appearance at the Global Women's Forum Dubai in 2024, she discussed moments of self-doubt and the importance of continuing. What I take from that is that confidence doesn't always come first. Sometimes you gain it by taking one manageable step and learning from the result.","I admire this because it sounds more realistic than imagining successful people never feel uncertain. When I face an unfamiliar project, I can waste time trying to have a perfect plan before I begin. Her story reminds me to identify the next useful action, get some feedback and adjust. For me, that is a valuable lesson from her success."]},{"name":"在成功公司工作的人","module":"The person I'd choose is Huda Kattan, who works in the company she founded, Huda Beauty. I would describe the business as successful because it grew from a product launched in Dubai into a brand selling beyond the region. As a founder, she represents both the products and the business. That combination of creative work and responsibility interests me.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段；保留第2、3、4段。若题目明确要求你私人认识的员工，改用M12，不能声称与Huda有私人关系。","answer_script":["The person I'd choose is Huda Kattan, who works in the company she founded, Huda Beauty. It's a cosmetics business associated with Dubai. I know about her through public sources, and I became interested after seeing the brand in a shopping mall.","The brand launched in 2013 and is based in Dubai. Its products are sold through its own online store as well as retailers such as Sephora. I would describe it as successful because it has grown beyond the place where it began and has a recognisable name.","What interests me about Huda's work is that being a founder involves both creative decisions and business responsibility. I imagine these roles sometimes pull in different directions: a product may be exciting, but the company also has to consider customers, timing and cost. That makes the job demanding.","I'd like to ask her how she decides which ideas deserve more attention and which ones should be dropped. I'm interested in that process because teams often have more ideas than time. I find her work memorable because it shows how practical expertise can develop into a business, and how communicating clearly can help people understand what the company offers."]},{"name":"看过的名人采访（ForbesWomen真实采访）","module":"I'd like to describe a YouTube interview with Huda Kattan that I watched one evening at home. It was published by ForbesWomen in April 2022 and was called 'Huda Kattan On Building The Next Billion-Dollar Brand'. She discussed her entrepreneurial journey and what making an impact in beauty meant to her. I found it interesting because the focus was on her ideas and business experience, rather than simply promoting a product.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段和第3段；保留第2、4段。模块放在开头，第4段的If I had the chance to meet her句可保留作个人感受。此处的观看时间是样例，可改为实际时间；引用的是ForbesWomen采访，不是论坛讲话。","answer_script":["I'd like to describe a YouTube interview with Huda Kattan that I watched one evening at home. It was published by ForbesWomen in April 2022 and was called 'Huda Kattan On Building The Next Billion-Dollar Brand'. She discussed her entrepreneurial journey and what making an impact in beauty meant to her. I found it interesting because the focus was on her ideas and business experience, rather than simply promoting a product.","I already knew that she was the founder of Huda Beauty, a company associated with Dubai, but I wanted to hear more about the person behind the brand. I watched the interview on my laptop at home, when I had enough time to follow it without rushing.","The subject that interested me was the experience of turning an idea into a business. I liked considering what success means beyond having a recognisable name. My reaction was that an interview can be useful when it helps you think about the decisions a person makes, rather than only their public image.","I don't work in the beauty industry, but I enjoy hearing how people approach a challenge in another field. It gives me a different perspective on my own work. I felt more curious about how founders balance creative ideas with responsibility, and I'd recommend this interview to a friend who's interested in starting a business."]},{"name":"名人出演的广告（#FauxFilter真实宣传照）","module":"I'd like to describe an online advertisement for Huda Beauty's #FauxFilter foundation featuring Huda Kattan. I saw the campaign image on the brand's website. It showed her with other women in a group photograph, and the product was being promoted through the campaign. What caught my attention was that the image felt friendly and personal. It made me curious about how brands use their founders in advertising.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段和第3段；保留第2段。第4段改用本条closing，避免继续回答人物题。该素材是品牌官方网页上的2017年产品广告宣传照，不是电视广告，也不是采访。","closing":"I found it memorable because the person behind the company appeared in its own advertising. That gave the brand a human face. It didn't make me buy the foundation, but it encouraged me to find out more about the business and the story behind it.","answer_script":["I'd like to describe an online advertisement for Huda Beauty's #FauxFilter foundation featuring Huda Kattan. I saw the campaign image on the brand's website. It showed her with other women in a group photograph, and the product was being promoted through the campaign. What caught my attention was that the image felt friendly and personal. It made me curious about how brands use their founders in advertising.","The image was part of the brand's 2017 campaign, which I found through an article called 'The Making Of Our #FauxFilter Foundation'. The article explained that Huda appeared in a group picture taken near the end of the shoot. I liked the connection between the founder and the product being advertised.","I'm not particularly interested in buying foundation, but I found the advertising idea interesting. A company can show a product on its own, or it can introduce a person who helps customers recognise the brand. In this case, seeing Huda made me curious about the business behind the image.","The advertisement was memorable because it had a human element. It didn't persuade me to buy something I didn't need, but it encouraged me to learn more about the company. I think that's a useful effect of advertising: attracting interest first, while leaving customers to decide whether the product is relevant to them."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do people admire successful businesspeople?","a":"People may admire them because they turn an idea into something useful and create jobs. Their stories can also make difficult goals feel possible. Still, I think we should judge their decisions and behaviour, instead of admiring wealth alone.","q_zh":"人们为什么钦佩成功的商人？"},{"q":"Do famous people make advertisements more effective?","a":"They can attract attention and help people remember a product. A founder may also explain why the product was developed. However, fame doesn't prove quality, so customers should still consider whether the product meets their needs and fits their budget.","q_zh":"名人能让广告更有效吗？"},{"q":"What makes an interview interesting?","a":"An interesting interview asks specific questions and gives the guest space to explain. I prefer hearing about a decision and its consequences to hearing general advice. Follow-up questions are useful because they can reveal details the guest might otherwise leave out.","q_zh":"什么会让一次采访变得有趣？"},{"q":"What should young people learn from celebrities?","a":"They can learn practical habits such as working consistently, accepting feedback and communicating clearly. However, they should also remember that a public story is selective. Copying a celebrity's daily routine may be less useful than understanding the decisions behind it.","q_zh":"年轻人应该向名人学习什么？"}],"verified_sources":[{"title":"Dubai Women Establishment: Global Women's Forum Dubai account","url":"https://dwe.gov.ae/en/media-center/huda-kattan-says-dubai-fuelled-her-journey-to-global-success-at-the-global-womens-forum-ceo-and-founder-of-huda-beauty-highlights-dubais-pivotal-role-in-her-entrepreneurial-success/","published":"2024-11-26","accessed":"2026-10-07","supports":"Dubai起步；2013年以假睫毛推出品牌；早期美容博客及化妆师经历；创业路径、自我怀疑与坚持；扩展至欧洲和美国。属于论坛活动报道，不是采访证据。"},{"title":"ForbesWomen: Extended Interview | Huda Kattan On Building The Next Billion-Dollar Brand","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCRBsfazOJ0","published":"2022-04-03","accessed":"2026-10-07","supports":"已核验发布者、标题、日期及官方描述：在2022 Forbes 30/50 Summit坐下来接受采访，谈创业历程及美妆领域影响。未声称完整逐字观看或核验具体对话，模块不杜撰问题、引语或时码。"},{"title":"Huda Beauty: The Making Of Our #FauxFilter Foundation","url":"https://hudabeauty.com/en-sr/blogs/beauty-news/the-making-of-our-fauxfilter-foundation","published":"2017-10-04","accessed":"2026-10-07","supports":"品牌官方产品campaign文章；Campaign Shoot段明确Huda出现在最后的群体拥抱照片；模块将其描述为线上产品宣传照，不冒充电视广告。"},{"title":"Huda Beauty company profile","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/hudabeauty","accessed":"2026-10-07","supports":"品牌2013年成立，总部Dubai，创始人与内容/产品工作的关系。避免使用会变动的粉丝数量、员工数量、职务或收入。"},{"title":"Madame Tussauds Dubai: Huda and Mona Kattan","url":"https://www.madametussauds.com/dubai/information/news/huda-and-mona-kattan/","published":"2022-09-20","accessed":"2026-10-07","supports":"迪拜本地知名人物边界；Huda Beauty于2013年成立及以假睫毛闻名的品牌背景。"}],"category":"人物","title_en":"Huda Kattan: business, an interview and an advertisement","audio":"audio/f78f518542c58a59.m4a"},{"id":"M12","title":"朋友 Alex 的小咖啡店：成功生意、条理与快乐","keywords":"small business → coffee shop → successful businessperson → organised person → happy person → customer service → solving difficulties","example_notice":"可修改的虚构练习样例。Alex、咖啡店、经营问题与解决办法均未被确认属于用户经历；使用前改为自己熟悉且能回答细节的问题。","script":["I'd like to talk about my friend Alex, who runs a small coffee shop near a residential area. I met him through a mutual friend a few years ago. Since then, I've visited his shop fairly often, usually on a Saturday morning.","When he first opened it, the business was difficult. There weren't many customers in the morning, and some food was left unsold at the end of each day. Instead of immediately spending more money on advertising, he asked regular customers what they wanted and checked which items actually sold.","He reduced the menu to a few reliable choices, prepared smaller batches and introduced a simple breakfast combination. He also created a quiet corner where customers could read or work. Gradually, people started coming back. What I like most is the service: he remembers regular customers' orders and deals with problems politely. Once, my coffee arrived cold, and he replaced it without making the situation awkward.","I think the shop succeeds because he understands his customers and pays attention to everyday details. He keeps a clear stock list and gives his team sensible tasks, but he's also friendly and enjoys chatting with people. I'm pleased to see his hard work paying off. His experience reminds me that running a good business often depends on steady improvements, rather than one dramatic idea."],"variants":[{"name":"有条理的人","module":"The person I'd choose is Alex, a friend who runs a coffee shop. Before opening each morning, he checks a short list covering supplies, cleaning and staff duties. He labels the ingredients and records what needs replacing. When the shop gets busy, everybody already knows their role. I like his approach because it prevents confusion without turning every small task into a complicated process.","omit":"用此模块替换第1段；保留第2、3段作为条理带来的结果。第4段最后一句改为：He has shown me that being organised can make work calmer and more efficient.","answer_script":["The person I'd choose is Alex, a friend who runs a coffee shop. Before opening each morning, he checks a short list covering supplies, cleaning and staff duties. He labels the ingredients and records what needs replacing. When the shop gets busy, everybody already knows their role. I like his approach because it prevents confusion without turning every small task into a complicated process.","I met him through a mutual friend a few years ago and now visit the shop quite often. When he first opened it, some food was left unsold at the end of each day. He checked which items sold and asked regular customers what they wanted.","He then reduced the menu, prepared smaller batches and introduced a simple breakfast combination. He keeps track of stock and gives his team sensible tasks, so less time is wasted wondering what to do next. When I visited on a busy Saturday, he could explain a customer's order while still keeping the queue moving.","What I admire is that his system is practical. He doesn't spend the whole day making lists; he uses short checks to prevent problems and then gets on with the work. He has shown me that being organised can make a busy workplace calmer. I now try to make my own task lists shorter and clearer for the same reason."]},{"name":"快乐的人","module":"What makes Alex seem happy is the way he treats ordinary moments. He greets familiar customers warmly and jokes with his team when the shop is quiet. Even after a tiring shift, he enjoys telling me about a small improvement, like a customer recommending the shop to a neighbour. He doesn't pretend everything is perfect, but he notices what has gone well.","omit":"用此模块替换第2段的困难背景；保留第1、3、4段。第1段首句改为：I'd like to describe my friend Alex, who usually seems cheerful and satisfied with his work.","answer_script":["I'd like to describe my friend Alex, who usually seems cheerful and satisfied with his work. He runs a small coffee shop near a residential area. I met him through a mutual friend, and I visit his shop quite often on Saturday mornings.","What makes Alex seem happy is the way he treats ordinary moments. He greets familiar customers warmly and jokes with his team when the shop is quiet. Even after a tiring shift, he enjoys telling me about a small improvement, like a customer recommending the shop to a neighbour. He doesn't pretend everything is perfect, but he notices what has gone well.","I think his happiness comes partly from doing work that allows him to meet people. He remembers regular customers' orders and enjoys hearing about their week. Once, when my coffee arrived cold, he made a fresh one and checked that it was right. He handled the problem calmly instead of letting it spoil the atmosphere.","Of course, running the shop involves long days and practical difficulties. What I admire is that he can acknowledge those problems and still enjoy the good parts of his work. His mood often makes other people feel relaxed too. When I leave the shop, I usually feel a little better, even if I've only stopped for a quick coffee."]},{"name":"做困难事情并成功的人","module":"Alex's biggest difficulty was making the shop financially sustainable when there were too few customers. He couldn't simply ignore the waste or wait for things to improve. He looked at sales, spoke to customers and changed the menu. I respect him because he dealt with the problem patiently. The shop now has regular visitors, which gives him a much more stable business.","omit":"用此模块替换第4段；保留第1、2、3段。强调困难、行动、可见结果和我的感受，不编造营业收入。","answer_script":["I'd like to talk about my friend Alex, who runs a small coffee shop near a residential area. I met him through a mutual friend a few years ago. Since then, I've visited his shop fairly often, usually on a Saturday morning.","When he first opened it, the business was difficult. There weren't many customers in the morning, and some food was left unsold at the end of each day. Instead of immediately spending more money on advertising, he asked regular customers what they wanted and checked which items actually sold.","He reduced the menu to a few reliable choices, prepared smaller batches and introduced a simple breakfast combination. He also created a quiet corner where customers could read or work. Gradually, people started coming back. What I like most is the service: he remembers regular customers' orders and deals with problems politely. Once, my coffee arrived cold, and he replaced it without making the situation awkward.","I'm pleased to see his hard work paying off. I respect him because he looked at the actual problem instead of hoping it would disappear. The shop now has regular visitors, and his experience reminds me that success can come from a series of sensible improvements, rather than one dramatic idea."]},{"name":"在店里得到好服务","module":"I'd like to describe a time I received good service at my friend Alex's coffee shop. I went there one Saturday morning and ordered a latte, but it arrived colder than I expected. When I mentioned it, he listened, apologised and made a fresh one. He also checked that the replacement was right. I appreciated how quickly he solved the problem.","omit":"用此模块替换第1、2段；第3段只保留服务描写，删除菜单、早餐、阅读区及重复的冷咖啡例子。第4段只保留对服务和细节的评价。","answer_script":["I'd like to describe a time I received good service at my friend Alex's coffee shop. I went there one Saturday morning and ordered a latte, but it arrived colder than I expected. When I mentioned it, he listened, apologised and made a fresh one. He also checked that the replacement was right. I appreciated how quickly he solved the problem.","I met Alex through a mutual friend a few years ago, and I visit his shop fairly often. Even so, I didn't want him to replace my coffee just because we were friends. I appreciated that he handled it in the same professional way he would handle any customer's complaint.","The replacement arrived quickly, and he asked me to try it before he went back behind the counter. He didn't make excuses or suggest that I was being difficult. That small response helped me feel comfortable about saying what was wrong, and I could enjoy the rest of my visit.","For me, good service isn't about making everything perfect the first time. It's also about listening and solving a problem politely when something goes wrong. I left feeling that the shop cared about its customers. I've continued going there, partly because the coffee is good and partly because I know an issue will be taken seriously."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do some small businesses succeed?","a":"Successful small businesses often understand a specific group of customers and keep their costs under control. A neighbourhood coffee shop, for example, can benefit from reliable service and repeat visits. Consistency may matter more than offering a huge menu.","q_zh":"为什么有些小企业能取得成功？"},{"q":"Is it important for managers to be organised?","a":"Yes, because other people depend on their decisions. Clear schedules and responsibilities help a team avoid wasted effort. However, managers should leave room for unexpected problems. A detailed plan is useful only if they can adjust it when circumstances change.","q_zh":"对管理者来说，做事有条理重要吗？"},{"q":"Does enjoying your job make you happier?","a":"It can, because work takes up a large part of our week. Enjoying daily tasks and getting along with colleagues can improve someone's mood. However, reasonable working hours and financial security matter too; interest alone cannot solve every workplace problem.","q_zh":"喜欢自己的工作会让你更快乐吗？"},{"q":"What makes customers return to a shop?","a":"Customers usually return when they know what to expect. Good quality, fair prices and friendly service all help. If something goes wrong, handling it politely can also build trust. Remembering a regular customer's preferences makes the experience more personal.","q_zh":"什么会让顾客再次光顾一家店？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"人物","title_en":"Alex and his small cafe","audio":"audio/0d51a56c67d10354.m4a"},{"id":"M13","title":"Roger Federer：钦佩的运动员与克服困难","keywords":"运动员 → 钦佩的人 → 克服困难 → 成功人士 → 想见的人 → 现场体育赛事（独立版本）","usage_notes":["所有个人观看、学习和到场经历均为可修改样例，不代表用户事实。","母稿讲钦佩的运动员；克服困难题突出2016年受伤与2017年复出。","现场体育赛事模块使用另一场真实比赛，不能把Federer录像或电视观看说成亲临现场。到场和同行经历仅为样例。"],"script":["I'd like to talk about Roger Federer, the retired Swiss tennis player. I first became interested in him when I watched some of his matches on television as a student. I didn't understand every rule, but I could tell that his movement and timing were special.","He finished his career with twenty Grand Slam singles titles, including eight Wimbledon titles. What I admire most, though, is the way he makes a difficult sport look natural. His movements seem smooth, and watching him has made me appreciate the importance of technique.","One part of his career that really impressed me was his return after injury. He missed the second half of the 2016 season because of a knee problem. Then, in 2017, he came back and won both the Australian Open and Wimbledon. To me, that is a powerful example of recovering from a setback.","I also like the fact that I can learn something from his story without becoming a professional athlete. When I'm struggling with a new skill, I sometimes expect results too quickly. Thinking about his comeback reminds me to be patient, work on the basics and give myself time. That's why I admire him as both a sportsman and an example of persistence."],"variants":[{"name":"克服困难的人：替换第1段","module":"The person I'd choose is Roger Federer, because his comeback after a knee injury really impressed me. I learned about it while watching a programme about his career. The difficulty wasn't just missing matches; he had to return to a demanding sport after several months away. I haven't experienced anything on that scale, but his story changed how I think about setbacks and the time needed to recover.","omit":"删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留第2至4段，第3段是重点。","word_count":68,"answer_script":["The person I'd choose is Roger Federer, because his comeback after a knee injury really impressed me. I learned about it while watching a programme about his career. The difficulty wasn't just missing matches; he had to return to a demanding sport after several months away. I haven't experienced anything on that scale, but his story changed how I think about setbacks and the time needed to recover.","He finished his career with twenty Grand Slam singles titles, including eight Wimbledon titles. What I admire most, though, is the way he makes a difficult sport look natural. His movements seem smooth, and watching him has made me appreciate the importance of technique.","One part of his career that really impressed me was his return after injury. He missed the second half of the 2016 season because of a knee problem. Then, in 2017, he came back and won both the Australian Open and Wimbledon. To me, that is a powerful example of recovering from a setback.","I also like the fact that I can learn something from his story without becoming a professional athlete. When I'm struggling with a new skill, I sometimes expect results too quickly. Thinking about his comeback reminds me to be patient, work on the basics and give myself time. That's why I admire him as both a sportsman and an example of persistence."],"answer_word_count":228},{"name":"想见的名人：替换第1段","module":"A famous person I'd really like to meet is Roger Federer. I've watched many of his matches, and I'd love to hear how he dealt with pressure and setbacks during his career. If I had a few minutes with him, I'd ask how he stayed motivated when progress was slow. I'd be more interested in his approach to learning than in getting a photograph or discussing his trophies.","omit":"删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留其余段落。不要改成已经见过他。","word_count":68,"answer_script":["A famous person I'd really like to meet is Roger Federer. I've watched many of his matches, and I'd love to hear how he dealt with pressure and setbacks during his career. If I had a few minutes with him, I'd ask how he stayed motivated when progress was slow. I'd be more interested in his approach to learning than in getting a photograph or discussing his trophies.","He finished his career with twenty Grand Slam singles titles, including eight Wimbledon titles. What I admire most, though, is the way he makes a difficult sport look natural. His movements seem smooth, and watching him has made me appreciate the importance of technique.","One part of his career that really impressed me was his return after injury. He missed the second half of the 2016 season because of a knee problem. Then, in 2017, he came back and won both the Australian Open and Wimbledon. To me, that is a powerful example of recovering from a setback.","I also like the fact that I can learn something from his story without becoming a professional athlete. When I'm struggling with a new skill, I sometimes expect results too quickly. Thinking about his comeback reminds me to be patient, work on the basics and give myself time. That's why I admire him as both a sportsman and an example of persistence."],"answer_word_count":228},{"name":"现场体育赛事：可独立朗读的完整事件模块","module":"A live sporting event I enjoyed was the men's final at the Dubai Duty Free Tennis Championships on the first of March, 2025. I went with a friend to the Dubai Duty Free Tennis Stadium. The match was between Stefanos Tsitsipas and Felix Auger-Aliassime, and Tsitsipas won six-three, six-three. Being in the crowd was exciting: I could hear the ball striking the rackets and feel everyone's reaction to each point. We talked about the match afterwards, and it made me want to attend another tennis event.","omit":"删除整篇Federer母稿，此段独立使用。比赛日期、人物、场馆、结果已核验；亲临、朋友同行、感官体验是样例，只用于真实到场经历的改写，不能录像冒充现场。可按真实经历继续展开购票、座位、最难忘一分和离场感受。","word_count":86,"answer_script":["A live sporting event I enjoyed was the men's final at the Dubai Duty Free Tennis Championships on the first of March, 2025. I went with a friend to the Dubai Duty Free Tennis Stadium. The match was between Stefanos Tsitsipas and Felix Auger-Aliassime, and Tsitsipas won six-three, six-three.","We arrived before the match and had time to find our seats and look around. I'd watched tennis at home before, but being there felt different. I could hear the ball striking the rackets, and the players seemed much faster when I saw them with my own eyes.","The crowd became quiet before each point, then reacted together when a rally ended. I found myself paying more attention than I normally would in front of a television. Even when I didn't fully understand a tactical decision, the tension was easy to feel.","Afterwards, my friend and I discussed the match on our way home. I enjoyed both the sport and the feeling of sharing an evening with so many other spectators. The result was part of the experience, but what I remember most is the atmosphere. It made me want to attend another tennis event."],"answer_word_count":194},{"masterId":"M13","name":"interesting_video","keywords":"Federer → Dartmouth 2024 → 练习 → 自然表达 → 英语","note":"观看时间、推荐人及感受均为样例。实际视频是Federer在Dartmouth的2024年毕业典礼演讲，不是采访，也没有称为短视频。官方核验：https://home.dartmouth.edu/news/2024/06/2024-commencement-address-roger-federer。","answer_script":["An interesting video I watched was a recording of Roger Federer's 2024 commencement speech at Dartmouth. A friend recommended it to me a few months ago. I knew him as a tennis player, so I was curious about what he would say to graduating students.","I watched it at home when I had some time in the evening. He shared lessons from tennis, but the part that stayed with me was the idea that a performance which looks effortless can actually require a great deal of work.","That caught my attention because I sometimes compare my own speaking with people who sound very confident. I notice the result, but I don't always think about the practice behind it. His explanation helped me look at that difference in a more useful way.","I also enjoyed the way he mixed personal experiences with a relaxed style. The video didn't feel like a list of instructions I had to memorise. I could understand the main idea and connect it with something I was trying to improve myself.","Afterwards, I thought about my English practice. Instead of expecting every answer to sound natural immediately, I felt more willing to repeat it and make small changes. I found the video interesting because advice from a different field could still be useful in my everyday life."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do people admire successful athletes?","a":"I think people admire both their achievements and the effort behind them. We usually see the final performance, but knowing how much training it required makes it more impressive. Their setbacks can also make their success feel relatable.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"人们为什么钦佩成功的运动员？"},{"q":"Is talent more important than hard work in sport?","a":"Talent certainly helps, especially at the highest level, but it needs to be developed. A gifted athlete still has to practise and learn from mistakes. I'd say talent creates an opportunity, while consistent work helps someone make use of it.","word_count":40,"q_zh":"在体育运动中，天赋比努力更重要吗？"},{"q":"How is watching sport in a stadium different from watching it at home?","a":"In a stadium, the atmosphere is much stronger because you share the experience with other spectators. At home, you get a clearer view and useful commentary. I enjoy both, but attending an event usually leaves a stronger memory.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"在体育场看比赛与在家看比赛有什么不同？"}],"verified_sources":[{"title":"ATP：Federer的20项大满贯冠军","url":"https://www.atptour.com/en/news/federer-retirement-grand-slams","supports":"职业生涯20项大满贯单打冠军。"},{"title":"ATP：Federer职业生涯回顾","url":"https://www.atptour.com/en/news/the-story-of-roger-federer","supports":"2016年后半程因膝伤缺席、2017年复出并夺澳网和温网。"},{"title":"ATP官方2017年新闻稿","url":"https://www.atptour.com/-/media/sites/atp-tour/press/press-releases/17-july-2017-federer-qualifies-nitto-atp-finals.pdf?hash=3A4EADC63241298599A3F20CA8E5B958&sc=0","supports":"2017年第八次温网冠军及2016年最后六个月休赛。"},{"title":"Dubai Duty Free Tennis Championships：2025男单决赛","url":"https://dubaidutyfreetennischampionships.com/third-time-lucky-as-stefanos-tsitsipas-defeats-auger-aliassime-to-finally-claim-title-at-dubai-duty-free-tennis-championships/","supports":"2025年3月1日、Dubai Duty Free Tennis Stadium、Tsitsipas以6-3和6-3击败Auger-Aliassime。个人到场经历并非来源事实。"},{"title":"Dartmouth · Federer的2024毕业典礼演讲","url":"https://home.dartmouth.edu/news/2024/06/2024-commencement-address-roger-federer"}],"word_count":206,"category":"人物","title_en":"Roger Federer and lessons from sport","audio":"audio/d53cb311ba010164.m4a"},{"id":"M14","title":"龟兔赛跑：动物故事、开心的阅读与童年学习","keywords":"动物故事 → 故事 → 书（故事集版本） → 开心的阅读经历 → 童年学到的事 → 坚持 → 喜欢的角色","usage_notes":["父亲讲故事、小学阅读、学骑车等个人经历均为样例。","仅问一个故事时用母稿；仅问一本书时用Aesop's Fables故事集版本，并对应自己真正读过的书或版本。龟兔赛跑本身是短寓言，不能无说明地当成长篇小说。","母稿把动物称为tortoise和hare；不要把野生动物题误当成文学角色题。"],"script":["An animal story I remember clearly is The Tortoise and the Hare. It's a short fable associated with Aesop, and I first heard it from my father when I was in primary school. Later, I read an illustrated version myself, which made me feel quite proud.","The story is about a race between two very different animals. The hare is fast and confident, while the tortoise moves slowly. Because the hare thinks winning will be easy, he stops for a nap. The tortoise keeps going and reaches the finish before him.","As a child, I found the ending funny and surprising. At the beginning, I was certain that the hare would win, so I wanted to turn the pages quickly. I also liked the pictures because they helped me understand what was happening without needing an adult to explain every sentence.","The lesson has stayed with me: steady effort matters, and being good at something doesn't mean you can stop trying. I think of it when I'm learning a skill and comparing myself with people who improve faster. The story reminds me to focus on my own progress. It's simple, but that's probably why I still remember it after so many years."],"variants":[{"name":"一本喜欢的书：替换第1段","module":"The book I'd like to describe is Aesop's Fables, an illustrated collection of short stories that I read when I was in primary school. I liked it because I could finish one story at a time and still have something to think about. The story I remember best is The Tortoise and the Hare, so I'll use that example to explain why the collection made such a strong impression on me.","omit":"删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留第2至4段。自己实际读过故事集才用这一版本，故事集名称可换真实版本。不能称龟兔赛跑为长篇小说。","word_count":71,"answer_script":["The book I'd like to describe is Aesop's Fables, an illustrated collection of short stories that I read when I was in primary school. I liked it because I could finish one story at a time and still have something to think about. The story I remember best is The Tortoise and the Hare, so I'll use that example to explain why the collection made such a strong impression on me.","The story is about a race between two very different animals. The hare is fast and confident, while the tortoise moves slowly. Because the hare thinks winning will be easy, he stops for a nap. The tortoise keeps going and reaches the finish before him.","As a child, I found the ending funny and surprising. At the beginning, I was certain that the hare would win, so I wanted to turn the pages quickly. I also liked the pictures because they helped me understand what was happening without needing an adult to explain every sentence.","The lesson has stayed with me: steady effort matters, and being good at something doesn't mean you can stop trying. I think of it when I'm learning a skill and comparing myself with people who improve faster. The story reminds me to focus on my own progress. It's simple, but that's probably why I still remember it after so many years."],"answer_word_count":227},{"name":"开心的阅读经历：替换第1段","module":"A reading experience that made me happy was finishing an illustrated version of The Tortoise and the Hare by myself in primary school. My father had told me the story before, but reading it without help felt different. I remember sitting beside him and explaining the ending in my own words. He listened patiently, and I felt that I was finally becoming a more independent reader.","omit":"删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留第2至4段。开心原因是独立阅读与分享；不是把听故事等同于自己阅读。","word_count":66,"answer_script":["A reading experience that made me happy was finishing an illustrated version of The Tortoise and the Hare by myself in primary school. My father had told me the story before, but reading it without help felt different. I remember sitting beside him and explaining the ending in my own words. He listened patiently, and I felt that I was finally becoming a more independent reader.","The story is about a race between two very different animals. The hare is fast and confident, while the tortoise moves slowly. Because the hare thinks winning will be easy, he stops for a nap. The tortoise keeps going and reaches the finish before him.","As a child, I found the ending funny and surprising. At the beginning, I was certain that the hare would win, so I wanted to turn the pages quickly. I also liked the pictures because they helped me understand what was happening without needing an adult to explain every sentence.","The lesson has stayed with me: steady effort matters, and being good at something doesn't mean you can stop trying. I think of it when I'm learning a skill and comparing myself with people who improve faster. The story reminds me to focus on my own progress. It's simple, but that's probably why I still remember it after so many years."],"answer_word_count":222},{"name":"童年学到的事：替换第4段","module":"I connected this lesson with learning to ride a bicycle. Some of my friends could already ride without help, while I kept losing my balance. My father reminded me of the tortoise, and we practised for a short time each evening. Eventually, I managed to ride down our street on my own. The story helped me understand that progress can be slow without being a failure.","omit":"删除母稿第4段，用此段结束；第1段开头可说A lesson I learned as a child was to keep practising instead of comparing myself with others. 骑车经历是样例。","word_count":66,"answer_script":["An important lesson I learned as a child was to keep practising instead of comparing myself with other people. My father helped me understand this when I was learning to ride a bicycle in primary school. At the time, I thought I was unusually slow at learning.","Some of my friends could already ride without help, while I kept losing my balance. I became frustrated and wanted to stop trying. My father reminded me of The Tortoise and the Hare, a story he'd told me before. In it, the slow tortoise keeps going and wins while the confident hare takes a nap.","The connection was simple: I didn't have to be the fastest learner to make progress. We practised for a short time each evening on a quiet part of our street. He stayed beside me, and I gradually became more comfortable balancing and turning.","Eventually, I managed to ride a short distance on my own. I was excited, but the bigger change was in how I understood learning. I realised that progress could be slow without being a failure. I still find that lesson useful when I'm studying something difficult or picking up a new skill. It helps me focus on small improvements rather than other people's results."],"answer_word_count":209}],"followups":[{"q":"Why are animal stories popular with children?","a":"Animals make stories easy to follow and give writers a simple way to show different personalities. A child can understand a confident hare or a patient tortoise without a long explanation. The pictures and unexpected endings also help.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"为什么动物故事受到孩子们的欢迎？"},{"q":"Should children's stories always teach a lesson?","a":"I don't think every story needs an obvious lesson. Some can simply be funny or imaginative. However, a lesson can be useful when it grows naturally out of the story, rather than sounding like an adult giving instructions.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"儿童故事是否都应该传达一个道理？"},{"q":"Is it better for parents to read to children or let them read alone?","a":"I think both are valuable at different stages. Reading together helps children enjoy books before they can understand everything themselves. As they gain confidence, reading alone gives them independence, while discussing a story afterwards keeps the experience social.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"父母读书给孩子听，还是让孩子自己阅读更好？"}],"verified_sources":[{"title":"Library of Congress：The Hare & the Tortoise","url":"https://read.gov/aesop/025.html","supports":"传统寓言角色、赛跑、野兔打盹、乌龟获胜的核心情节。"},{"title":"Penguin Random House：Aesop's Fables","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/831773/aesop-s-fables---classics-by-aesop/","supports":"Aesop's Fables是故事集，收录The Tortoise and the Hare等寓言；并非证明个人读过特定版本。"}],"word_count":202,"category":"事物","title_en":"The Tortoise and the Hare","audio":"audio/12f8d0647be493dd.m4a"},{"id":"M15","title":"规则分开讲：上海现有垃圾分类／希望UAE回收更便利","keywords":"现有法律 → 喜欢的规则 → 环保 → 希望引入的规则 → 所在国 → 城市改善","usage_notes":["主稿说的是中国上海已有的地方垃圾分类规则，2019年7月1日起实施；不代表中国所有地区都使用相同四分类体系。","访问上海、亲属厨房、垃圾桶、小贴纸等个人经历为样例。","题目若明确your country：只有在与自己的国别答案一致时才能说上海是中国的地方规则。题目明确所在国UAE时用未来规则版本；把UAE称为the country where I currently live，不自动称my home country。","未来版本是个人政策建议，不是已经实施的UAE法规，也不暗示UAE目前不存在回收措施。"],"script":["An existing rule I think is useful is Shanghai's household waste sorting rule. Shanghai is a city in China, and sorting household rubbish has been legally required there since the first of July, 2019. I'm talking about a local rule in Shanghai, rather than one identical rule for the whole country.","The system separates household waste into four categories: recyclables, hazardous waste, wet waste and dry waste. For example, food leftovers belong with wet waste, while materials that can be recycled should go into the appropriate recycling bin. Hazardous items need to be handled separately.","I became more aware of this rule during a visit to relatives in Shanghai. In their kitchen, they kept separate containers and checked the labels before throwing things away. At first, I found it a little confusing, especially when an item contained different materials. After a few days, though, the basic routine felt much easier.","I support the idea because it encourages people to think about what happens after they throw something away. However, I think clear signs and convenient collection points are essential. People are more likely to follow a rule when they understand it and can fit it into their daily routine. For me, good environmental rules need practical support as well as expectations."],"variants":[{"name":"希望在所在国引入的规则：完整替代稿","module":"A rule I'd like to see introduced more widely in the UAE, where I currently live, would require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear instructions. This is my suggestion for improving access, rather than a claim that the country has no recycling services. I'd want the rule to focus on making recycling easier for ordinary residents.\n\nFor example, each building could have an accessible collection area for paper, plastic bottles and metal cans. The signs could use simple pictures and several languages, so new residents would understand what belongs in each container. Building managers would also need to arrange regular collection.\n\nI started thinking about this while sorting packaging at home. Sometimes I have a few empty bottles or delivery boxes, and I want to deal with them properly without making a separate trip across the city. A reliable collection point close to home would make the routine much simpler.\n\nI'd prefer a gradual introduction, with clear guidance before penalties. If people misunderstand the system, helping them correct the mistake would be more useful than immediately punishing them.\n\nThe main reason I support this idea is that convenience affects behaviour. When the easier choice is also the environmentally responsible choice, more people are likely to follow it consistently.","omit":"删除整篇上海现有规则母稿，此版本独立朗读。使用would/could，不要改成UAE已经实施这一具体新规则。个人包装、出行体验为样例。","word_count":212,"answer_script":["A rule I'd like to see introduced more widely in the UAE, where I currently live, would require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear instructions. This is my suggestion for improving access, rather than a claim that the country has no recycling services. I'd want the rule to focus on making recycling easier for ordinary residents.","For example, each building could have an accessible collection area for paper, plastic bottles and metal cans. The signs could use simple pictures and several languages, so new residents would understand what belongs in each container. Building managers would also need to arrange regular collection.","I started thinking about this while sorting packaging at home. Sometimes I have a few empty bottles or delivery boxes, and I want to deal with them properly without making a separate trip across the city. A reliable collection point close to home would make the routine much simpler.","I'd prefer a gradual introduction, with clear guidance before penalties. If people misunderstand the system, helping them correct the mistake would be more useful than immediately punishing them.","The main reason I support this idea is that convenience affects behaviour. When the easier choice is also the environmentally responsible choice, more people are likely to follow it consistently."],"answer_word_count":212},{"name":"希望引入回收便利规则：独立短回答","module":"I'd like the UAE, where I currently live, to require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear signs. I don't mean that recycling services are absent; I'd like access to become more consistent. Residents could separate paper, bottles and cans without making a special journey. I'd introduce the rule gradually and explain the system before using penalties. For me, making a responsible choice convenient is more effective than simply telling people to behave better.","omit":"删除整篇上海现有规则母稿；此段可作简短回答，或先练未来规则的主线。完整Part 2用上面的整篇替代稿，不将两个国家的规则拼接。","word_count":77,"answer_script":["A rule I'd like to see introduced more widely in the UAE, where I currently live, would require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear instructions. This is my suggestion for improving access, rather than a claim that the country has no recycling services. I'd want the rule to focus on making recycling easier for ordinary residents.","For example, each building could have an accessible collection area for paper, plastic bottles and metal cans. The signs could use simple pictures and several languages, so new residents would understand what belongs in each container. Building managers would also need to arrange regular collection.","I started thinking about this while sorting packaging at home. Sometimes I have a few empty bottles or delivery boxes, and I want to deal with them properly without making a separate trip across the city. A reliable collection point close to home would make the routine much simpler.","I'd prefer a gradual introduction, with clear guidance before penalties. If people misunderstand the system, helping them correct the mistake would be more useful than immediately punishing them.","The main reason I support this idea is that convenience affects behaviour. When the easier choice is also the environmentally responsible choice, more people are likely to follow it consistently."],"answer_word_count":212},{"name":"中国的地方规则：明确国家范围开头","module":"A useful rule in China that I'd like to discuss is Shanghai's household waste sorting requirement. It applies in Shanghai, so I wouldn't describe its exact four-category system as a single rule followed everywhere in China. I learned more about it while visiting relatives there. What interested me was how a rule about an ordinary daily activity could encourage people to take more responsibility for their rubbish.","omit":"仅删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留第2至4段。your country必须与自己的实际国别表述一致。","word_count":67,"answer_script":["A useful rule in China that I'd like to discuss is Shanghai's household waste sorting requirement. It applies in Shanghai, so I wouldn't describe its exact four-category system as a single rule followed everywhere in China. I learned more about it while visiting relatives there. What interested me was how a rule about an ordinary daily activity could encourage people to take more responsibility for their rubbish.","The system separates household waste into four categories: recyclables, hazardous waste, wet waste and dry waste. For example, food leftovers belong with wet waste, while materials that can be recycled should go into the appropriate recycling bin. Hazardous items need to be handled separately.","I became more aware of this rule during a visit to relatives in Shanghai. In their kitchen, they kept separate containers and checked the labels before throwing things away. At first, I found it a little confusing, especially when an item contained different materials. After a few days, though, the basic routine felt much easier.","I support the idea because it encourages people to think about what happens after they throw something away. However, I think clear signs and convenient collection points are essential. People are more likely to follow a rule when they understand it and can fit it into their daily routine. For me, good environmental rules need practical support as well as expectations."],"answer_word_count":227},{"masterId":"M15","name":"proposed_home_country","answer_script":["A new rule I'd like to introduce more widely in China, my home country, would require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear instructions. Some places already have useful systems, but I'd like residents in more communities to have easy access to them. The focus would be on making recycling a simple part of everyday life.","For example, each building could have an accessible collection area for paper, plastic bottles and metal cans. The signs could use simple pictures and several languages, so new residents would understand what belongs in each container. Building managers would also need to arrange regular collection.","I started thinking about this while sorting packaging at home. Sometimes I have a few empty bottles or delivery boxes, and I want to deal with them properly without making a separate trip across the city. A reliable collection point close to home would make the routine much simpler.","I'd prefer a gradual introduction, with clear guidance before penalties. If people misunderstand the system, helping them correct the mistake would be more useful than immediately punishing them.","The main reason I support this idea is that convenience affects behaviour. When the easier choice is also the environmentally responsible choice, more people are likely to follow it consistently."],"keywords":"中国 → 住宅楼 → 分类指引 → 定期收集 → 方便居民","note":"本题用中国作为祖国样例，上海现有规则和全国推广建议分开讲。若选择UAE，需明确它是你现居的国家。","omit":"本题用中国作为祖国样例，上海现有规则和全国推广建议分开讲。若选择UAE，需明确它是你现居的国家。"}],"followups":[{"q":"Do environmental rules change people's habits?","a":"They can, especially when the required action is clear and convenient. A rule gives people a reason to start, but good facilities help them continue. Without practical support, some people may follow it only when someone is watching.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"环保规则会改变人们的习惯吗？"},{"q":"Should people be fined for failing to recycle?","a":"Fines may be appropriate for repeated, deliberate violations, but I'd begin with education. Someone who misunderstands a label needs guidance. Someone who keeps ignoring a clear rule may need a stronger consequence. The response should match the situation.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"人们没有按要求回收垃圾时，应该被罚款吗？"},{"q":"Who should take responsibility for reducing waste?","a":"I think the responsibility should be shared. Residents can sort their rubbish, businesses can reduce unnecessary packaging, and governments can organise reliable collection. Expecting only one group to solve the problem would leave important parts of the system unchanged.","word_count":39,"q_zh":"谁应该为减少垃圾承担责任？"}],"verified_sources":[{"title":"上海市政府英文网站：Guide to Sorting Garbage","url":"https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-Community/20231213/4d01af34ad254b83a60eafe4e9d95007.html","supports":"2019年7月1日起上海依法分类；四类及常见垃圾例子。"},{"title":"上海市政府英文网站：A guide to waste classification","url":"https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-ResidentChecklist/20231212/15dc5685586b44b3ad419639b102687c.html","supports":"现行公开指引列明recyclable、hazardous、wet、dry四类。UAE未来建议并非该来源事实。"}],"word_count":211,"category":"事物","title_en":"An existing waste rule and a proposed recycling rule","audio":"audio/8bdf5133802dd9e6.m4a"},{"id":"M16","title":"迪拜公共新闻：RTA新增公交线路与优化现有线路","keywords":"新闻 → 好消息 → 本地新闻 → 城市改善 → 公共交通 → 网上看到的信息 → 社区变化","usage_notes":["RTA新闻发布日期是2026年1月6日；正文写四条新增线路从2026年1月9日起实施。不要因标题含6th January而把实施日写成1月6日。","主稿的2026年9月看到新闻、朋友分享、个人选择公交等属于样例。新闻本身发生于2026年1月，不能说9月才推出这些线路。","RTA正文说超过70条额外内部线路获优化；改道、覆盖和高峰时段调整不等于每条公交都变快，也不保证用户实际通勤节省固定分钟。"],"script":["A piece of local news I found encouraging was about improvements to Dubai's bus network. I read an RTA announcement in September 2026 after a friend shared the link. The announcement itself was published on the sixth of January, so I was discovering an earlier development rather than reading about something launched that week.","According to the announcement, four new public bus routes were scheduled to start operating on the ninth of January. RTA also announced improvements to more than seventy existing internal routes, including changes to route coverage and services during busy periods. The aim was to make everyday travel more convenient.","This caught my attention because I live in Dubai and sometimes use public transport. I don't use every route mentioned, so I can't say that the changes directly shortened my own commute. Still, better connections could make buses a more practical option for people travelling between neighbourhoods.","After reading the article, I checked whether any of the routes were relevant to places I visit. I also sent the link back to my friend with a short comment saying that this was the kind of local news I liked: a practical improvement that could affect ordinary daily life. It made me feel positive about the city, and I would like to see the network continue to improve."],"variants":[{"name":"所在城市的积极变化：替换第1段","module":"A positive change in the city where I live is the improvement of Dubai's bus network. I learned about one specific set of changes through an RTA announcement that a friend shared with me in September 2026. The announcement was from January, and it described new routes and adjustments to existing services. I liked the fact that it focused on a practical part of city life that many residents depend on.","omit":"删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留第2至4段。明确是城市层面的改善，不声称某条线路就在自家门口。","word_count":71,"answer_script":["A positive change in the city where I live is the improvement of Dubai's bus network. I learned about it through an RTA announcement a friend shared in September 2026. The announcement was from January and described new routes and adjustments to existing services. I appreciated its focus on something useful to ordinary residents.","According to the announcement, four new public bus routes were scheduled to start operating on the ninth of January. RTA also announced improvements to more than seventy existing internal routes, including changes to route coverage and services during busy periods. The aim was to make everyday travel more convenient.","This caught my attention because I live in Dubai and sometimes use public transport. I don't use every route mentioned, so I can't say that the changes directly shortened my own commute. Still, better connections could make buses a more practical option for people travelling between neighbourhoods.","After reading the article, I checked whether any of the routes were relevant to places I visit. I also sent the link back to my friend with a short comment saying that this was the kind of local news I liked: a practical improvement that could affect ordinary daily life. It made me feel positive about the city, and I would like to see the network continue to improve."],"answer_word_count":219},{"name":"让你开心的新闻：替换第4段","module":"It made me happy because useful improvements don't always have to be dramatic. For someone who relies on buses, a better connection could make the journey to work or an appointment easier. I also liked being able to read the details from an official source rather than guessing from a short social media post. My reaction was positive, although I'd still need to check the route information before planning a journey.","omit":"删除母稿第4段，用此段结束；保留第1至3段。使用could表达潜在好处，避免把个人希望说成已经核实的效果。","word_count":71,"answer_script":["A piece of local news I found encouraging was about improvements to Dubai's bus network. I read an RTA announcement in September 2026 after a friend shared the link. The announcement itself was published on the sixth of January, so I was discovering an earlier development rather than reading about something launched that week.","According to the announcement, four new public bus routes were scheduled to start operating on the ninth of January. RTA also announced improvements to more than seventy existing internal routes, including changes to route coverage and services during busy periods. The aim was to make everyday travel more convenient.","This caught my attention because I live in Dubai and sometimes use public transport. I don't use every route mentioned, so I can't say that the changes directly shortened my own commute. Still, better connections could make buses a more practical option for people travelling between neighbourhoods.","It made me happy because useful improvements don't always have to be dramatic. For someone who relies on buses, a better connection could make the journey to work or an appointment easier. I also liked being able to read the details from an official source rather than guessing from a short social media post. My reaction was positive, although I'd still need to check the route information before planning a journey."],"answer_word_count":221},{"name":"从网上了解到的有用信息：替换第1段","module":"Some useful information I found online was an RTA announcement about changes to Dubai's bus services. A friend sent me the official link in September 2026, and I read it on my phone. It was a January announcement, so I checked the dates carefully. What made it useful was that it named a specific public transport development, rather than giving general advice about getting around the city.","omit":"删除母稿第1段，用此段开头；保留第2至4段。不要把1月发布的公告说成9月刚发生的新政策。","word_count":67,"answer_script":["Some useful information I found online was an RTA announcement about Dubai's bus services. A friend sent me the official link in September 2026, and I read it on my phone. It was a January announcement, so I checked the dates carefully. It named a specific transport development, which helped me understand the city's services.","According to the announcement, four new public bus routes were scheduled to start operating on the ninth of January. RTA also announced improvements to more than seventy existing internal routes, including changes to route coverage and services during busy periods. The aim was to make everyday travel more convenient.","This caught my attention because I live in Dubai and sometimes use public transport. I don't use every route mentioned, so I can't say that the changes directly shortened my own commute. Still, better connections could make buses a more practical option for people travelling between neighbourhoods.","After reading the article, I checked whether any of the routes were relevant to places I visit. I also sent the link back to my friend with a short comment saying that this was the kind of local news I liked: a practical improvement that could affect ordinary daily life. It made me feel positive about the city, and I would like to see the network continue to improve."],"answer_word_count":220}],"followups":[{"q":"Why is local news important?","a":"Local news helps people understand changes that may affect their daily lives, such as transport services or public facilities. National news can feel distant, while a local development may influence tomorrow's journey or a decision about where to spend time.","word_count":40,"q_zh":"本地新闻为什么重要？"},{"q":"How can people check whether news is reliable?","a":"I'd look at the original source, check the publication date and compare important details with another reliable report. A headline may leave out useful information. For public services, an official announcement is usually a good place to start.","word_count":38,"q_zh":"人们如何判断新闻是否可靠？"},{"q":"What makes people choose public transport?","a":"Reliability and convenience matter a lot. If a service goes where people need to travel and arrives predictably, it becomes easier to use regularly. Price also matters, but a cheap journey isn't very attractive if it requires several difficult transfers.","word_count":40,"q_zh":"什么会让人们选择公共交通？"}],"verified_sources":[{"title":"Dubai RTA：Launching 4 New Bus Routes and Upgrading 70","url":"https://www.rta.ae/wps/portal/rta/ae[LOCAL_PATH_REMOVED]","supports":"2026年1月6日发布；正文为四条新线路自1月9日起实施，并优化超过70条额外内部线路。"}],"word_count":219,"category":"经历","title_en":"News about Dubai's public transport","audio":"audio/f3235dd5a0184aa2.m4a"},{"id":"M17","title":"杭州西湖与再次游览杭州","keywords":"杭州 → 西湖 → 步道 → 朋友 → 重游","personalisation_note":"全部到访、朋友、吃饭、拍照及感受均为样例，待替换。杭州仅作为中国城市旅游例子，不代表用户家乡。未写湖泊排名、具体历史年代或未核实的历史故事。","script":["I'd like to describe West Lake in Hangzhou, a city in Zhejiang Province in eastern China. I visited it with a friend during a short holiday last year. We had a busy few weeks before the trip, so we wanted somewhere we could explore without rushing.","We spent an afternoon walking along the paths beside the lake. What I remember most is the space around the water. There were trees beside the path, and we could stop whenever we noticed a view we liked. I took a few photos, but I also put my phone away for part of the walk.","At one point, we sat down and watched the light change on the water. We talked about ordinary things and didn't feel that we had to keep moving to another attraction. Afterwards, we found somewhere nearby to have a simple meal.","For me, the lake is important because it gives people a place to enjoy being outdoors while visiting a city. I liked the balance between walking, looking around and having time to talk.","I'd happily go back, especially with someone who enjoys a slower kind of holiday. Next time, I'd leave more time to explore Hangzhou beyond the lake, rather than trying to fit everything into one afternoon."],"variants":[{"name":"国内重要湖泊","module":"The lake I'd choose is West Lake in Hangzhou, in eastern China. I visited it during a holiday and spent an afternoon walking beside the water. I remember the trees along the path and the changing light on the lake. To me, its importance comes from the experience it offers: people can walk, spend time together and enjoy an outdoor space within a city. I would describe what I actually saw rather than try to remember statistics about its size.","omit":"删掉将杭州称为家乡的任何句子；不用未经核实的最大、最古老、全国排名等说法。主体使用湖泊、水边步道及个人观察。","answer_script":["An important lake in China that I'd like to describe is West Lake in Hangzhou, in Zhejiang Province. I visited it with a friend during a short holiday last year. We had a busy few weeks before the trip, so we wanted somewhere we could explore without rushing.","We spent an afternoon walking along the paths beside the lake. What I remember most is the space around the water. There were trees beside the path, and we could stop whenever we noticed a view we liked. I took a few photos, but I also put my phone away for part of the walk.","At one point, we sat down and watched the light change on the water. We talked about ordinary things and didn't feel that we had to keep moving to another attraction. Afterwards, we found somewhere nearby to have a simple meal.","For me, the lake is important because it gives people a place to enjoy being outdoors while visiting a city. I liked the balance between walking, looking around and having time to talk.","I'd happily go back, especially with someone who enjoys walking and spending time outdoors. I'd leave enough time to enjoy the lake properly instead of trying to fit several activities into one afternoon. To me, that is what makes a place worth visiting."]},{"name":"想再次游览的城市","module":"A city I'd like to visit again is Hangzhou. I went there on a short holiday, and West Lake was the part I enjoyed most. However, I only had a little time to walk through nearby streets and try some food, so I felt I had seen only a small part of the city. On another trip, I'd stay longer, spend one morning by the lake and leave an afternoon free to explore a different neighbourhood. I prefer that to following a packed schedule.","omit":"首句主体改为整个城市；保留一次已去过的经历。删掉纯湖泊重要性结尾，加入其他街区、吃饭及第二次旅行安排。","answer_script":["A city I'd like to visit again is Hangzhou, in eastern China. I went there with a friend during a short holiday last year, but the trip felt too short. What I enjoyed most was being able to slow down and spend time outdoors.","We spent an afternoon walking beside West Lake. There were trees along the path, and we stopped several times to look at the water. We also sat down for a while and talked, without feeling that we had to move straight to another attraction.","Away from the lake, we walked through some nearby streets and found a place to eat. I enjoyed noticing ordinary parts of the city as well as the view by the water. However, we didn't have much time to explore further.","On a second visit, I'd stay for a few days. I'd leave one morning for the lake and spend another afternoon looking around a different neighbourhood. I'd also allow time for a meal with anyone I knew in the area.","I'd like to return because I already know one part I enjoy, but still feel curious about the rest. I prefer that kind of trip to a packed schedule where I spend most of the day checking what I need to do next."]},{"name":"将来想首次游览的城市：独立未去过版本","module":"A city I'd like to visit in the future is Hangzhou. I haven't been there yet, but photographs of West Lake have made me curious about it. I'd like to spend a few days there with a friend who enjoys walking. We could explore the paths beside the lake, try a local meal and leave time to look around the city. I'd choose a slower trip because I want to experience the place properly rather than just take a photograph and leave.","omit":"未去过的城市改用苏州，与杭州家乡及西湖游览经历保持一致。","answer_script":["A city I'd like to visit in the future is Suzhou, in eastern China. I haven't been there yet, but photographs of its canals have made me curious about it. I'd like to go with a friend who enjoys walking and a slower kind of holiday.","The place I'd most like to see is one of the canals. I'd spend a morning exploring the paths beside the water, stopping when we found somewhere pleasant to sit. I wouldn't want the whole visit to become a list of photographs I needed to take.","I'd also leave time to explore another part of the city. We could look around some streets, find somewhere to eat and choose one other activity according to what interested us. I'd rather make a realistic plan than try to see everything in a day.","Before booking, I'd check the weather, transport and accommodation costs. I would also look for recent practical information so that I understood how to get between the places we wanted to visit.","What attracts me is the possibility of combining a city visit with time by the water. I spend a lot of time indoors, so that balance sounds appealing. I'd hope to come home with a clearer impression of the place and a few memories shared with a friend."],"keywords":"苏州 → 尚未去过 → 运河 → 慢慢散步 → 将来计划"},{"name":"学习并喜爱历史的人：同行朋友Adam","module":"A person I know who enjoys learning history is my friend Adam. He reads short articles, watches documentaries and compares old photographs with the way a place looks today. During our trip to Hangzhou, he was curious about how people had used the lakeside in the past. He didn't pretend to know every answer. Instead, he wrote down a few questions to check later. What he enjoys most is understanding ordinary people's lives, rather than simply remembering dates or famous names.","omit":"主体是喜欢并学习历史的朋友，删去纯景点介绍。学习方法及行为均为人物经历样例；不把未核实的西湖历史当事实，不用我想了解历史代替他喜欢历史。","answer_script":["A person I know who enjoys learning history is my friend Adam. We became friends through work, and I noticed his interest during a short trip we took to Hangzhou last year. He was curious about more than taking photographs of the scenery.","When we walked beside West Lake, he wondered how people had used the lakeside in the past and how the area had changed. He didn't pretend to know every answer. Instead, he made a note of a few questions he wanted to check later.","He usually learns through short articles and documentaries. He also likes comparing old photographs with modern views, because that helps him notice details he might otherwise miss. If two sources give different information, he tries to understand the difference before repeating the story to someone else.","What he enjoys most is learning about ordinary people's lives. He has told me that history becomes more interesting when he can imagine how someone worked, travelled or spent time with their family. Dates matter to him, but they aren't his main interest.","I like talking to him because he asks questions in a patient, curious way. His interest has encouraged me to pay more attention to the background of places I visit, instead of looking at them only as attractive views."]},{"masterId":"M17","name":"hometown_public_space","answer_script":["A public place I like in my hometown is the area around West Lake in Hangzhou. When I am there, I enjoy walking along the paths beside the lake, especially when I want a break from a busy routine.","We spent an afternoon walking along the paths beside the lake. What I remember most is the space around the water. There were trees beside the path, and we could stop whenever we noticed a view we liked. I took a few photos, but I also put my phone away for part of the walk.","At one point, we sat down and watched the light change on the water. We talked about ordinary things and didn't feel that we had to keep moving to another attraction. Afterwards, we found somewhere nearby to have a simple meal.","For me, the lake is important because it gives people a place to enjoy being outdoors while visiting a city. I liked the balance between walking, looking around and having time to talk.","I'd happily go back, especially with someone who enjoys a slower kind of holiday. Next time, I'd leave more time to explore Hangzhou beyond the lake, rather than trying to fit everything into one afternoon."],"keywords":"杭州 → 西湖 → 湖边步道 → 和朋友散步 → 放松","note":"家乡暂以杭州作完整样例；请把整篇地点和经历改成你的真实家乡。","omit":"家乡暂以杭州作完整样例；请把整篇地点和经历改成你的真实家乡。"}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do people enjoy visiting lakes?","a":"I think lakes give people something peaceful to look at and space to walk around. People can spend time together without needing a complicated activity. However, the experience depends on the weather and how crowded the area is.","q_zh":"人们为什么喜欢去湖边游览？"},{"q":"Is it better to visit the same city again or explore somewhere new?","a":"Both can be enjoyable. A new city offers different experiences, while a second visit lets people explore more deeply and spend less time finding their way around. I would choose according to my budget and the purpose of the trip.","q_zh":"再次游览同一座城市，还是探索一个新地方更好？"},{"q":"How can cities protect popular outdoor places?","a":"They can provide bins, maintain paths and explain simple rules clearly. It also helps to manage busy areas so that visitors don't damage plants or disturb others. Protection works better when people understand why a place needs care.","q_zh":"城市如何保护受欢迎的户外场所？"}],"verified_sources":[{"title":"苏州市政府 · 运河资料","url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/szdtcyb/202411/066c4903706b4f6f934636a3e0bb2357.shtml"}],"category":"地点","title_en":"Hangzhou and West Lake","audio":"audio/d8d63a948d40e627.m4a"},{"id":"M18","title":"迪拜Sunset Beach：自然、安静与傍晚天空","keywords":"海边 → 散步 → 傍晚 → 天空 → 放松","personalisation_note":"全部到访、同行朋友、天空颜色和咖啡馆经历为样例，待替换。地点选官方旅游网站列出的Sunset Beach。咖啡馆用[Café NAME]待填真实店名，不虚构某家营业场所；安静仅描述那次到访，不保证该处始终安静。","script":["A natural place I enjoy visiting is Sunset Beach in Dubai. I went there with a friend one evening a few months ago, after a week when we had both spent too much time indoors. We wanted a short break without planning a whole day out.","We walked along the sand and then found a place to sit away from the busier part of the beach. It wasn't completely silent, but I could hear the waves more clearly than the conversations around us. There was a light breeze, which made sitting outside comfortable.","The most memorable part was the sky. At first, it was quite bright, but later the colours became softer. I noticed shades of orange near the horizon, with a little pink above them. We took a photograph, although it didn't quite capture what we could see.","For a while, we stopped talking and simply watched the water. I normally feel that I should be checking a message or finishing something, so it was pleasant to have no particular task.","I left feeling calmer. What I liked wasn't an expensive activity or a special event. It was the chance to slow down and pay attention to something outside my usual routine. I'd go back when I needed a similar break."],"variants":[{"name":"自然地点","module":"The natural place I'd choose is Sunset Beach in Dubai. What attracts me is the open view of the sea, the sound of the waves and the feeling of the sand under my feet. On my last visit, I walked for a while and then sat down to watch the water. I didn't need to buy anything or organise an activity. Although the beach is within the city, that visit gave me a welcome break from indoor spaces and screens.","omit":"主体保留海、水、沙、风及实际活动；压缩城市建筑和消费。不能把海滩说成山地、森林或湖泊。","answer_script":["A natural place I enjoy visiting is Sunset Beach in Dubai. I went there with a friend one evening a few months ago, after a week when we had both spent too much time indoors. We wanted a short break without planning a whole day out.","We walked along the sand and then found a place to sit away from the busier part of the beach. It wasn't completely silent, but I could hear the waves more clearly than the conversations around us. There was a light breeze, which made sitting outside comfortable.","The most memorable part was the sky. At first, it was quite bright, but later the colours became softer. I noticed shades of orange near the horizon, with a little pink above them. We took a photograph, although it didn't quite capture what we could see.","For a while, we stopped talking and simply watched the water. I normally feel that I should be checking a message or finishing something, so it was pleasant to have no particular task.","I left feeling calmer. What I liked wasn't an expensive activity or a special event. It was the chance to slow down and pay attention to something outside my usual routine. I'd go back when I needed a similar break."]},{"name":"靠近自然的咖啡馆","module":"A café close to nature that I'd choose is [CAFÉ NAME], near Sunset Beach. I went there after a walk with a friend and chose a seat where I could see the sea. I ordered a cold drink, and we stayed for about half an hour. What I liked was being able to enjoy the view while sitting comfortably. The conversation felt relaxed, and I didn't keep checking my phone. I'd return for the setting rather than for a particularly unusual menu.","omit":"先填实际去过、有对应视野的咖啡馆；本段经历为样例。主体改为店名、位置、饮料、座位、服务或环境；不能只讲海滩却声称回答咖啡馆。","answer_script":["A café close to nature that I'd like to describe is a small beachside cafe, near Sunset Beach in Dubai. I went there with a friend one evening after we had spent some time walking beside the sea. We wanted somewhere to sit and have a drink.","We chose a table where we could see the water. The view was the main reason I liked the place. I could notice the light changing outside while sitting comfortably, which felt different from spending another evening inside a shopping centre.","I ordered a cold drink, and we stayed for about half an hour. We talked about our week and a few things we hoped to do at the weekend. The conversation felt relaxed because neither of us was trying to get to another activity immediately.","I remember putting my phone away for most of the visit. There was enough to look at outside, and I didn't feel that I needed something else to keep me interested. The drink was pleasant, but it wasn't the most memorable part.","I'd go back for the setting and the chance to spend quiet time with a friend. For me, a café near nature can turn an ordinary break into something more refreshing, as long as it is comfortable and doesn't feel rushed."]},{"name":"观察天空的经历","module":"One time I paid close attention to the sky was during an evening visit to Sunset Beach. I was there with a friend, and we noticed the light becoming softer as the sun went down. There was orange near the horizon and a little pink above it. I took a photograph, but then put my phone away and watched for a few more minutes. I found the experience relaxing because the colours were changing slowly and there was no reason to rush.","omit":"主体是一次具体观察天空的经历；删除咖啡馆及城市游览。不能套成星空、日出或极光，除非另有真实对应经历。","answer_script":["One time I paid close attention to the sky was during an evening visit to Sunset Beach in Dubai. I was there with a friend a few months ago, after a week when we had both spent too much time indoors.","We walked along the sand and found somewhere to sit away from the busier area. At first, we were talking about work, but then we noticed the light beginning to change. We stopped our conversation for a while and looked towards the horizon.","The sky had been quite bright when we arrived. Later, there was orange near the horizon and a little pink above it. The colours were softer than before, and the water reflected some of the light. I liked noticing that change gradually rather than looking up only for a moment.","I took a photograph, but it didn't quite capture what I could see. So I put my phone away and watched for a few more minutes. My friend did the same, and neither of us felt that we needed to speak constantly.","I remember the experience because it was simple and relaxing. It made me realise how often I ignore my surroundings when I'm busy. I'd like to make more time for moments like that, even when I only have a short break."]},{"name":"安静或放松的地方","module":"A place where I felt relaxed was a quieter part of Sunset Beach. I went there in the evening and sat a little away from the busiest area. I could still hear people, but the sound of the waves stood out more. For a while, I wasn't talking or looking at my phone. I just watched the water and let my thoughts settle. I wouldn't describe every visit as quiet, but on that particular evening the setting helped me switch off.","omit":"安静指个人到访时的局部体验，不写从不拥挤、始终无人。若题卡要求自己家里的放松地点，改用M20独立模块。","answer_script":["A place where I felt relaxed was a quieter part of Sunset Beach in Dubai. I went there with a friend one evening a few months ago, after a busy week indoors. We wanted a short break without planning a whole day out.","We walked along the sand and then found a place to sit away from the busier part of the beach. It wasn't completely silent, but I could hear the waves more clearly than the conversations around us. There was a light breeze, which made sitting outside comfortable.","The most memorable part was the sky. At first, it was quite bright, but later the colours became softer. I noticed shades of orange near the horizon, with a little pink above them. We took a photograph, although it didn't quite capture what we could see.","For a while, we stopped talking and simply watched the water. I normally feel that I should be checking a message or finishing something, so it was pleasant to have no particular task.","I left feeling calmer. I wouldn't describe every visit to the beach as quiet, but on that particular evening the setting helped me switch off. I liked having no urgent task, and I'd return when I needed a similar break from my usual routine."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do some people prefer quiet places?","a":"Quiet places can make it easier to think or rest after a busy day. People don't need to compete with noise or constant activity. However, preferences differ, and some people feel more comfortable with a little background sound.","q_zh":"为什么有些人更喜欢安静的地方？"},{"q":"Why might people choose a café near the sea?","a":"The view can make an ordinary drink feel like a small break. People may also enjoy sitting somewhere different from their home or office. Still, a good location doesn't replace comfortable seats, reasonable prices and helpful service.","q_zh":"人们为什么可能会选择海边的咖啡馆？"},{"q":"Do people notice the sky as much as they used to?","a":"Some probably don't, because work and phones take up much of their attention. However, people still enjoy sunsets and often photograph them. I think noticing the sky depends more on someone's daily habits than on their age.","q_zh":"人们现在还像过去一样关注天空吗？"}],"verified_sources":["https://www.visitdubai.com/en/places-to-visit/sunset-beach","https://www.visitdubai.com/articles/best-places-for-views-of-burj-al-arab"],"category":"地点","title_en":"Sunset Beach and time close to nature","audio":"audio/fc14dbbc83758bef.m4a"},{"id":"M19","title":"公共建筑Mohammed Bin Rashid Library；高楼另用Burj Khalifa","keywords":"图书馆 → 书架形建筑 → 公共空间 → 阅读 → 哈利法塔","personalisation_note":"图书馆到访、读书、同行人及感受均为样例。官方核验事实：图书馆位于Dubai Creek旁，外形取意传统书托，共七层；哈利法塔位于迪拜，高828米。图书馆不作为高楼答案；哈利法塔模块仅描述从外部看到，没有冒称登塔。","script":["A public building I'd like to describe is Mohammed Bin Rashid Library in Dubai. It stands beside Dubai Creek, and its design is inspired by a traditional book rest. The library has seven levels, but what first caught my attention was its unusual shape rather than its height.","I visited it one afternoon after a friend suggested going somewhere different from our usual cafés. Before that visit, I had seen photographs of the building, but I wanted to understand what it was like to spend time there.","We looked around and then found somewhere to sit and read. I chose a book in English and spent some time working through a few pages. I didn't understand every word, but the setting helped me stay focused instead of moving between different things on my phone.","What I appreciated most was that the visit had a clear purpose without feeling rushed. I could read, notice the building and take a short break from work. It felt different from being in a shopping centre, where I often end up looking at things I don't need.","I'd recommend it to someone interested in books or architecture. For me, a useful public building offers more than an interesting photograph. It gives people somewhere to learn and spend their time well."],"variants":[{"name":"公共建筑","module":"The public building I'd choose is Mohammed Bin Rashid Library, beside Dubai Creek. I first noticed its shape in photographs, because the design is based on a traditional book rest. During my visit, I looked around and spent some time reading a book in English. What I liked was having somewhere to learn without the distractions I often have at home. I'd recommend it to a friend who enjoys reading or wants to see an unusual building with a practical purpose.","omit":"公共事实仅用已核验位置、外形与层数；删未经核实的免费、随时进入、开放时间及借书规定。","answer_script":["A public building I'd like to describe is Mohammed Bin Rashid Library in Dubai. It stands beside Dubai Creek, and its design is inspired by a traditional book rest. The library has seven levels, but what first caught my attention was its unusual shape rather than its height.","I visited it one afternoon after a friend suggested going somewhere different from our usual cafés. Before that visit, I had seen photographs of the building, but I wanted to understand what it was like to spend time there.","We looked around and then found somewhere to sit and read. I chose a book in English and spent some time working through a few pages. I didn't understand every word, but the setting helped me stay focused instead of moving between different things on my phone.","What I appreciated most was that the visit had a clear purpose without feeling rushed. I could read, notice the building and take a short break from work. It felt different from being in a shopping centre, where I often end up looking at things I don't need.","I'd recommend it to someone interested in books or architecture. For me, a useful public building offers more than an interesting photograph. It gives people somewhere to learn and spend their time well."]},{"name":"外形特别的一座建筑","module":"An unusual building I'd like to describe is Mohammed Bin Rashid Library in Dubai. Its design is inspired by a traditional book rest, which suits a place connected with reading. I liked that relationship between the appearance and the purpose. When I saw it in person, I spent a little time looking at the outside before going in. The visit reminded me that a building doesn't have to be extremely tall to be memorable. A clear idea in the design can be just as interesting.","omit":"不能把图书馆叫摩天楼；若题卡明确要求高建筑或高楼，整篇换用下面哈利法塔独立稿。","answer_script":["An unusual building I'd like to describe is Mohammed Bin Rashid Library in Dubai. It stands beside Dubai Creek, and its design is inspired by a traditional book rest. I first saw it in photographs and became curious about what it would look like in person.","I visited it one afternoon with a friend. Before going in, we spent a little time looking at the outside. What interested me was the relationship between its appearance and its purpose. A design connected with books seemed suitable for a place where people come to read and learn.","The library has seven levels, but its height wasn't what made it memorable to me. I liked being able to recognise a clear idea in the shape, rather than seeing another building that looked much like the ones around it.","Inside, we looked around and then found somewhere to sit. I spent some time reading a book in English, which gave the visit a practical purpose as well. It was more enjoyable than simply arriving, taking a photograph and leaving again.","I'd recommend the building to someone interested in architecture or reading. It reminded me that a public building can have an unusual appearance while still serving an ordinary, useful purpose. That combination is the reason it stayed in my mind."]},{"name":"高楼：Burj Khalifa独立完整稿","module":"A tall building I'd like to describe is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 metres high, and I saw it up close during an afternoon out with a friend. I had seen plenty of photographs before, but standing near it gave me a much stronger impression of its size. What I noticed first was how far I had to look up. From the ground, the upper part seemed very distant, and it was difficult to fit the whole building into one photograph. We walked around the nearby area and stopped at a place where we could see it more clearly. I haven't visited an observation deck inside it, so I can't describe that experience. What I'm describing is seeing it from outside. I enjoyed noticing how the appearance changed as we moved and looked from different angles. I don't usually take a strong interest in tall buildings, but this one made me curious about how such a large structure is designed and built. It stayed in my mind because the real experience felt different from seeing an image on a screen.","omit":"整篇替换图书馆主稿，不保留七层、书托、读书段。样例只说看到外部；如果题卡要求内部到访或登塔，必须改为真实符合条件的经历，不能把看到外部算成已经登塔。","answer_script":["A tall building I'd like to describe is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 metres high, and I saw it up close during an afternoon out with a friend. I had seen plenty of photographs before, but standing near it gave me a much stronger impression of its size.","What I noticed first was how far I had to look up. From the ground, the upper part seemed very distant, and it was difficult to fit the whole building into one photograph. We walked around the nearby area and stopped where we could see it more clearly.","I haven't visited an observation deck inside it, so I can't describe that experience. What I'm describing is seeing it from outside. I enjoyed noticing how the appearance changed as we moved and looked from different angles.","I don't usually take a strong interest in tall buildings, but this one made me curious about how such a large structure is designed and built. I'd like to learn a little more about that process before another visit.","It stayed in my mind because the real experience felt different from seeing an image on a screen. I'd like to go back at a different time of day to notice the light on its surface."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Are libraries still useful when people can read online?","a":"Yes, because a library provides a place to focus as well as reading materials. Some people also find it easier to learn away from home. Digital resources are useful, but they don't remove the need for shared study spaces.","q_zh":"人们可以在线阅读时，图书馆还有用吗？"},{"q":"What makes a public building successful?","a":"I think it needs to serve a clear purpose and be comfortable for the people who use it. An impressive appearance can attract attention, but access, maintenance and practical facilities matter more during an ordinary visit.","q_zh":"一座公共建筑具备什么特点才算成功？"},{"q":"Why are people interested in very tall buildings?","a":"Their size can create a strong impression, especially when people see them close up. Some visitors enjoy the views, while others are interested in engineering. However, height alone doesn't tell us whether a building is useful or pleasant inside.","q_zh":"人们为什么对很高的建筑感兴趣？"}],"verified_sources":["https://www.visitdubai.com/en/places-to-visit/mohammed-bin-rashid-library","https://www.visitdubai.com/en/articles/libraries-in-dubai","https://www.burjkhalifa.ae/img/fact-sheet.pdf","https://www.burjkhalifa.ae/the-tower/"],"category":"地点","title_en":"A public library and a separate tall-building example","audio":"audio/b6d6dc5e464ea6ee.m4a"},{"id":"M20","title":"祖母家、搬进公寓与自己家里的放松角落","keywords":"祖母 → 熟悉的家 → 探望 → 距离 → 自己的空间","personalisation_note":"祖母、房子、花园、距离、居住与搬家经历全部为样例，待替换。祖母家不是自己的现住处。杭州和迪拜均不自动当作用户家乡；家乡模块保留待填事实。","script":["A home I enjoy visiting is my grandmother's house. I used to go there quite often when I was younger, and I still associate it with spending unhurried time with my family. It isn't a large or modern place, but it feels familiar to me.","The room I remember best is the living room. There is a comfortable sofa, a small table and some family photographs. My grandmother also looks after a few plants near the house. When I visit, we usually have something to drink and talk about what has happened since we last saw each other.","On my last visit, I helped her with a small job and then stayed for lunch. Nothing especially exciting happened, but I enjoyed having time for an ordinary conversation. I didn't feel that I had to keep checking the time.","Although I like visiting, I wouldn't choose to live there permanently. It is too far from the places I need to reach for work, and I'd prefer having my own space and routine. As an adult, I moved into an apartment closer to work, which suited my daily life better.","So the house is special because of the person and memories connected with it. Enjoying a visit doesn't necessarily mean that it would be the right place for me to live."],"variants":[{"name":"搬家或改善生活的变化","module":"A change that made my daily life easier was moving into an apartment closer to work. Before moving, I spent too much time travelling, and I often got home feeling tired. I compared a few places and chose one that suited my budget and routine. On the first weekend, I unpacked the things I needed most and arranged a small place to read. The move involved some effort, but afterwards I had more time in the evening and felt more settled.","omit":"主体换为搬家前后，不再把祖母家作为现住处；通勤、费用及时间全部换成真实情况。","answer_script":["A change that made my daily life easier was moving into an apartment closer to work. It happened a while ago, when I realised that the time I spent travelling was affecting the rest of my day. I often got home feeling tired.","I compared a few places and tried to think beyond the first impression. The location mattered, but I also needed somewhere within my budget and with enough room for the things I used regularly. I didn't need a particularly large apartment.","Once I had chosen a place, I made a simple plan for moving. I packed the things I didn't use every day first and kept the important items together. A friend helped me carry a few things, which made the day less stressful.","On the first weekend, I unpacked what I needed most and arranged a small place to read. It took a little time before the apartment felt familiar, but I enjoyed deciding how to use the space.","The biggest improvement was having more time in the evening. I could prepare a meal, take a short walk or relax instead of feeling that the whole day had disappeared into work and travel. The move involved some effort, but it suited the routine I wanted to have."]},{"name":"自己家里放松的地方：独立完整模块","module":"The place where I like to relax at home is a small corner of my living room. I have a comfortable chair there, with a lamp and a little space beside it for a drink or a book. I usually sit there after work, once I've finished the things I need to do around the apartment. Sometimes I read a few pages, and sometimes I just sit quietly for a while. I try to keep my work laptop away from that corner, because otherwise a short break turns into checking messages. What I enjoy most is the feeling of having no urgent task. It isn't a large or beautifully decorated space, but it suits me. Even twenty minutes there can make the rest of my evening feel calmer.","omit":"整段独立描述自己的现住处，删除祖母、探望、不想居住和距离工作太远。房间、椅子、灯、活动均需个人化。","answer_script":["The place where I like to relax at home is a small corner of my living room. I have a comfortable chair there, with a lamp and a little space beside it for a drink or a book. It isn't a large or impressive area.","I usually sit there after work, once I've finished the things I need to do around the apartment. Sometimes I read a few pages, and sometimes I just sit quietly for a while. I like having an activity that doesn't involve another screen.","I try to keep my work laptop away from that corner. Otherwise, a short break can turn into checking messages and thinking about unfinished tasks. On some evenings, I also leave my phone in another room so that I can properly rest.","One weekend, I spent part of an afternoon there reading a novel. I wasn't following a schedule or trying to finish a certain number of pages. I simply enjoyed being comfortable and having enough time to stay with the story.","What I enjoy most is the feeling of having no urgent task. The space suits the way I relax, even though it is quite simple. Twenty quiet minutes there can make the rest of my evening feel calmer and more separate from work."]},{"name":"家乡：独立待填事实版本","module":"My hometown is [CITY], in [REGION]. I grew up there, so I know the area around my old home quite well. One place I remember especially clearly is [PLACE], where I used to [ACTIVITY] with [PERSON]. What I liked was [POSITIVE DETAIL], although [NEGATIVE DETAIL] could sometimes be inconvenient. I now live elsewhere, but I still miss [SPECIFIC THING]. When I go back, I'd like to spend some time walking through familiar streets and meeting people I know.","omit":"填实际城市及细节；不能直接把杭州旅游或迪拜海边稿作为家乡。若用户不是在那里长大，将I grew up there替换成真实生活阶段。","answer_script":["My hometown is [CITY], in [REGION]. I grew up there, so I know the area around my old home quite well. When I think about it, I usually remember ordinary places and familiar people rather than one famous attraction.","One place I remember especially clearly is [PLACE]. I used to go there with [PERSON] to [ACTIVITY]. What I liked most was [POSITIVE DETAIL]. Those visits were part of my usual life, so I didn't think of the place as especially important at the time.","I also miss [LOCAL FOOD OR OTHER SPECIFIC THING]. It reminds me of spending time with my family, and I would usually try to enjoy it during a visit. Small details like that can make a familiar place feel different from somewhere I am only passing through.","Of course, there are things I don't like as much. For example, [NEGATIVE DETAIL] could sometimes be inconvenient. I wouldn't say that living there was perfect, but my memories are mostly positive.","I now live elsewhere, so going back would give me a chance to notice what has changed. I'd like to walk through familiar streets and meet people I know. For me, the connection with my hometown comes mainly from the years I spent there and the experiences linked with it."]},{"name":"喜欢拜访但不想居住的别人家：祖母家","module":"A home I like to visit but wouldn't want to live in is my grandmother's house. I enjoy the familiar rooms, family photographs and the time we spend talking over a drink. However, it is too far from the places I need to reach for work, and living there would make my daily routine less convenient. I also prefer having my own space. So I would be happy to visit and stay for lunch, while continuing to live somewhere that suits my everyday needs.","omit":"明确祖母是房主，喜欢探望与不想永久居住是两个独立理由；不把她的房子称为自己的现住处。","answer_script":["A home I enjoy visiting but wouldn't want to live in is my grandmother's house. I used to go there quite often when I was younger, and I still associate it with spending unhurried time with my family. It isn't a large or modern place, but it feels familiar to me.","The room I remember best is the living room. There is a comfortable sofa, a small table and some family photographs. My grandmother also looks after a few plants near the house. When I visit, we usually have something to drink and talk about what has happened since we last saw each other.","On my last visit, I helped her with a small job and then stayed for lunch. Nothing especially exciting happened, but I enjoyed having time for an ordinary conversation. I didn't feel that I had to keep checking the time.","Although I like visiting, I wouldn't choose to live there permanently. It is too far from the places I need to reach for work, and I'd prefer having my own space and routine. As an adult, I moved into an apartment closer to work, which suited my daily life better.","So the house is special because of the person and memories connected with it. Enjoying a visit doesn't necessarily mean that it would be the right place for me to live."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do people enjoy visiting relatives' homes?","a":"The attraction is often the relationship rather than the building itself. People can share a meal, hear family news and feel connected with familiar memories. However, a pleasant visit doesn't mean that living together would suit everyone.","q_zh":"人们为什么喜欢去亲戚家做客？"},{"q":"What should people consider before moving home?","a":"They should think about the total cost, the journey to work and the kind of routine they want. It is also sensible to visit the area at different times, because noise and traffic can change during the day.","q_zh":"人们搬家前应该考虑什么？"},{"q":"Is a large home always more comfortable?","a":"Not necessarily. More space can help a family, but it also means more cleaning and possibly higher costs. A smaller home can be comfortable if the layout works well and people have enough room for their usual activities.","q_zh":"大房子一定住得更舒服吗？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"地点","title_en":"My grandmother's home and moving into my own flat","audio":"audio/ca45729b9079bf2a.m4a"},{"id":"M21","title":"学习英语的长期目标、表达课程与自信时刻","keywords":"英语 → 长期目标 → 录音 → 表达 → 自信","personalisation_note":"英语水平、每日练习、课程、工作表达及同事反馈全部是待替换的个人经历样例。课程版确有教师、授课及练习，不能把同事指导直接说成参加正式课程；没有保证考试分数或结果。","script":["A long-term goal I'd like to achieve is being able to use English comfortably in work and study. I understand a lot when I read, but I sometimes hesitate when explaining my own ideas. I want that gap to shrink.","This matters because good ideas are less useful if I can't communicate them clearly. I'd like to take part in discussions, ask questions when something is unclear and explain a problem without worrying much about finding the perfect words.","I've started with a simple routine. I choose a short question, record an answer and listen back. If a sentence is difficult to say, I try again with simpler language. I also read or listen to something useful and explain the main point in my own words.","Some days feel easier than others. I don't expect every recording to be better than the previous one, but I can notice small changes, such as pausing less or giving a clearer example. That helps me continue when progress feels slow.","I would consider the goal achieved when I can express what I mean and follow a conversation more confidently. It isn't about using impressive words all the time. For me, it is about being able to communicate naturally and take part more fully."],"variants":[{"name":"正式表达课程","module":"A course that impressed me was a short course on giving presentations. I took it because I needed to explain ideas at work more clearly. The teacher asked us to begin with one main message and support it with a simple example. We practised in small groups and received feedback. I realised that I was including details the audience didn't need. Afterwards, I used the method in a team presentation, and the discussion became easier because people understood my main point.","omit":"整个答案改为实际参加过的正式课程；明确教师、内容、练习、反馈和结果。删掉只有自学录音却声称上过课程的版本。","answer_script":["A course that impressed me was a short course on giving presentations. I took it a while ago because I often needed to explain ideas at work, but I found it difficult to decide what to include and what to leave out. It was held in a training room at my workplace in Dubai.","The teacher asked us to begin with one main message and support it with a simple example. That sounded easy, but during the first exercise I realised that I was adding details which didn't help the audience understand my point.","We practised in small groups and gave each other feedback. I tried again with fewer slides and a clearer order. The teacher also asked us to explain our ideas without reading whole sentences from the screen, which made the exercise feel more practical.","After the course, I used the method in a team presentation. I began with the problem and one example before explaining the details. People understood the idea more quickly, and their questions helped us have a useful discussion.","What impressed me most was the chance to practise rather than simply listen to advice. I left with a method I could use straight away. I still need preparation before a presentation, but I now have a clearer way to organise my thoughts."]},{"name":"为提高语言水平做过的具体行动","module":"One thing I did to improve my English was record myself answering a short question every day. I usually chose a topic connected with my daily life, so I could concentrate on explaining my meaning. After listening back, I noticed where I hesitated and tried again using simpler words. Sometimes I asked a friend whether my example was clear. The routine helped me move from recognising words when I read to using them while speaking, which was the part I needed to practise.","omit":"主体是一项已采取的具体语言学习行动，删掉纯未来目标和正式课程细节。练习频率、开始时间与反馈必须换成真实信息。","answer_script":["One thing I did to improve my English was start recording myself answering a short question each day. I began a few months ago because I realised that reading and listening alone weren't giving me enough practice in expressing my own ideas.","I usually chose a topic connected with my daily life, such as a recent outing or something I had learned at work. That meant I could concentrate on explaining my meaning instead of trying to invent an interesting story at the same time.","After recording, I listened back and noticed the places where I hesitated. Sometimes the problem was a word I couldn't remember. More often, I was trying to make a sentence too complicated. I then answered the same question again using simpler language.","Occasionally, I asked a friend whether my example was clear. I found that more useful than only asking whether the answer sounded good. If the meaning was difficult to follow, I changed the order or added one concrete detail.","The routine didn't solve everything, but it made speaking feel less unfamiliar. I could notice small improvements, and it was easy enough to continue on a busy day. I'd keep using it because it gives me practice and a clear way to check my progress."]},{"name":"感到有信心的时刻","module":"A moment when I felt confident was after explaining a new idea to my team in English. Before the meeting, I had practised with one clear example instead of trying to include every detail. During the discussion, people understood the main point and asked questions I could answer. I didn't speak perfectly, but I managed to explain what I meant. That experience made me feel more capable because I could see that useful communication mattered more than having an impressive sentence ready.","omit":"重点改为一次具体时刻、之前的担心、当时表现及为什么产生信心。删掉未来目标尚未实现与保证语言已完全熟练的说法。","answer_script":["A moment when I felt confident was after explaining a new idea to my team in English. It happened a few months ago, during a meeting about a small work project. Before the meeting, I was worried that I would lose my words or confuse people.","I prepared by choosing one main message and a simple example. I also practised saying it aloud, because an explanation that looks clear on a page can still be difficult to say. A colleague helped me notice where I was adding unnecessary details.","When the meeting started, I spoke a little more slowly than usual. I explained the problem first, then used the example to show how the idea could help. I didn't remember every sentence I had practised, but I could still get the main point across.","The change in my confidence came when people began asking useful questions. Their questions showed that they understood the idea, and I could answer without restarting my whole explanation. One colleague also said that the example had made things clearer.","I felt pleased because I had managed something I had been nervous about. The experience didn't mean that speaking English was suddenly easy, but it gave me evidence that preparation and clear language could help me communicate. Since then, I've felt more willing to speak up."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do people set long-term goals?","a":"A long-term goal can give everyday actions a clearer purpose. It helps people decide what to practise and what to spend time on. However, the goal needs smaller steps, otherwise it may feel too distant to influence daily choices.","q_zh":"人们为什么制定长期目标？"},{"q":"Is a formal course always better than learning alone?","a":"A course can provide structure and useful feedback, while learning alone offers more flexibility. The better choice depends on the skill and the person. I think combining independent practice with occasional guidance can be helpful when people have limited time.","q_zh":"上正规课程一定比自学更好吗？"},{"q":"How can people become more confident when speaking?","a":"They can practise manageable situations and gradually try more difficult ones. Clear feedback also helps, because it shows what already works and what needs attention. Confidence is easier to build when people can recognise progress through a specific experience.","q_zh":"人们如何在讲话时变得更自信？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"经历","title_en":"An English goal, a course and a confident moment","audio":"audio/9674c4841afbdbc3.m4a"},{"id":"M22","title":"有特殊意义的歌曲Happy Birthday to You","keywords":"熟悉旋律 → 生日晚餐 → 朋友 → 一起唱 → 个人意义","personalisation_note":"生日聚餐、共同唱歌、收到惊喜及个人听感均为样例，可与M08给朋友组织生日晚餐的版本共享。主人公是过生日的朋友，不是我自己生日；没有引用歌词，也没有分数保证。","script":["A song that has special meaning for me is Happy Birthday to You. It is a familiar song, but I associate it with being remembered and spending time with people I care about. The meaning comes from the occasions rather than a recording.","One evening that stands out was a birthday dinner we arranged for a friend. We had kept the plan simple and met at a place that was convenient for everyone. Towards the end of the meal, someone brought out a cake and we sang.","None of us was a particularly good singer, and we didn't all start at the same moment. However, that made the experience feel relaxed rather than embarrassing. Our friend looked surprised and then started smiling, which made me enjoy the song even more.","What I like about the tune is that it is easy to recognise and join in with. I don't need to concentrate on a complicated performance. I can simply take part and pay attention to the people around me.","I wouldn't put the song on when I'm working or travelling. Still, hearing it at a celebration brings back warm memories. For me, it shows how even a simple piece of music can become meaningful through the experiences connected with it."],"variants":[{"name":"一次听到这首歌的具体回忆","module":"A time I remember hearing this song was at a birthday dinner we organised for a friend. Near the end of the meal, someone brought out the cake and everyone began singing. We weren't all in tune, but our friend smiled and seemed pleased that we had remembered him. I liked the relaxed sound of our voices together. The memory is meaningful because the song helped turn an ordinary dinner into a shared moment, without needing a complicated performance or an expensive plan.","omit":"主体是听歌或共同唱歌的具体经历，不把大部分时间花在蛋糕外观和预订餐厅。朋友过生日与自己生日是不同版本，不混用he和I。","answer_script":["One time I remember hearing Happy Birthday to You was at a dinner we organised for a friend. It happened a few months ago, when a small group of us met after work. We wanted to mark his birthday without arranging a large event.","Near the end of the meal, someone brought out a cake and we began singing. I hadn't thought much about the song beforehand, but hearing all our voices together changed the atmosphere. The conversation stopped for a moment, and everyone's attention moved towards our friend.","We weren't all in tune, and a couple of people started slightly late. I found that quite funny. It sounded like a group of friends enjoying themselves rather than a performance where every detail needed to be right.","Our friend looked surprised and then started smiling. That reaction is the part I remember most clearly. The familiar tune gave everyone an easy way to take part, including people who were usually quieter during the conversation.","I left with a warm memory of the evening. The song wasn't unusual, but the people and the occasion made it special. It reminded me that music can help us express care in a simple way, even when nobody in the room has a particularly good singing voice."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why can a simple song have personal meaning?","a":"People connect music with the times and people around them. A simple song can bring back a strong memory if they heard it during an important occasion. The emotional connection may matter more than the complexity of the music.","q_zh":"为什么一首简单的歌也能对一个人有特殊意义？"},{"q":"Why do people sing together at celebrations?","a":"Singing gives people an easy shared activity and can change the atmosphere quickly. Even someone who doesn't know everyone can join in with a familiar tune. The purpose is usually participation and enjoyment rather than a perfect performance.","q_zh":"人们为什么在庆祝活动中一起唱歌？"},{"q":"Does everyone enjoy the same kind of music?","a":"No, because people's preferences develop through different experiences. Some enjoy calm music, while others want something energetic. Their choice can also change with the situation, so a person may enjoy one style while relaxing and another at a celebration.","q_zh":"所有人都喜欢同一种音乐吗？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"事物","title_en":"Happy Birthday to You","audio":"audio/e23efed32999cb3a.m4a"},{"id":"M23","title":"朋友画的Dubai Creek水彩画","keywords":"水彩画 → Dubai Creek → 小船 → 暖色 → 朋友礼物","personalisation_note":"朋友画画、赠送、画面、摆放地点及观画感受全部为可替换样例。作品没有冒称真实公共馆藏或知名艺术家作品；描述的是一幅想象的个人绘画，不把画面当Dubai Creek当天确有的公共事实。","script":["A piece of art I like is a watercolour painting of Dubai Creek that a friend gave me. He enjoys painting in his free time, and he made it after we spent an afternoon walking around the area.","The picture shows a boat on the water, with a row of buildings behind it. The walls are painted in warm, pale colours, while the water has different shades of blue. There are a few soft reflections, which make the scene feel calm rather than completely still.","What caught my attention was that it didn't include every detail. My friend had left out things that weren't important to the scene. That made it easier to notice the boat, the light and the relationship between the colours.","He gave it to me later as a gift. I put it near my desk, where I could see it without it taking up much space. I look at it after a busy day, and it reminds me of our walk and conversation.","I like it partly because of the picture itself, but also because someone I know took the time to make it. I wouldn't try to judge its financial value. For me, its value comes from the memory and the thought behind the gift."],"variants":[{"name":"收到的一件艺术品礼物","module":"An artistic gift I received was a small watercolour painting from a friend. It showed a boat on Dubai Creek and some buildings in warm colours behind it. We had walked around the area together, so the picture reminded me of an experience we shared. He gave it to me afterwards, and I put it near my desk. What made the gift special was that he had created it himself and chosen a scene with a personal meaning, instead of buying something without much thought.","omit":"明确我收到、朋友绘制并赠送。保留画面和个人意义，不说自己画的，也不把它说成买来的名画。","answer_script":["An artistic gift I received was a small watercolour painting from a friend. He enjoys painting in his free time and gave it to me after we had spent an afternoon exploring the area around Dubai Creek. I hadn't expected him to make something connected with that outing.","The painting shows a small boat on the water, with buildings behind it. He used warm, pale colours for the walls and several shades of blue for the water. The soft reflections make the picture feel calm, which matches the way I remember the quieter part of our walk.","I liked that he hadn't tried to include every small detail. Instead, he focused on the boat, the light and a few colours that worked well together. When I first looked at it, I noticed the overall feeling before examining the separate parts.","I put it near my desk, where I could see it regularly. It doesn't take up much space, but it gives that part of the room a more personal feeling. Sometimes it also reminds me to take a break from work.","What made the gift special was the time and thought behind it. My friend had chosen a scene linked with something we had done together. So I value it as both a picture I enjoy looking at and a reminder of our friendship."]}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do people enjoy looking at art?","a":"Art can give people something interesting to notice and a different way to think about familiar things. Some enjoy the colours or shapes, while others connect with the subject. People don't need to understand every detail to enjoy a picture.","q_zh":"人们为什么喜欢欣赏艺术作品？"},{"q":"Are handmade gifts more meaningful than bought gifts?","a":"They can be, because they show that someone spent time making something for another person. However, a bought gift can also be thoughtful if it suits the recipient. I think understanding the person matters more than the method.","q_zh":"手工制作的礼物比买来的礼物更有意义吗？"},{"q":"Should children have opportunities to make art?","a":"Yes, because making art lets them try ideas and express things in different ways. They can also learn patience through practice. The activity should allow exploration rather than making every child feel that the result has to be perfect.","q_zh":"孩子们应该有机会进行艺术创作吗？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"事物","title_en":"A watercolour of Dubai Creek","audio":"audio/1ae689715ef0e538.m4a"},{"id":"M24","title":"不喜欢的买菜短途、堵车、无聊等候室与耳机包裹","keywords":"买菜 → 短途 → 堵车 → 等待 → 耳机替换件","personalisation_note":"出行、驾驶、堵车时长、服务中心与包裹均为个人经历样例。包裹版本为店员确认故障后寄来耳机替换件，可与M06换货故事衔接；若M06已经写现场立即拿到新耳机，两种版本必须选其一，不同时背。没有虚构公告或公共事件。","script":["A short journey I don't enjoy is the drive from home to the supermarket when the roads are busy. I make it because I need to buy groceries, but it can take much longer than the distance would suggest.","One Saturday, I left at a busy time without thinking about the journey. I had things to do afterwards, so I assumed I could get the shopping finished quickly. Instead, the traffic moved slowly, and I spent much longer on the road than I had planned.","What bothered me most was the uncertainty. I could see that the supermarket wasn't very far away, but I couldn't tell how long it would take to reach it. I kept thinking about the other tasks waiting for me at home.","When I finally arrived, I still had to choose everything and pay, so the whole errand felt less simple than I had expected. Nothing serious happened. It was mainly a frustrating use of time for an ordinary task.","Since then, I've tried to go at a quieter time and prepare a list before leaving. That doesn't make the journey exciting, but it makes it easier to manage. I dislike it because a short, necessary trip can sometimes take up too much of my day."],"variants":[{"name":"一次长时间堵车","module":"One time I was stuck in traffic was on the way to the supermarket on a Saturday. I had left at a busy hour and expected a quick trip, but the cars moved very slowly. I spent about half an hour on a journey that was usually much shorter. I felt frustrated because I had other things to do afterwards. Once I arrived, I changed my plan for the afternoon, and since then I've tried to choose a quieter time for shopping.","omit":"讲一次过去事件并填实际堵车时长，不只讲经常坐的路线。驾驶者是我；不同时描述自己开车又自由看视频或玩手机。","answer_script":["One time I was stuck in traffic was on the way to the supermarket on a Saturday. I had left home at a busy hour and expected a quick journey, because the distance wasn't very long. I also had several other things planned for that afternoon.","After a few minutes, the cars began moving very slowly. I spent about half an hour on a journey that was usually much shorter. I couldn't see a clear reason for the delay, so I didn't know when the traffic would improve.","I was driving, which meant I needed to keep paying attention to the road. I tried to stay patient, but I kept thinking about the time I was losing. I was especially annoyed because I had assumed that buying a few groceries would be a simple errand.","When I reached the supermarket, I decided to change my plan for the rest of the afternoon. I bought the things I needed most and left the less urgent tasks for another day. That helped me stop feeling that everything had to happen at once.","The experience wasn't dangerous or dramatic, but it was frustrating. Since then, I've tried to go shopping at a quieter time and leave a little more room in my schedule. It reminded me that a short distance doesn't always mean a short journey."]},{"name":"无聊的服务中心等候室","module":"A place I found boring was the waiting room of a customer-service centre. I had gone there to update some account details, but I needed to wait for my number to be called. There were rows of chairs and a few information posters, with little else to do. I had expected a short visit and hadn't brought anything to read. After a while, I stopped checking the time and simply waited. The staff helped me eventually, but the waiting itself felt much longer than the task.","omit":"主体是一个具体地点和在那里等待的经历；删除买菜、自己驾驶、堵车。服务中心及事项是样例，不声称是某家真实机构的流程。","answer_script":["A place I found boring was the waiting room of a customer-service centre. I went there a while ago to update some account details, and I expected the visit to be fairly quick. However, I needed to wait for my number to be called.","The room had rows of chairs and a few information posters on the walls. There wasn't much to look at, and most people were sitting quietly. I found a seat and checked the papers I had brought, but that only took a few minutes.","After that, I kept looking at the time and the number being shown. I hadn't brought a book because I didn't expect to wait long. I tried reading the information posters, although most of it wasn't connected with the reason I was there.","What made the place boring was having very little to do while not knowing exactly how long I would be waiting. I couldn't simply leave, because I still needed to get the account issue sorted out. The visit took around forty minutes before someone could help me.","The staff dealt with the task once it was my turn, so I wouldn't describe the whole service as bad. It was mainly the waiting room experience that I disliked. Next time, I'd bring something to read and allow more time."]},{"name":"等待期待已久的耳机包裹","module":"Something I waited for was a package containing replacement headphones. My original pair had developed a fault, and the shop had agreed to send another pair after checking the problem. I needed them for listening practice and work, so I was eager for them to arrive. The delivery took longer than expected, and I checked the tracking information several times. I contacted the shop once for an update. When the package finally arrived, I tested the headphones and felt relieved that the problem was over.","omit":"主体是等待实物包裹；说明替换件、寄件人、等待时长和结果。删买菜及服务中心等候室；店员同意换货不等于当时已经现场拿到替换件。","answer_script":["Something I waited for was a package containing replacement headphones. My original pair had developed a fault, and the shop had agreed to send another pair after checking the problem. I used the headphones for listening practice and work, so I wanted them back quite quickly.","I expected the package by the end of that week, but it took about ten days to arrive. During the wait, I used an older pair which wasn't as comfortable. That wasn't a serious problem, but it reminded me of the replacement whenever I needed to listen to something.","At first, I checked the tracking information several times a day. However, seeing the same update didn't make the delivery any faster. I eventually contacted the shop once, asked for a clearer estimate and then tried to stop checking so often.","When the package arrived, I opened it and tested both sides of the headphones. I was pleased that they worked properly, and I could finally return to my usual listening routine. I also felt relieved that I didn't need another conversation about the fault.","What made the wait frustrating was not knowing exactly when it would end. The experience taught me that a useful update can matter almost as much as a quick delivery. It helped me manage my expectations and spend less time checking."]},{"masterId":"M24","name":"disliked_shop","answer_script":["A place I visit regularly but don't particularly like is the supermarket near my flat in Dubai. I go there about once a week to buy groceries. It's convenient, which is why I keep using it, but the experience is usually quite tiring.","I normally go after work, when quite a few other people have the same idea. The aisles can feel crowded, and there is often a queue at the checkout. I only need a few basic things, but finding them sometimes takes longer than I expect.","The layout is another reason I don't enjoy it. Items occasionally move to a different shelf, so I walk around looking for something I bought easily the previous week. There is also background music and a lot of activity, which makes it hard to relax after a busy day.","I remember one evening when I went in just to buy vegetables, bread and milk. I spent more time waiting to pay than choosing the food. By the time I got home, I felt that a small everyday task had taken up most of my evening.","I still shop there because it is nearby and the prices are reasonable. However, I try to go at quieter times and make a list before I leave. I don't dislike shopping in general; I just prefer an experience where I can find what I need and get home without too much waiting."],"keywords":"附近超市 → 每周买菜 → 拥挤与排队 → 花费时间 → 避开高峰","note":"常去的地点版与不喜欢的短途旅行版分别回答。","omit":"常去的地点版与不喜欢的短途旅行版分别回答。"}],"followups":[{"q":"Why do ordinary journeys sometimes feel stressful?","a":"People may expect a simple task to take very little time, so an unexpected delay disrupts the rest of their plans. Uncertainty can also be frustrating. Leaving a little extra time can help, although not everyone has that flexibility.","q_zh":"为什么普通的出行有时也会让人感到压力？"},{"q":"How can organisations make waiting less unpleasant?","a":"They can give a realistic estimate and explain what is happening. Clear updates help people decide how to use their time. Comfortable seating or something useful to read can also help, but information matters more when the delay is uncertain.","q_zh":"机构如何减轻等待时的不愉快感受？"},{"q":"Do people expect deliveries to be faster now?","a":"Many probably do, because they are used to seeing delivery estimates and tracking updates. However, speed isn't the only concern. A reliable estimate and clear communication can make a longer wait easier to accept than an unexplained delay.","q_zh":"人们现在对配送速度的要求更高了吗？"}],"verified_sources":[],"category":"经历","title_en":"A regular shopping trip, traffic and waiting","audio":"audio/6cf27fe3725a5c6a.m4a"}],"topics":[{"id":"T001","title":"一次让你满意的重要决定","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["I'd like to describe a decision I made while working on a small project with my team. We had a repetitive task that involved checking information manually, and I wanted to build a tool to make it easier.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"keywords":"重复工作 → 大方案 → 同事提议 → 小原型 → 测试成功 → 改变看法。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an important decision you were satisfied with.","audio":"audio/23b21937cd25ee34.m4a"},{"id":"T002","title":"认识的人做成一件难事","category":"人物","masterId":"M12","script":["I'd like to talk about my friend Alex, who runs a small coffee shop near a residential area. I met him through a mutual friend a few years ago. Since then, I've visited his shop fairly often, usually on a Saturday morning.","When he first opened it, the business was difficult. There weren't many customers in the morning, and some food was left unsold at the end of each day. Instead of immediately spending more money on advertising, he asked regular customers what they wanted and checked which items actually sold.","He reduced the menu to a few reliable choices, prepared smaller batches and introduced a simple breakfast combination. He also created a quiet corner where customers could read or work. Gradually, people started coming back. What I like most is the service: he remembers regular customers' orders and deals with problems politely. Once, my coffee arrived cold, and he replaced it without making the situation awkward.","I'm pleased to see his hard work paying off. I respect him because he looked at the actual problem instead of hoping it would disappear. The shop now has regular visitors, and his experience reminds me that success can come from a series of sensible improvements, rather than one dramatic idea."],"keywords":"small business → coffee shop → successful businessperson → organised person → happy person → customer service → solving difficulties","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone you know who achieved something difficult.","audio":"audio/384f2395ca4b0bad.m4a"},{"id":"T003","title":"性格乐观的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["A happy person I know is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and gradually became friends. He isn't excited all the time, but he usually seems comfortable with himself and finds something positive in an ordinary day.","He enjoys small things, like having a good conversation or helping someone finish a task. When a plan goes wrong, he tends to focus on what we can try next rather than complain about the whole situation. That makes it pleasant to work with him.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","I think he is a happy person because he doesn't expect everything to be perfect. He puts effort into things he can change and doesn't spend the whole day worrying about things he can't control. Being around him often improves my mood."],"keywords":"Adam → 进度不顺 → 冷静应对 → 小步骤 → 团队安心","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person who usually has a positive attitude.","audio":"audio/291d159131878e88.m4a"},{"id":"T004","title":"看过的名人采访","category":"经历","masterId":"M11","script":["I'd like to describe a YouTube interview with Huda Kattan that I watched one evening at home. It was published by ForbesWomen in April 2022 and was called 'Huda Kattan On Building The Next Billion-Dollar Brand'. She discussed her entrepreneurial journey and what making an impact in beauty meant to her. I found it interesting because the focus was on her ideas and business experience, rather than simply promoting a product.","I already knew that she was the founder of Huda Beauty, a company associated with Dubai, but I wanted to hear more about the person behind the brand. I watched the interview on my laptop at home, when I had enough time to follow it without rushing.","The subject that interested me was the experience of turning an idea into a business. I liked considering what success means beyond having a recognisable name. My reaction was that an interview can be useful when it helps you think about the decisions a person makes, rather than only their public image.","I don't work in the beauty industry, but I enjoy hearing how people approach a challenge in another field. It gives me a different perspective on my own work. I felt more curious about how founders balance creative ideas with responsibility, and I'd recommend this interview to a friend who's interested in starting a business."],"keywords":"Huda Kattan → ForbesWomen → 创业 → 观看采访 → 感受","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an interview with a famous person that you watched.","audio":"audio/99b4a231495d8e42.m4a"},{"id":"T005","title":"有条理的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["I'd like to talk about a colleague of mine called Adam. We met at work about two years ago, and we gradually became friends. He's a few years older than me, and he's someone I often turn to when I need advice.","What stands out about him is how organised he is. Before starting a task, he writes down the main steps and decides what needs to be done first. He doesn't make things complicated. In fact, he's usually the person who makes a confusing situation easier to understand.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Since then, I've tried to follow his approach. Whenever a task feels overwhelming, I break it into smaller steps. So he's had a positive influence on the way I work."],"keywords":"认识同事 → 做事有条理 → 我遇到困难 → 他教方法 → 我的变化。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person who organises things well.","audio":"audio/c00af183d1131772.m4a"},{"id":"T006","title":"嘈杂的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M03","script":["A noisy place I remember visiting is a busy market near Dubai Creek. I went there with a friend on a weekend afternoon. We wanted to explore the area, look at the small shops and see something different from our usual surroundings.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","The narrow paths were full of shoppers. I could hear sellers calling to customers, groups talking loudly and carts moving between the shops. The sounds overlapped, so my friend and I sometimes had to repeat ourselves. I found it lively at first, but after a while I wanted a break.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I enjoyed looking around, but I wouldn't want to spend the whole day there. The noise made it difficult to concentrate on a conversation. Moving to the quieter waterfront afterwards helped me appreciate the difference. So it was interesting to visit, even though it wasn't somewhere I could fully relax."],"keywords":"旧迪拜市场 → 喊价与人群 → 难以交谈 → 离开喧闹 → 仍有活力","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a place where there was a lot of noise.","audio":"audio/a6a6b8791db65725.m4a"},{"id":"T007","title":"城市里的自然空间","category":"地点","masterId":"M18","script":["A natural place I enjoy visiting is Sunset Beach in Dubai. I went there with a friend one evening a few months ago, after a week when we had both spent too much time indoors. We wanted a short break without planning a whole day out.","We walked along the sand and then found a place to sit away from the busier part of the beach. It wasn't completely silent, but I could hear the waves more clearly than the conversations around us. There was a light breeze, which made sitting outside comfortable.","The most memorable part was the sky. At first, it was quite bright, but later the colours became softer. I noticed shades of orange near the horizon, with a little pink above them. We took a photograph, although it didn't quite capture what we could see.","For a while, we stopped talking and simply watched the water. I normally feel that I should be checking a message or finishing something, so it was pleasant to have no particular task.","I left feeling calmer. What I liked wasn't an expensive activity or a special event. It was the chance to slow down and pay attention to something outside my usual routine. I'd go back when I needed a similar break."],"keywords":"海边 → 散步 → 傍晚 → 天空 → 放松","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a natural space in the city where you live.","audio":"audio/fc14dbbc83758bef.m4a"},{"id":"T008","title":"攒钱购买的东西","category":"事物","masterId":"M06","script":["I'd like to talk about a pair of headphones that I saved up to buy. I wanted them because I often needed to concentrate in places where there was background noise. I also thought they would be useful for listening to English recordings.","They were more expensive than the basic headphones I had used before, so I didn't buy them immediately. I compared a few options and put aside a little money each month. I also cut back on a few small purchases that I didn't really need.","When I finally bought them, I was pleased because I had made a deliberate choice rather than buying something on impulse. I started using them regularly for work and language practice.","A few weeks later, one side stopped working properly. I took them back to the shop, expecting a long argument. Instead, the assistant listened carefully, checked the problem and explained the next steps. After confirming the fault, the shop arranged a replacement.","That experience made the purchase more memorable. I appreciated both the product and the way the problem was handled. For me, the value wasn't just the price or the brand. It was having something useful and knowing that I could get help when it didn't work as expected."],"keywords":"需要专注 → 攒钱和比较 → 购买 → 出问题 → 店员换货 → 实际价值。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe something you saved up to buy.","audio":"audio/f06e3e348f714cbf.m4a"},{"id":"T009","title":"童年学会的实用技能","category":"经历","masterId":"M07","script":["I'd like to talk about my grandmother and a skill she taught me when I was a child. She enjoyed looking after plants, and whenever I visited her, I liked spending time in the small garden near her home.","When I was about ten, she helped me grow a plant of my own. At first, I thought I only needed to put it in the soil and water it as much as possible. She explained that plants needed the right amount of water and enough light, and that doing more wasn't always doing better.","We checked the plant together every few days. I was impatient because I wanted to see a result immediately. She encouraged me to notice small changes instead of expecting something dramatic overnight.","Eventually, I saw new leaves, and I felt surprisingly proud. It was a small achievement, but it was something I had helped create and look after myself.","What I admire about my grandmother is her patience. She didn't make me feel foolish when I made mistakes. She explained things calmly and let me try again. I still remember that experience because it taught me more than how to care for a plant. It also taught me to be consistent and to give things time."],"keywords":"童年去祖母家 → 种植物 → 我的失败 → 她教耐心 → 现在仍记得。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a useful skill you learned as a child.","audio":"audio/c3a8b306a2bcd931.m4a"},{"id":"T010","title":"喜欢拍照的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["A person I know who really enjoys photography is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and became friends. Outside work, he often takes photos of ordinary streets, small shops and interesting patterns in buildings.","He usually uses his phone rather than carrying a lot of equipment. What I like about his photos is that he notices details other people walk past. He might photograph the reflection in a window or the shadow of a tree instead of a famous landmark.","Last month, we went for a walk near Dubai Creek. I took a quick photo and thought the scene looked rather ordinary. Adam suggested moving a few steps to the side and waiting until fewer people were in the picture. The result looked much clearer.","He also explained that good light matters more than simply having an expensive camera. I enjoyed learning something practical without having to study a long list of technical terms. We compared our pictures afterwards and talked about why they looked different.","I appreciate his hobby because it encourages him to pay attention to his surroundings. His example has made me look more carefully when I go for a walk. I still don't take photos as seriously as he does, but I understand why he enjoys it."],"keywords":"Adam → 旧迪拜 → 拍照 → 留意细节 → 分享照片","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who enjoys taking photographs.","audio":"audio/9ea7e40b9f0b0490.m4a"},{"id":"T011","title":"你钦佩的长辈","category":"人物","masterId":"M07","script":["I'd like to talk about my grandmother and a skill she taught me when I was a child. She enjoyed looking after plants, and whenever I visited her, I liked spending time in the small garden near her home.","When I was about ten, she helped me grow a plant of my own. At first, I thought I only needed to put it in the soil and water it as much as possible. She explained that plants needed the right amount of water and enough light, and that doing more wasn't always doing better.","We checked the plant together every few days. I was impatient because I wanted to see a result immediately. She encouraged me to notice small changes instead of expecting something dramatic overnight.","Eventually, I saw new leaves, and I felt surprisingly proud. It was a small achievement, but it was something I had helped create and look after myself.","What I admire about my grandmother is her patience. She didn't make me feel foolish when I made mistakes. She explained things calmly and let me try again. I still remember that experience because it taught me more than how to care for a plant. It also taught me to be consistent and to give things time."],"keywords":"童年去祖母家 → 种植物 → 我的失败 → 她教耐心 → 现在仍记得。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an older person you admire.","audio":"audio/c3a8b306a2bcd931.m4a"},{"id":"T012","title":"认真听不感兴趣的话题","category":"经历","masterId":"M07","script":["A time I listened to something I wasn't initially interested in was when my grandmother explained how she looked after her plants. I visited her one afternoon, and she was excited to show me a plant that had produced new leaves.","At first, I didn't really care about the details. I thought she would point out the plant quickly, but she began explaining the light, watering and changes she had noticed over several weeks. I was tempted to change the subject.","I kept listening because I knew the hobby mattered to her. She had put time and effort into it, and I didn't want to make her feel that her excitement was unimportant. I put my phone away and asked a couple of simple questions.","As the conversation continued, I became more interested. I could see that she enjoyed noticing small changes and solving practical problems. I also learned why giving a plant too much attention could sometimes be less helpful than being patient.","I felt glad that I had listened properly. The conversation made her happy and helped me understand her hobby rather than just see it as a collection of pots. It reminded me that showing interest in another person's experience can matter even when the subject isn't one of my favourites."],"keywords":"祖母 → 植物话题 → 起初不感兴趣 → 认真听 → 理解","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you listened carefully to a topic you did not find interesting.","audio":"audio/ad68db0de23746f6.m4a"},{"id":"T013","title":"在商店获得的好服务","category":"经历","masterId":"M06","script":["The good service I'd like to describe was the help I received in a shop when my headphones stopped working. I had bought them a few weeks earlier after saving up. Because I used them often, I was disappointed when one side began to fail.","I brought the headphones and the proof of purchase back to the shop. The assistant asked me to explain what had happened and listened without interrupting. He then checked the problem instead of immediately suggesting that I had caused it.","He explained the next steps in language I could understand and told me what information the shop needed. After confirming the fault, the staff arranged a replacement. I appreciated knowing what was happening, rather than being passed from one person to another.","The assistant also gave me time to ask questions and check the replacement. I had expected the visit to be stressful, but it was straightforward. The most helpful part was his calm attitude, which made me feel that the problem was being taken seriously.","That experience made the purchase more memorable. I appreciated both the product and the way the problem was handled. For me, the value wasn't just the price or the brand. It was having something useful and knowing that I could get help when it didn't work as expected."],"keywords":"耳机问题 → 店员倾听 → 检查 → 解释更换 → 放心","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe good service you received in a shop.","audio":"audio/421068e5a892b42f.m4a"},{"id":"T014","title":"手工做东西的技能","category":"经历","masterId":"M07","script":["A person I know who is good at making things by hand is my grandmother. When I was a child, I often visited her home and watched her repair clothes or make small useful items. She enjoyed the process and didn't rush through it.","One summer, when I was about ten, she helped me make a simple cloth bag. We chose some spare material and decided on a size that I could use for a few books. She showed me how to measure it and join the pieces carefully.","My first attempt was uneven, and I wanted to start again. She explained that we could undo one small section and fix it instead. That made the task feel less intimidating. I slowly began to understand that a mistake didn't mean the whole item was ruined.","When we finished, the bag wasn't perfect, but it was useful. I felt proud that I had helped make something rather than just buy it. I used it afterwards, which made the experience more memorable.","I admire her patience and practical skills. She could turn simple materials into something that solved a small everyday problem. I don't make many things by hand now, but the lesson has stayed with me: work carefully, notice mistakes and improve one part at a time."],"keywords":"祖母 → 纸板盒 → 手工收纳 → 剪裁粘贴 → 耐心","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a skill for making something by hand.","audio":"audio/67c06156d6567dfc.m4a"},{"id":"T015","title":"和朋友度过的愉快夜晚","category":"经历","masterId":"M03","script":["One enjoyable evening was when a friend and I explored an older part of Dubai and then sat down for a drink near the creek. It happened on a weekend a few months ago. Neither of us wanted a big event; we just wanted time to talk.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","As it became darker, the area felt calmer. We walked past the shops, took a few photos and then chose somewhere comfortable to sit. We talked about things that had happened that week, shared a few funny stories and stopped checking our phones for a while.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"keywords":"Adam → 旧迪拜 → 散步晚餐 → 轻松交谈 → 好心情","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an enjoyable evening you spent with friends.","audio":"audio/ea69a9a36c035b24.m4a"},{"id":"T016","title":"浪费时间的活动","category":"经历","masterId":"M05","script":["An activity I regularly do that I consider a waste of time is scrolling through short posts on my phone. It often happens after work. I tell myself that I'll look for a few minutes, but the activity can take up much more of the evening than I intended.","The problem was that I didn't feel rested afterwards. I was still tired, and sometimes I went to bed later than I had planned. So I decided to replace part of that screen time with a short walk.","I started with just ten minutes because I knew I wouldn't stick to an ambitious exercise plan. When the weather was comfortable, I walked outside. On other days, I found somewhere indoors where I could move around. I usually left my phone in my pocket and paid attention to my surroundings.","After a while, a friend began joining me. That made the habit easier to maintain because we could chat and remind each other to go. We weren't trying to become athletes. We just wanted to do something more active after sitting for most of the day.","I consider it a waste of time because I usually haven't chosen a clear purpose and I remember very little afterwards. A few useful posts do appear, but they don't justify all the time I spend. I'm trying to keep a limit and choose a more deliberate way to relax."],"keywords":"短视频 → 不知不觉 → 影响休息 → 放远手机 → 散步","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an activity that you think wastes time.","audio":"audio/d3f733a06385b4a0.m4a"},{"id":"T017","title":"拥挤的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M03","script":["A crowded place I've visited is a market near Dubai Creek. I went there with a friend on a weekend afternoon. We wanted to explore the small shops and take a few photos, but there were more people than we had expected.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","At some points, the path was so busy that we had to wait before moving forward. People stopped to look at products while others tried to pass them. I kept my bag close and paid attention to where my friend was, because it would have been easy to lose each other.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","The crowd gave the market an energetic atmosphere, but it also made simple things take longer. I was glad we eventually found a quiet place to sit. If I go again, I'll choose a less busy time so that I can enjoy the shops without constantly moving around other people."],"keywords":"市场 → 周末 → 人群 → 放慢脚步 → 选择安静路线","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a crowded place you visited.","audio":"audio/38e6c6601b3533d8.m4a"},{"id":"T018","title":"喜欢学历史的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M09","script":["I'd like to talk about Ben, a childhood friend who learns about history in his free time. We grew up in the same neighbourhood, and we still talk regularly. His interest has made me look at familiar places differently.","His interest started with a box of his grandfather's old photographs. Ben wanted to know who the people were and why the streets looked different. He asked his grandfather about them and put the pictures in an album with short descriptions. It became a record of his family's life as well as the town's history.","When we visited a local museum, he showed me an old railway map and explained how trains had helped the town develop. He didn't just repeat dates from the labels. He connected the railway with local shops, jobs and travel, which made the explanation easy to follow.","He also takes photographs of interesting museum displays and looks up unfamiliar details afterwards. I used to think history was mostly about remembering facts for school, but his enthusiasm changed my mind. Through him, I've realised that it can explain ordinary places and help us understand how people lived before us."],"keywords":"childhood friend → good at learning languages → English and Chinese → history lover → old photographs → museum","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person who enjoys learning about history.","audio":"audio/69eaa4d2fc6a999d.m4a"},{"id":"T019","title":"教你新技能的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["The person I'd like to describe is my colleague Adam, who taught me how to present a complicated idea clearly. We met at work about two years ago, and he is a few years older than me. Before he helped me, I often included too many details when explaining something.","What stands out about him is how organised he is. Before starting a task, he writes down the main steps and decides what needs to be done first. He doesn't make things complicated. In fact, he's usually the person who makes a confusing situation easier to understand.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Since then, I've tried to follow his approach. Whenever a task feels overwhelming, I break it into smaller steps. So he's had a positive influence on the way I work."],"keywords":"Adam → 表达混乱 → 主旨加例子 → 练习 → 清楚沟通","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who taught you a new skill.","audio":"audio/5600ea75015f8bef.m4a"},{"id":"T020","title":"让你失望的电影","category":"事物","masterId":"M02","script":["The film I'd choose is The Martian. I watched it at home a few months ago after reading the novel by Andy Weir. Because I had enjoyed the book, I expected the film to give me the same sense of involvement, but some parts disappointed me.","The story follows an astronaut called Mark Watney who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to work out how to survive and contact Earth. The main idea is interesting, and I liked the fact that science and practical thinking were important to the story.","My disappointment was mainly about the pace of the problem-solving. In the book, I could spend time following his thoughts and understanding why a particular solution might work. In the film, some of those steps felt rushed, so I was less involved in the decisions.","The visuals were impressive, and the acting was enjoyable, but I sometimes felt that a difficult problem had been solved before I fully understood it. I watched it with a friend, and we discussed that difference afterwards.","I wouldn't describe it as a terrible film. My expectations were simply too closely connected to the book. I learned that an adaptation can tell the same story while creating a different experience. If I watched it again, I'd probably judge it more on its own terms."],"keywords":"The Martian电影 → 读过原著 → 期待细节 → 节奏更快 → 个人失望","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a film that disappointed you.","audio":"audio/3082418a5f20caa8.m4a"},{"id":"T021","title":"经常走但不喜欢的短途","category":"经历","masterId":"M24","script":["A short journey I don't enjoy is the drive from home to the supermarket when the roads are busy. I make it because I need to buy groceries, but it can take much longer than the distance would suggest.","One Saturday, I left at a busy time without thinking about the journey. I had things to do afterwards, so I assumed I could get the shopping finished quickly. Instead, the traffic moved slowly, and I spent much longer on the road than I had planned.","What bothered me most was the uncertainty. I could see that the supermarket wasn't very far away, but I couldn't tell how long it would take to reach it. I kept thinking about the other tasks waiting for me at home.","When I finally arrived, I still had to choose everything and pay, so the whole errand felt less simple than I had expected. Nothing serious happened. It was mainly a frustrating use of time for an ordinary task.","Since then, I've tried to go at a quieter time and prepare a list before leaving. That doesn't make the journey exciting, but it makes it easier to manage. I dislike it because a short, necessary trip can sometimes take up too much of my day."],"keywords":"买菜 → 短途 → 堵车 → 等待 → 耳机替换件","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a short journey you often make but do not enjoy.","audio":"audio/6cf27fe3725a5c6a.m4a"},{"id":"T022","title":"受欢迎的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["A popular person I know is my colleague Adam. We met at work about two years ago and gradually became friends. Many people in our team enjoy working with him because he is approachable and takes other people's questions seriously.","He remembers small things about people and is willing to help without making a big show of it. For example, if someone is new to the team, he explains the basic information and checks whether they are comfortable asking questions. That makes people feel included.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","I think he is popular because people feel respected around him. He doesn't need to dominate a conversation or impress everyone. His friendliness and willingness to help are enough. I enjoy his company for the same reasons, and I try to learn from the way he treats others."],"keywords":"Adam → 耐心 → 愿意帮忙 → 清楚解释 → 大家信任","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person who is popular with others.","audio":"audio/7d30cb63ef8cacda.m4a"},{"id":"T023","title":"你钦佩的运动员","category":"人物","masterId":"M13","script":["I'd like to talk about Roger Federer, the retired Swiss tennis player. I first became interested in him when I watched some of his matches on television as a student. I didn't understand every rule, but I could tell that his movement and timing were special.","He finished his career with twenty Grand Slam singles titles, including eight Wimbledon titles. What I admire most, though, is the way he makes a difficult sport look natural. His movements seem smooth, and watching him has made me appreciate the importance of technique.","One part of his career that really impressed me was his return after injury. He missed the second half of the 2016 season because of a knee problem. Then, in 2017, he came back and won both the Australian Open and Wimbledon. To me, that is a powerful example of recovering from a setback.","I also like the fact that I can learn something from his story without becoming a professional athlete. When I'm struggling with a new skill, I sometimes expect results too quickly. Thinking about his comeback reminds me to be patient, work on the basics and give myself time. That's why I admire him as both a sportsman and an example of persistence."],"keywords":"运动员 → 钦佩的人 → 克服困难 → 成功人士 → 想见的人 → 现场体育赛事（独立版本）","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a sports player you admire.","audio":"audio/d53cb311ba010164.m4a"},{"id":"T024","title":"帮助别人改善健康习惯","category":"经历","masterId":"M05","script":["A person whose fitness I helped improve is a friend called Sam. Like me, he spent most of his working day sitting down. He wanted to be more active, but he found it difficult to start an exercise routine that he could continue.","A few months ago, I suggested that we begin with a short walk after work. I didn't give him complicated fitness advice. I simply thought doing something together would make the first step easier. We agreed to try ten minutes rather than set an ambitious target.","When the weather was comfortable, we walked outside. Otherwise, we found somewhere suitable indoors. I checked in with him before the walk and tried to make the plan convenient. On days when one of us felt tired, we still did a shorter version instead of cancelling everything.","After a few weeks, he said the routine had become easier to maintain. He also enjoyed having a break between work and the rest of the evening. I can't claim that it transformed his health, but it did help him spend more time moving regularly.","The hardest part was getting started and keeping the plan simple. I'm pleased that I could support him without putting pressure on him. Helping with a small habit was more practical than telling him to make a huge change overnight."],"keywords":"Sam → 久坐 → 我邀请散步 → 坚持 → 日常改善","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you helped someone develop healthier habits.","audio":"audio/3a33caf871504f9c.m4a"},{"id":"T025","title":"一座高楼","category":"地点","masterId":"M19","script":["A tall building I'd like to describe is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 metres high, and I saw it up close during an afternoon out with a friend. I had seen plenty of photographs before, but standing near it gave me a much stronger impression of its size.","What I noticed first was how far I had to look up. From the ground, the upper part seemed very distant, and it was difficult to fit the whole building into one photograph. We walked around the nearby area and stopped where we could see it more clearly.","I haven't visited an observation deck inside it, so I can't describe that experience. What I'm describing is seeing it from outside. I enjoyed noticing how the appearance changed as we moved and looked from different angles.","I don't usually take a strong interest in tall buildings, but this one made me curious about how such a large structure is designed and built. I'd like to learn a little more about that process before another visit.","It stayed in my mind because the real experience felt different from seeing an image on a screen. I'd like to go back at a different time of day to notice the light on its surface."],"keywords":"Burj Khalifa → Dubai → 高楼外观 → 观察 → 印象","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a tall building that impressed you.","audio":"audio/518ac28610b21497.m4a"},{"id":"T026","title":"看过的有趣视频","category":"事物","masterId":"M13","script":["An interesting video I watched was a recording of Roger Federer's 2024 commencement speech at Dartmouth. A friend recommended it to me a few months ago. I knew him as a tennis player, so I was curious about what he would say to graduating students.","I watched it at home when I had some time in the evening. He shared lessons from tennis, but the part that stayed with me was the idea that a performance which looks effortless can actually require a great deal of work.","That caught my attention because I sometimes compare my own speaking with people who sound very confident. I notice the result, but I don't always think about the practice behind it. His explanation helped me look at that difference in a more useful way.","I also enjoyed the way he mixed personal experiences with a relaxed style. The video didn't feel like a list of instructions I had to memorise. I could understand the main idea and connect it with something I was trying to improve myself.","Afterwards, I thought about my English practice. Instead of expecting every answer to sound natural immediately, I felt more willing to repeat it and make small changes. I found the video interesting because advice from a different field could still be useful in my everyday life."],"keywords":"Federer → Dartmouth 2024 → 练习 → 自然表达 → 英语","note":"观看时间、推荐人及感受均为样例。实际视频是Federer在Dartmouth的2024年毕业典礼演讲，不是采访，也没有称为短视频。官方核验：https://home.dartmouth.edu/news/2024/06/2024-commencement-address-roger-federer。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an interesting video you watched.","audio":"audio/8335f137585359f7.m4a"},{"id":"T027","title":"无聊的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M24","script":["A place I found boring was the waiting room of a customer-service centre. I went there a while ago to update some account details, and I expected the visit to be fairly quick. However, I needed to wait for my number to be called.","The room had rows of chairs and a few information posters on the walls. There wasn't much to look at, and most people were sitting quietly. I found a seat and checked the papers I had brought, but that only took a few minutes.","After that, I kept looking at the time and the number being shown. I hadn't brought a book because I didn't expect to wait long. I tried reading the information posters, although most of it wasn't connected with the reason I was there.","What made the place boring was having very little to do while not knowing exactly how long I would be waiting. I couldn't simply leave, because I still needed to get the account issue sorted out. The visit took around forty minutes before someone could help me.","The staff dealt with the task once it was my turn, so I wouldn't describe the whole service as bad. It was mainly the waiting room experience that I disliked. Next time, I'd bring something to read and allow more time."],"keywords":"买菜 → 短途 → 堵车 → 等待 → 耳机替换件","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a place where you felt bored.","audio":"audio/38ee9d004af7ab41.m4a"},{"id":"T028","title":"一次早起的经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M05","script":["A time I got up earlier than usual was one Saturday when I arranged to meet a friend for a morning walk. We wanted to go out before the day became too hot, so we agreed to meet shortly after sunrise.","I'm not normally someone who wakes up very early on a day off. To make it easier, I prepared my clothes and set an alarm the night before. I also went to bed a little earlier instead of staying on my phone.","When the alarm rang, I wanted to go back to sleep. However, I knew my friend was expecting me, so I got ready and left. Once I was outside, I began to feel more awake. The streets were quieter than usual, and the air felt more comfortable.","We walked for a while and then had breakfast together. I enjoyed having time to talk without feeling rushed. By the time I got home, I had already done something pleasant, and there was still most of the day left.","I was glad I had made the effort. I wouldn't want to wake up at that time every weekend, but it showed me why some people enjoy an early start. Planning one enjoyable activity made getting out of bed much easier."],"keywords":"约好散步 → 前晚准备 → 早起 → 安静街道 → 值得","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an occasion when you got up early.","audio":"audio/fc9e58c61d38ab2d.m4a"},{"id":"T029","title":"喜欢种植物的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M07","script":["I'd like to talk about my grandmother and a skill she taught me when I was a child. She enjoyed looking after plants, and whenever I visited her, I liked spending time in the small garden near her home.","When I was about ten, she helped me grow a plant of my own. At first, I thought I only needed to put it in the soil and water it as much as possible. She explained that plants needed the right amount of water and enough light, and that doing more wasn't always doing better.","We checked the plant together every few days. I was impatient because I wanted to see a result immediately. She encouraged me to notice small changes instead of expecting something dramatic overnight.","Eventually, I saw new leaves, and I felt surprisingly proud. It was a small achievement, but it was something I had helped create and look after myself.","What I admire about my grandmother is her patience. She didn't make me feel foolish when I made mistakes. She explained things calmly and let me try again. I still remember that experience because it taught me more than how to care for a plant. It also taught me to be consistent and to give things time."],"keywords":"童年去祖母家 → 种植物 → 我的失败 → 她教耐心 → 现在仍记得。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who likes growing plants.","audio":"audio/c3a8b306a2bcd931.m4a"},{"id":"T030","title":"希望在祖国引入的新规则","category":"事物","masterId":"M15","script":["A new rule I'd like to introduce more widely in China, my home country, would require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear instructions. Some places already have useful systems, but I'd like residents in more communities to have easy access to them. The focus would be on making recycling a simple part of everyday life.","For example, each building could have an accessible collection area for paper, plastic bottles and metal cans. The signs could use simple pictures and several languages, so new residents would understand what belongs in each container. Building managers would also need to arrange regular collection.","I started thinking about this while sorting packaging at home. Sometimes I have a few empty bottles or delivery boxes, and I want to deal with them properly without making a separate trip across the city. A reliable collection point close to home would make the routine much simpler.","I'd prefer a gradual introduction, with clear guidance before penalties. If people misunderstand the system, helping them correct the mistake would be more useful than immediately punishing them.","The main reason I support this idea is that convenience affects behaviour. When the easier choice is also the environmentally responsible choice, more people are likely to follow it consistently."],"keywords":"中国 → 住宅楼 → 分类指引 → 定期收集 → 方便居民","note":"本题用中国作为祖国样例，上海现有规则和全国推广建议分开讲。若选择UAE，需明确它是你现居的国家。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a new rule you would like your home country to introduce.","audio":"audio/5584a871df24e440.m4a"},{"id":"T031","title":"童年好友","category":"人物","masterId":"M09","script":["I'd like to talk about my childhood friend Ben. We grew up in the same neighbourhood and became friends when we were about ten. We used to ride our bikes after school, and although we now live in different cities, we still talk regularly.","My clearest memory of Ben is from a school sports day. I fell off my bike on the way home and felt embarrassed because other children were watching. He stayed with me, checked that I was all right and walked his own bike beside mine. It was a small gesture, but it showed me that I could count on him.","We were both quite curious as children. We built small things from cardboard, borrowed books from the library and argued about which bike route was faster. These days, we have different interests and live in different cities, but we still exchange messages. He sometimes practises Chinese with me, and I ask him about his latest history project.","What makes the friendship valuable is that we can speak honestly without trying to impress each other. He remembers what I was like before I started working, and that makes talking to him feel comfortable. I'm glad we've stayed in touch because a friendship like that has grown through years of ordinary, shared experiences."],"keywords":"childhood friend → good at learning languages → English and Chinese → history lover → old photographs → museum","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a friend you had when you were a child.","audio":"audio/58450a8d86d5ea0d.m4a"},{"id":"T032","title":"想从事医疗工作的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M10","script":["I'd like to talk about my cousin Sara, who wants to become a nurse. She's a few years younger than me, and we've known each other since childhood. We usually meet at family gatherings, but recently we've also been talking about her future career.","Her interest in nursing began when our grandmother spent several days in hospital. Sara noticed that the nurses did much more than check equipment. They explained what was happening and helped our grandmother feel less anxious. She said she wanted a job where her work could make a practical difference to someone's day.","To explore the idea, she volunteered at a community health event last summer. Her role was simple: welcoming visitors, showing them where to queue and helping them complete basic forms. She didn't provide medical treatment. One older visitor was confused about the registration process, and Sara patiently explained each step. Afterwards, she told me that she had enjoyed helping him feel comfortable.","Her plan is to apply for a nursing course, improve her science knowledge and keep volunteering when she can. She knows the work can involve long shifts and difficult situations, so she doesn't see it as an easy career. I admire her because her ambition is based on real interest and some first-hand experience, rather than just the title."],"keywords":"medical career → nurse → cousin → volunteering → patient communication → future plans","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who would like to work in healthcare.","audio":"audio/ac913d1a1e925fba.m4a"},{"id":"T033","title":"经营生意的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M12","script":["I'd like to talk about my friend Alex, who runs a small coffee shop near a residential area. I met him through a mutual friend a few years ago. Since then, I've visited his shop fairly often, usually on a Saturday morning.","When he first opened it, the business was difficult. There weren't many customers in the morning, and some food was left unsold at the end of each day. Instead of immediately spending more money on advertising, he asked regular customers what they wanted and checked which items actually sold.","He reduced the menu to a few reliable choices, prepared smaller batches and introduced a simple breakfast combination. He also created a quiet corner where customers could read or work. Gradually, people started coming back. What I like most is the service: he remembers regular customers' orders and deals with problems politely. Once, my coffee arrived cold, and he replaced it without making the situation awkward.","I think the shop succeeds because he understands his customers and pays attention to everyday details. He keeps a clear stock list and gives his team sensible tasks, but he's also friendly and enjoys chatting with people. I'm pleased to see his hard work paying off. His experience reminds me that running a good business often depends on steady improvements, rather than one dramatic idea."],"keywords":"small business → coffee shop → successful businessperson → organised person → happy person → customer service → solving difficulties","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who runs a business.","audio":"audio/0d51a56c67d10354.m4a"},{"id":"T034","title":"一次改变原计划的经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M08","script":["One time I changed a plan was when I was organising a birthday gathering for a friend. My original idea was to have a small picnic outdoors. A few of us would bring food, sit together and keep the afternoon simple and inexpensive.","However, on the morning of the gathering, the weather looked windy, and the forecast suggested that rain was possible. I realised that the food and decorations would be difficult to manage outside. I also didn't want everyone to arrive and then feel uncomfortable.","I checked with the group and suggested meeting at a restaurant instead. I found somewhere within our budget, confirmed that there was room for us and sent everyone the new address and time. Another friend contacted the person bringing the cake so that it went to the right place.","The change meant that we no longer needed to prepare picnic food or carry everything outdoors. We could simply meet, order a meal and enjoy the evening. The birthday friend seemed pleased, and the atmosphere was relaxed because nobody was worrying about the weather.","I was happy with the decision because the important part of the plan was spending time together. Although the setting changed, we still achieved that. The experience taught me to keep the purpose of an event in mind and make a practical adjustment when the original arrangement becomes difficult."],"keywords":"朋友生日 → 野餐 → 天气 → 餐厅 → 大家满意","note":"全部生日、天气、餐厅及结果为样例。生日主角是朋友；我负责组织并改变计划。天气只是这次样例经历，没有声称某日确有公共天气事件。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you changed a plan you had made.","audio":"audio/9ac0f64de895dbd4.m4a"},{"id":"T035","title":"一次团队合作","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["A time I worked in a group was when a few colleagues and I built a small tool for a repeated task at work. We wanted to reduce the amount of manual checking. Each person understood a different part of the problem, so working together was important.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"keywords":"请求管理 → 分工 → 小原型 → 测试 → 合作","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a task you completed as part of a team.","audio":"audio/e0a10c7be0dbf7bd.m4a"},{"id":"T036","title":"做过的重要决定","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["I'd like to describe a decision I made while working on a small project with my team. We had a repetitive task that involved checking information manually, and I wanted to build a tool to make it easier.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"keywords":"重复工作 → 大方案 → 同事提议 → 小原型 → 测试成功 → 改变看法。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an important decision you made.","audio":"audio/23b21937cd25ee34.m4a"},{"id":"T037","title":"现场观看的体育比赛","category":"经历","masterId":"M13","script":["A live sporting event I enjoyed was the men's final at the Dubai Duty Free Tennis Championships on the first of March, 2025. I went with a friend to the Dubai Duty Free Tennis Stadium. The match was between Stefanos Tsitsipas and Felix Auger-Aliassime, and Tsitsipas won six-three, six-three.","We arrived before the match and had time to find our seats and look around. I'd watched tennis at home before, but being there felt different. I could hear the ball striking the rackets, and the players seemed much faster when I saw them with my own eyes.","The crowd became quiet before each point, then reacted together when a rally ended. I found myself paying more attention than I normally would in front of a television. Even when I didn't fully understand a tactical decision, the tension was easy to feel.","Afterwards, my friend and I discussed the match on our way home. I enjoyed both the sport and the feeling of sharing an evening with so many other spectators. The result was part of the experience, but what I remember most is the atmosphere. It made me want to attend another tennis event."],"keywords":"运动员 → 钦佩的人 → 克服困难 → 成功人士 → 想见的人 → 现场体育赛事（独立版本）","note":"比赛本身有公开资料；现场观看、同行者与感受是样例。运动员主稿与现场比赛是不同版本。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a sporting event you watched in person.","audio":"audio/6c6c318f591c5757.m4a"},{"id":"T038","title":"特殊场合吃过的食物","category":"事物","masterId":"M08","script":["A food that people often eat on a special occasion is birthday cake. In my experience, it is usually brought out near the end of a birthday meal and shared with friends or family. The style depends on what the person likes.","One example I remember is a chocolate cake at a friend's birthday dinner. It had a small decoration connected to his hobby. We had arranged the dinner simply, but the cake made the evening feel more like a celebration.","A basic cake is made by preparing a mixture, baking it and then adding some decoration or a topping. I don't think the recipe has to be complicated. The important thing is that everyone can share it and that it suits the person whose birthday it is.","When we brought out my friend's cake, we gathered around, sang and took a few photos. He hadn't expected the personal decoration, so his reaction was the most memorable part. Afterwards, we cut the cake and continued talking.","I associate this food with making time for other people. It gives a group a small shared moment, rather than just another item to eat. That's why even a simple birthday cake can feel special. If the question required a traditional festival food, I'd choose a different example."],"keywords":"朋友生日 → 蛋糕 → 简单装饰 → 分享 → 特殊意义","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe food you ate on a special occasion.","audio":"audio/9124bc438fd5f812.m4a"},{"id":"T039","title":"擅长学语言的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M09","script":["Someone I know who's good at learning languages is my childhood friend Ben. We became friends when we were about ten, and we still practise together through voice messages even though we now live in different cities.","One thing I admire about him is the way he learns languages. He studies English by watching short videos with subtitles, noting useful expressions and recording himself using them. He also learns Chinese, and we practise together through voice messages. Rather than memorising long lists, he uses new words in simple conversations. Recently, he managed to order a meal in Chinese and ask the waiter about the ingredients without switching to English.","What impresses me most is how confidently Ben uses the languages he learns. When we practise Chinese, he asks me to correct one or two mistakes at a time. The following week, those mistakes have usually disappeared. He also records the same English story twice and compares the recordings, so he can hear whether his speech is becoming clearer.","I admire his patience as much as his progress. When I make a mistake, he corrects me gently and adds a funny example, so the conversation doesn't become stressful. He has shown me that improving a language can come from small daily habits, rather than waiting until you feel ready to speak."],"keywords":"childhood friend → good at learning languages → English and Chinese → history lover → old photographs → museum","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who is good at learning languages.","audio":"audio/60eaaf8c9ad3c1d2.m4a"},{"id":"T040","title":"使用科技时遇到困难","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["A challenging technical problem I faced was getting a small tool to read information correctly. I was working on it with a team at work. The aim was to reduce manual checking, but our first attempt produced results we couldn't rely on.","At first, I thought the main function was wrong. However, after comparing a few examples, we realised that some of the information was written in a different format. The tool was treating those examples as if they followed the same pattern as the others.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"keywords":"新工具 → 报错 → 排查 → 同事帮助 → 解决","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a difficulty you had while using technology.","audio":"audio/48f780b0dd6b2466.m4a"},{"id":"T041","title":"有名人出现的广告","category":"事物","masterId":"M11","script":["I'd like to describe an online advertisement for Huda Beauty's #FauxFilter foundation featuring Huda Kattan. I saw the campaign image on the brand's website. It showed her with other women in a group photograph, and the product was being promoted through the campaign. What caught my attention was that the image felt friendly and personal. It made me curious about how brands use their founders in advertising.","The image was part of the brand's 2017 campaign, which I found through an article called 'The Making Of Our #FauxFilter Foundation'. The article explained that Huda appeared in a group picture taken near the end of the shoot. I liked the connection between the founder and the product being advertised.","I'm not particularly interested in buying foundation, but I found the advertising idea interesting. A company can show a product on its own, or it can introduce a person who helps customers recognise the brand. In this case, seeing Huda made me curious about the business behind the image.","The advertisement was memorable because it had a human element. It didn't persuade me to buy something I didn't need, but it encouraged me to learn more about the company. I think that's a useful effect of advertising: attracting interest first, while leaving customers to decide whether the product is relevant to them."],"keywords":"Huda Kattan → #FauxFilter → 宣传照 → 本人出镜 → 记住产品","note":"本例是Huda本人出镜的真实产品宣传照，可以谈视觉广告；不要描述成未核实的电视广告。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an advertisement featuring a famous person.","audio":"audio/1cd5186f92e7c794.m4a"},{"id":"T042","title":"推荐别人游览的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M17","script":["I'd like to describe West Lake in Hangzhou, a city in Zhejiang Province in eastern China. I visited it with a friend during a short holiday last year. We had a busy few weeks before the trip, so we wanted somewhere we could explore without rushing.","We spent an afternoon walking along the paths beside the lake. What I remember most is the space around the water. There were trees beside the path, and we could stop whenever we noticed a view we liked. I took a few photos, but I also put my phone away for part of the walk.","At one point, we sat down and watched the light change on the water. We talked about ordinary things and didn't feel that we had to keep moving to another attraction. Afterwards, we found somewhere nearby to have a simple meal.","For me, the lake is important because it gives people a place to enjoy being outdoors while visiting a city. I liked the balance between walking, looking around and having time to talk.","I'd happily go back, especially with someone who enjoys a slower kind of holiday. Next time, I'd leave more time to explore Hangzhou beyond the lake, rather than trying to fit everything into one afternoon."],"keywords":"杭州 → 西湖 → 步道 → 朋友 → 重游","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a place you would recommend to a visitor.","audio":"audio/d8d63a948d40e627.m4a"},{"id":"T043","title":"喜欢拜访但不想住的家","category":"地点","masterId":"M20","script":["A home I enjoy visiting but wouldn't want to live in is my grandmother's house. I used to go there quite often when I was younger, and I still associate it with spending unhurried time with my family. It isn't a large or modern place, but it feels familiar to me.","The room I remember best is the living room. There is a comfortable sofa, a small table and some family photographs. My grandmother also looks after a few plants near the house. When I visit, we usually have something to drink and talk about what has happened since we last saw each other.","On my last visit, I helped her with a small job and then stayed for lunch. Nothing especially exciting happened, but I enjoyed having time for an ordinary conversation. I didn't feel that I had to keep checking the time.","Although I like visiting, I wouldn't choose to live there permanently. It is too far from the places I need to reach for work, and I'd prefer having my own space and routine. As an adult, I moved into an apartment closer to work, which suited my daily life better.","So the house is special because of the person and memories connected with it. Enjoying a visit doesn't necessarily mean that it would be the right place for me to live."],"keywords":"祖母 → 熟悉的家 → 探望 → 距离 → 自己的空间","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a home you like visiting but would not want to live in.","audio":"audio/a35ddbff9e8577d8.m4a"},{"id":"T044","title":"和动物有关的故事","category":"事物","masterId":"M14","script":["An animal story I remember clearly is The Tortoise and the Hare. It's a short fable associated with Aesop, and I first heard it from my father when I was in primary school. Later, I read an illustrated version myself, which made me feel quite proud.","The story is about a race between two very different animals. The hare is fast and confident, while the tortoise moves slowly. Because the hare thinks winning will be easy, he stops for a nap. The tortoise keeps going and reaches the finish before him.","As a child, I found the ending funny and surprising. At the beginning, I was certain that the hare would win, so I wanted to turn the pages quickly. I also liked the pictures because they helped me understand what was happening without needing an adult to explain every sentence.","The lesson has stayed with me: steady effort matters, and being good at something doesn't mean you can stop trying. I think of it when I'm learning a skill and comparing myself with people who improve faster. The story reminds me to focus on my own progress. It's simple, but that's probably why I still remember it after so many years."],"keywords":"动物故事 → 故事 → 书（故事集版本） → 开心的阅读经历 → 童年学到的事 → 坚持 → 喜欢的角色","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a story involving an animal.","audio":"audio/12f8d0647be493dd.m4a"},{"id":"T045","title":"祖国一项有用的现有规定","category":"事物","masterId":"M15","script":["An existing rule I think is useful is Shanghai's household waste sorting rule. Shanghai is a city in China, and sorting household rubbish has been legally required there since the first of July, 2019. I'm talking about a local rule in Shanghai, rather than one identical rule for the whole country.","The system separates household waste into four categories: recyclables, hazardous waste, wet waste and dry waste. For example, food leftovers belong with wet waste, while materials that can be recycled should go into the appropriate recycling bin. Hazardous items need to be handled separately.","I became more aware of this rule during a visit to relatives in Shanghai. In their kitchen, they kept separate containers and checked the labels before throwing things away. At first, I found it a little confusing, especially when an item contained different materials. After a few days, though, the basic routine felt much easier.","I support the idea because it encourages people to think about what happens after they throw something away. However, I think clear signs and convenient collection points are essential. People are more likely to follow a rule when they understand it and can fit it into their daily routine. For me, good environmental rules need practical support as well as expectations."],"keywords":"现有法律 → 喜欢的规则 → 环保 → 希望引入的规则 → 所在国 → 城市改善","note":"中国的地方规定：上海生活垃圾分类，不能说成全国统一规定。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an existing environmental rule in your home country.","audio":"audio/8bdf5133802dd9e6.m4a"},{"id":"T046","title":"等待别人回复","category":"经历","masterId":"M06","script":["A time I waited a long time for a reply was when I contacted a shop about a problem with my headphones. One side had stopped working, and I wanted to know what I needed to bring in for a replacement.","I sent a short message with the purchase details and a description of the fault. I thought I would hear back fairly quickly, but after several days there was still no reply. I checked that I had used the correct contact information before sending a polite follow-up.","The wait was frustrating mainly because I didn't know what to do next. I was unsure whether the message had been received, whether the shop needed more information or whether I should visit in person. I didn't want to make an unnecessary trip.","In the end, I went to the shop with the headphones and the proof of purchase. An assistant checked the problem and explained the process. Once I had that information, I felt much more relaxed.","The experience reminded me that even a brief response can be helpful. It doesn't have to solve a problem immediately, but it should let the customer know what is happening. Since then, I've tried to acknowledge messages when I can't give a complete answer straight away."],"keywords":"售后咨询 → 等待 → 再联系 → 得到回复 → 松口气","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you had to wait for someone's reply.","audio":"audio/fd39899183957ff1.m4a"},{"id":"T047","title":"想实现的长期目标","category":"经历","masterId":"M21","script":["A long-term goal I'd like to achieve is being able to use English comfortably in work and study. I understand a lot when I read, but I sometimes hesitate when explaining my own ideas. I want that gap to shrink.","This matters because good ideas are less useful if I can't communicate them clearly. I'd like to take part in discussions, ask questions when something is unclear and explain a problem without worrying much about finding the perfect words.","I've started with a simple routine. I choose a short question, record an answer and listen back. If a sentence is difficult to say, I try again with simpler language. I also read or listen to something useful and explain the main point in my own words.","Some days feel easier than others. I don't expect every recording to be better than the previous one, but I can notice small changes, such as pausing less or giving a clearer example. That helps me continue when progress feels slow.","I would consider the goal achieved when I can express what I mean and follow a conversation more confidently. It isn't about using impressive words all the time. For me, it is about being able to communicate naturally and take part more fully."],"keywords":"英语 → 长期目标 → 录音 → 表达 → 自信","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a long-term goal you would like to achieve.","audio":"audio/9674c4841afbdbc3.m4a"},{"id":"T048","title":"一次改变想法的经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["An opinion I changed was my belief that a new idea should be fully developed before anyone tried it. I changed my mind during a small project at work. We wanted to build a tool that would make a repeated manual task easier.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"keywords":"项目方案 → 原先复杂 → 听取意见 → 小原型 → 改变想法","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you changed your opinion.","audio":"audio/4eb44cdcad7830f7.m4a"},{"id":"T049","title":"所在城市的一条新闻","category":"事物","masterId":"M16","script":["A piece of local news I found encouraging was about improvements to Dubai's bus network. I read an RTA announcement in September 2026 after a friend shared the link. The announcement itself was published on the sixth of January, so I was discovering an earlier development rather than reading about something launched that week.","According to the announcement, four new public bus routes were scheduled to start operating on the ninth of January. RTA also announced improvements to more than seventy existing internal routes, including changes to route coverage and services during busy periods. The aim was to make everyday travel more convenient.","This caught my attention because I live in Dubai and sometimes use public transport. I don't use every route mentioned, so I can't say that the changes directly shortened my own commute. Still, better connections could make buses a more practical option for people travelling between neighbourhoods.","After reading the article, I checked whether any of the routes were relevant to places I visit. I also sent the link back to my friend with a short comment saying that this was the kind of local news I liked: a practical improvement that could affect ordinary daily life. It made me feel positive about the city, and I would like to see the network continue to improve."],"keywords":"新闻 → 好消息 → 本地新闻 → 城市改善 → 公共交通 → 网上看到的信息 → 社区变化","note":"新闻公布于2026年1月6日，措施于1月9日生效；“何时看到新闻”是个人经历样例。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a piece of news about the city where you live.","audio":"audio/f3235dd5a0184aa2.m4a"},{"id":"T050","title":"一本让你读得入迷的书","category":"事物","masterId":"M02","script":["I'd like to talk about a novel called The Martian, by Andy Weir. I read it a few months ago after a friend recommended it. I usually prefer stories that feel practical, so the combination of science and adventure appealed to me.","The main character is an astronaut called Mark Watney, who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to find ways to stay alive and contact people on Earth. The situation sounds hopeless, but he doesn't give up. He deals with one problem at a time, using whatever resources he has.","What I enjoyed most was the way he thought through his difficulties. The book made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the story enjoyable as well.","I read a little in the evening, and I often continued longer than I had planned because I wanted to know what would happen next. I felt relieved whenever one of his ideas worked.","The story also gave me a useful reminder: a big problem becomes less frightening when you focus on the next small action. I think that's why it stayed with me. I'd recommend it to someone who enjoys a hopeful story with a clever main character."],"keywords":"推荐 → 被困火星 → 一次解决一个问题 → 紧张但有幽默 → 对我的启发。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a book you found exciting to read.","audio":"audio/429b3f4b9218f598.m4a"},{"id":"T051","title":"克服困难取得成功的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M11","script":["A person I know about who overcame difficulties and became successful is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. She's associated with Dubai, and I became interested in her through public articles about her business. I've never met her personally.","She launched her brand in Dubai in 2013 with false eyelashes, after working as a makeup artist and beauty blogger. Building a company from an idea is a considerable challenge, especially when there isn't a clear route to follow. It involves decisions as well as practical skills.","In an account of her appearance at the Global Women's Forum Dubai in 2024, she discussed moments of self-doubt and the importance of continuing. What I take from that is that confidence doesn't always come first. Sometimes you gain it by taking one manageable step and learning from the result.","I admire this because it sounds more realistic than imagining successful people never feel uncertain. When I face an unfamiliar project, I can waste time trying to have a perfect plan before I begin. Her story reminds me to identify the next useful action, get some feedback and adjust. For me, that is a valuable lesson from her success."],"keywords":"Dubai local celebrity → popular person → successful entrepreneur → overcoming difficulty → ForbesWomen interview → FauxFilter campaign","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person who overcame difficulties and succeeded.","audio":"audio/691f35f38663c74f.m4a"},{"id":"T052","title":"电子设备出了故障","category":"经历","masterId":"M06","script":["A problem I had with an electronic device was when one side of my headphones stopped working. I had bought them a few weeks earlier and was using them regularly for work and English recordings. At first, I thought the recording or connection might be the problem.","I tried a different recording and connected the headphones again. The same side still wasn't working, so I decided to stop guessing and contact the shop. I found the proof of purchase and explained when the fault had started.","The shop assistant checked the headphones and confirmed that they weren't working properly. He explained the replacement process clearly. I was relieved that I didn't have to understand the internal parts of the device in order to get help.","A few weeks later, one side stopped working properly. I took them back to the shop, expecting a long argument. Instead, the assistant listened carefully, checked the problem and explained the next steps. After confirming the fault, the shop arranged a replacement.","That experience made the purchase more memorable. I appreciated both the product and the way the problem was handled. For me, the value wasn't just the price or the brand. It was having something useful and knowing that I could get help when it didn't work as expected."],"keywords":"耳机断连 → 自己检查 → 联系门店 → 更换 → 学到方法","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a problem you had with an electronic device.","audio":"audio/90497dd34f101634.m4a"},{"id":"T053","title":"一座公共建筑","category":"地点","masterId":"M19","script":["A public building I'd like to describe is Mohammed Bin Rashid Library in Dubai. It stands beside Dubai Creek, and its design is inspired by a traditional book rest. The library has seven levels, but what first caught my attention was its unusual shape rather than its height.","I visited it one afternoon after a friend suggested going somewhere different from our usual cafés. Before that visit, I had seen photographs of the building, but I wanted to understand what it was like to spend time there.","We looked around and then found somewhere to sit and read. I chose a book in English and spent some time working through a few pages. I didn't understand every word, but the setting helped me stay focused instead of moving between different things on my phone.","What I appreciated most was that the visit had a clear purpose without feeling rushed. I could read, notice the building and take a short break from work. It felt different from being in a shopping centre, where I often end up looking at things I don't need.","I'd recommend it to someone interested in books or architecture. For me, a useful public building offers more than an interesting photograph. It gives people somewhere to learn and spend their time well."],"keywords":"图书馆 → 书架形建筑 → 公共空间 → 阅读 → 哈利法塔","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a public building you have visited.","audio":"audio/b6d6dc5e464ea6ee.m4a"},{"id":"T054","title":"印象深刻的聚会","category":"经历","masterId":"M08","script":["I'd like to describe a birthday dinner I helped organise for a friend. It happened a few months ago, and there were just a few of us. We wanted to make the evening special without turning it into a complicated or expensive event.","I checked when everyone was available and chose a place that was easy for us to reach. Another friend arranged the cake, while I made the reservation and confirmed the time. We also asked him what food he liked so that he would enjoy the meal.","On the evening itself, we arrived a little early and made sure everything was ready. The atmosphere was relaxed. We talked about work, shared some funny stories and took a few photos together.","The most memorable moment was when the cake came out. It was quite simple, but it had a small decoration connected to one of his hobbies. He hadn't expected it, and his reaction made the effort feel worthwhile.","I was pleased that the plan worked and that everyone had a good time. It reminded me that a successful celebration doesn't depend on spending a lot of money. Paying attention to the person and making time for each other can be much more important."],"keywords":"朋友生日 → 简单安排 → 分工 → 蛋糕惊喜 → 朋友高兴。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a party that made a strong impression on you.","audio":"audio/3fab4a86ba272c39.m4a"},{"id":"T055","title":"聪明解决问题的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["I'd like to describe my colleague Adam, who helped solve a problem in a simple but clever way. We met at work about two years ago. I often ask him for advice because he can identify what is actually making a task difficult.","The problem was that I had too much information in a presentation. My first reaction was to add even more explanation. Adam suggested doing the opposite: remove the unnecessary details and show one example that people could easily understand.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Since then, I've tried to follow his approach. Whenever a task feels overwhelming, I break it into smaller steps. So he's had a positive influence on the way I work."],"keywords":"Adam → 请求混乱 → 找到症结 → 简单列表 → 解决问题","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who found a clever solution to a problem.","audio":"audio/6a56547966ce241e.m4a"},{"id":"T056","title":"想引入的环保规则","category":"事物","masterId":"M15","script":["A new rule I'd like to introduce more widely in China, my home country, would require large residential buildings to provide convenient recycling points and clear instructions. Some places already have useful systems, but I'd like residents in more communities to have easy access to them. The focus would be on making recycling a simple part of everyday life.","For example, each building could have an accessible collection area for paper, plastic bottles and metal cans. The signs could use simple pictures and several languages, so new residents would understand what belongs in each container. Building managers would also need to arrange regular collection.","I started thinking about this while sorting packaging at home. Sometimes I have a few empty bottles or delivery boxes, and I want to deal with them properly without making a separate trip across the city. A reliable collection point close to home would make the routine much simpler.","I'd prefer a gradual introduction, with clear guidance before penalties. If people misunderstand the system, helping them correct the mistake would be more useful than immediately punishing them.","The main reason I support this idea is that convenience affects behaviour. When the easier choice is also the environmentally responsible choice, more people are likely to follow it consistently."],"keywords":"中国 → 住宅楼 → 分类指引 → 定期收集 → 方便居民","note":"本题用中国作为祖国样例，上海现有规则和全国推广建议分开讲。若选择UAE，需明确它是你现居的国家。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an environmental rule you would like to introduce.","audio":"audio/5584a871df24e440.m4a"},{"id":"T057","title":"最近做的一项生活改变","category":"经历","masterId":"M05","script":["I'd like to talk about a small change I made to my evening routine. I used to come home from work and immediately start looking at my phone. I told myself I was taking a short break, but quite often I ended up scrolling for nearly an hour.","The problem was that I didn't feel rested afterwards. I was still tired, and sometimes I went to bed later than I had planned. So I decided to replace part of that screen time with a short walk.","I started with just ten minutes because I knew I wouldn't stick to an ambitious exercise plan. When the weather was comfortable, I walked outside. On other days, I found somewhere indoors where I could move around. I usually left my phone in my pocket and paid attention to my surroundings.","After a while, a friend began joining me. That made the habit easier to maintain because we could chat and remind each other to go. We weren't trying to become athletes. We just wanted to do something more active after sitting for most of the day.","The walk gives me a clear break between work and the rest of my evening. The change is simple, but it helps me relax and makes me feel more in control of my time."],"keywords":"下班累 → 刷手机更久 → 十分钟散步 → 和朋友坚持 → 状态变好。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a recent change you made to your daily life.","audio":"audio/31bf46c69725e72d.m4a"},{"id":"T058","title":"想再次游览的城市","category":"地点","masterId":"M17","script":["A city I'd like to visit again is Hangzhou, in eastern China. I went there with a friend during a short holiday last year, but the trip felt too short. What I enjoyed most was being able to slow down and spend time outdoors.","We spent an afternoon walking beside West Lake. There were trees along the path, and we stopped several times to look at the water. We also sat down for a while and talked, without feeling that we had to move straight to another attraction.","Away from the lake, we walked through some nearby streets and found a place to eat. I enjoyed noticing ordinary parts of the city as well as the view by the water. However, we didn't have much time to explore further.","On a second visit, I'd stay for a few days. I'd leave one morning for the lake and spend another afternoon looking around a different neighbourhood. I'd also allow time for a meal with anyone I knew in the area.","I'd like to return because I already know one part I enjoy, but still feel curious about the rest. I prefer that kind of trip to a packed schedule where I spend most of the day checking what I need to do next."],"keywords":"杭州 → 西湖 → 步道 → 朋友 → 重游","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a city you would like to visit again.","audio":"audio/5d02ea0e267f8567.m4a"},{"id":"T059","title":"只见过一次却想再见的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["A person I only met once but would like to know better is a man called Adam. I met him at a small photography workshop last month. We spoke for about twenty minutes while practising how to take pictures of the street outside.","I noticed him because he was using a basic phone but still taking interesting photos. He didn't seem concerned about having the most expensive equipment. Instead, he paid attention to the light, the background and the position of the people in the picture.","When I asked how he made an ordinary scene look so good, he showed me a simple example. He moved a little to one side, waited for a person to walk past and then took the photo. That small change made the picture much more balanced.","He explained the idea patiently and asked me to try it myself. I liked the fact that he was willing to share what he knew without making me feel inexperienced. Before we left, he mentioned that he enjoyed photographing different cities.","I'd like to know more about his travels and see some of those photographs. He seemed observant, friendly and easy to talk to. Although our conversation was short, I came away with a useful idea and the feeling that we could have an interesting conversation again."],"keywords":"摄影活动 → 只见一次 → Adam → 实用建议 → 想再聊天","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person you have met only once and would like to meet again.","audio":"audio/0af724a19d1a4d06.m4a"},{"id":"T060","title":"将来想送给别人的礼物","category":"事物","masterId":"M06","script":["A gift I'd like to buy for a friend is a pair of comfortable headphones. My friend Sam enjoys listening to music and is also trying to improve his English. We've known each other for a few years, so I have a fairly good idea of what he would use.","He sometimes listens through his phone's speaker, which isn't very convenient when other people are nearby. I think headphones would let him enjoy recordings and practise listening without disturbing anyone. They could also be useful when he wants to concentrate.","I wouldn't choose the most expensive pair automatically. I'd compare comfort, sound quality and how easy they are to use. If possible, I'd ask him about his preferences without immediately revealing that I was thinking about a gift.","I'd probably give them to him on his birthday. I would include a short note explaining why I chose them, because I think that personal detail matters. I might also suggest an English podcast we could both listen to and discuss afterwards.","I'd choose this gift because it connects with his actual interests. A useful present can show that someone has paid attention to you. I hope he would enjoy it regularly, rather than put it away after the first day."],"keywords":"送给朋友 → 耳机 → 日常用途 → 预算 → 实用心意","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a gift you would like to give someone in the future.","audio":"audio/16e0f3649250bd70.m4a"},{"id":"T061","title":"将来第一次想去的城市","category":"地点","masterId":"M17","script":["A city I'd like to visit in the future is Suzhou, in eastern China. I haven't been there yet, but photographs of its canals have made me curious about it. I'd like to go with a friend who enjoys walking and a slower kind of holiday.","The place I'd most like to see is one of the canals. I'd spend a morning exploring the paths beside the water, stopping when we found somewhere pleasant to sit. I wouldn't want the whole visit to become a list of photographs I needed to take.","I'd also leave time to explore another part of the city. We could look around some streets, find somewhere to eat and choose one other activity according to what interested us. I'd rather make a realistic plan than try to see everything in a day.","Before booking, I'd check the weather, transport and accommodation costs. I would also look for recent practical information so that I understood how to get between the places we wanted to visit.","What attracts me is the possibility of combining a city visit with time by the water. I spend a lot of time indoors, so that balance sounds appealing. I'd hope to come home with a clearer impression of the place and a few memories shared with a friend."],"keywords":"苏州 → 尚未去过 → 运河 → 慢慢散步 → 将来计划","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a city you have not visited yet but would like to see.","audio":"audio/3cfefd8546d1f41f.m4a"},{"id":"T062","title":"收到蛋糕的一次经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M08","script":["A special cake I received was one my friends gave me on my birthday a few months ago. I hadn't planned a large celebration, so I was surprised when they invited me to a simple dinner and brought out the cake afterwards.","It was a chocolate cake with a small decoration connected to one of my hobbies. It wasn't especially large or expensive, but the detail showed that they had thought about me. They had arranged it without telling me, which made the surprise work.","We sat together, talked about things that had happened that week and took a few photos. When the cake arrived, everyone smiled and sang. I felt slightly embarrassed by the attention at first, but it was a very warm moment.","We shared the cake after the meal. What I remember most isn't the exact taste, although I enjoyed it. It's the feeling of spending time with people who had made an effort to celebrate with me. I also kept a photo of the cake as a reminder.","The cake was special because it felt personal. A simple gift can mean a lot when it reflects something about the person receiving it. I'd like to do something similar for a friend rather than assume that a more expensive present is always better."],"keywords":"我的生日 → 朋友安排 → 收到蛋糕 → 惊喜 → 被重视","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an occasion when you received a cake.","audio":"audio/aed6f20b51ceae42.m4a"},{"id":"T063","title":"为提高语言水平做过的事","category":"经历","masterId":"M21","script":["One thing I did to improve my English was start recording myself answering a short question each day. I began a few months ago because I realised that reading and listening alone weren't giving me enough practice in expressing my own ideas.","I usually chose a topic connected with my daily life, such as a recent outing or something I had learned at work. That meant I could concentrate on explaining my meaning instead of trying to invent an interesting story at the same time.","After recording, I listened back and noticed the places where I hesitated. Sometimes the problem was a word I couldn't remember. More often, I was trying to make a sentence too complicated. I then answered the same question again using simpler language.","Occasionally, I asked a friend whether my example was clear. I found that more useful than only asking whether the answer sounded good. If the meaning was difficult to follow, I changed the order or added one concrete detail.","The routine didn't solve everything, but it made speaking feel less unfamiliar. I could notice small improvements, and it was easy enough to continue on a busy day. I'd keep using it because it gives me practice and a clear way to check my progress."],"keywords":"英语 → 长期目标 → 录音 → 表达 → 自信","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe something you did to improve your language skills.","audio":"audio/77f601f6522a017f.m4a"},{"id":"T064","title":"祖国一处重要湖泊","category":"地点","masterId":"M17","script":["An important lake in China that I'd like to describe is West Lake in Hangzhou, in Zhejiang Province. I visited it with a friend during a short holiday last year. We had a busy few weeks before the trip, so we wanted somewhere we could explore without rushing.","We spent an afternoon walking along the paths beside the lake. What I remember most is the space around the water. There were trees beside the path, and we could stop whenever we noticed a view we liked. I took a few photos, but I also put my phone away for part of the walk.","At one point, we sat down and watched the light change on the water. We talked about ordinary things and didn't feel that we had to keep moving to another attraction. Afterwards, we found somewhere nearby to have a simple meal.","For me, the lake is important because it gives people a place to enjoy being outdoors while visiting a city. I liked the balance between walking, looking around and having time to talk.","I'd happily go back, especially with someone who enjoys walking and spending time outdoors. I'd leave enough time to enjoy the lake properly instead of trying to fit several activities into one afternoon. To me, that is what makes a place worth visiting."],"keywords":"杭州 → 西湖 → 步道 → 朋友 → 重游","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an important lake in your home country.","audio":"audio/abd5cffe22694b1b.m4a"},{"id":"T065","title":"花钱不多的外出活动","category":"经历","masterId":"M03","script":["A day out that cost me very little was an afternoon exploring an older part of Dubai with a friend. We chose it because we wanted to do something enjoyable without spending much. Most of the plan involved walking around, looking at the shops and taking photos.","We started near the creek and spent some time looking at the old buildings and small shops. What I liked was the atmosphere. It felt different from the modern shopping malls I normally see. There were narrow streets, people selling different products, and plenty of small details to notice.","At one point, we walked through a busy market. It was quite crowded, and I could hear people talking and calling out to customers. Later, we moved to a quieter spot by the water and took a few photos. The light was softer by then, which made the area look especially nice.","We only spent money on transport and a simple drink. We didn't book an expensive activity or buy things just because they were available. Sitting by the water and talking was one of the best parts, and that didn't require a large budget.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"keywords":"旧迪拜 → 步行 → 简单食物 → 少花钱 → 陪伴","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an outing that did not cost much money.","audio":"audio/bb017ab71855aac4.m4a"},{"id":"T066","title":"成功组织一次开心活动","category":"经历","masterId":"M08","script":["I'd like to describe a birthday dinner I helped organise for a friend. It happened a few months ago, and there were just a few of us. We wanted to make the evening special without turning it into a complicated or expensive event.","I checked when everyone was available and chose a place that was easy for us to reach. Another friend arranged the cake, while I made the reservation and confirmed the time. We also asked him what food he liked so that he would enjoy the meal.","On the evening itself, we arrived a little early and made sure everything was ready. The atmosphere was relaxed. We talked about work, shared some funny stories and took a few photos together.","The most memorable moment was when the cake came out. It was quite simple, but it had a small decoration connected to one of his hobbies. He hadn't expected it, and his reaction made the effort feel worthwhile.","I was pleased that the plan worked and that everyone had a good time. It reminded me that a successful celebration doesn't depend on spending a lot of money. Paying attention to the person and making time for each other can be much more important."],"keywords":"朋友生日 → 简单安排 → 分工 → 蛋糕惊喜 → 朋友高兴。","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a happy event you helped organise.","audio":"audio/3fab4a86ba272c39.m4a"},{"id":"T067","title":"印象深刻的一门课程","category":"经历","masterId":"M21","script":["A course that impressed me was a short course on giving presentations. I took it a while ago because I often needed to explain ideas at work, but I found it difficult to decide what to include and what to leave out. It was held in a training room at my workplace in Dubai.","The teacher asked us to begin with one main message and support it with a simple example. That sounded easy, but during the first exercise I realised that I was adding details which didn't help the audience understand my point.","We practised in small groups and gave each other feedback. I tried again with fewer slides and a clearer order. The teacher also asked us to explain our ideas without reading whole sentences from the screen, which made the exercise feel more practical.","After the course, I used the method in a team presentation. I began with the problem and one example before explaining the details. People understood the idea more quickly, and their questions helped us have a useful discussion.","What impressed me most was the chance to practise rather than simply listen to advice. I left with a method I could use straight away. I still need preparation before a presentation, but I now have a clearer way to organise my thoughts."],"keywords":"迪拜工作培训室 → 老师 → 主旨加例子 → 小组练习 → 实际应用","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a course that impressed you.","audio":"audio/a38278abe838a09b.m4a"},{"id":"T068","title":"接近自然的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M18","script":["A café close to nature that I'd like to describe is a small beachside cafe, near Sunset Beach in Dubai. I went there with a friend one evening after we had spent some time walking beside the sea. We wanted somewhere to sit and have a drink.","We chose a table where we could see the water. The view was the main reason I liked the place. I could notice the light changing outside while sitting comfortably, which felt different from spending another evening inside a shopping centre.","I ordered a cold drink, and we stayed for about half an hour. We talked about our week and a few things we hoped to do at the weekend. The conversation felt relaxed because neither of us was trying to get to another activity immediately.","I remember putting my phone away for most of the visit. There was enough to look at outside, and I didn't feel that I needed something else to keep me interested. The drink was pleasant, but it wasn't the most memorable part.","I'd go back for the setting and the chance to spend quiet time with a friend. For me, a café near nature can turn an ordinary break into something more refreshing, as long as it is comfortable and doesn't feel rushed."],"keywords":"Sunset Beach附近 → 小咖啡馆 → 看海 → 与朋友交谈 → 放松","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a place you like that is close to nature.","audio":"audio/66b53fd32e664ed4.m4a"},{"id":"T069","title":"一次堵车经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M24","script":["One time I was stuck in traffic was on the way to the supermarket on a Saturday. I had left home at a busy hour and expected a quick journey, because the distance wasn't very long. I also had several other things planned for that afternoon.","After a few minutes, the cars began moving very slowly. I spent about half an hour on a journey that was usually much shorter. I couldn't see a clear reason for the delay, so I didn't know when the traffic would improve.","I was driving, which meant I needed to keep paying attention to the road. I tried to stay patient, but I kept thinking about the time I was losing. I was especially annoyed because I had assumed that buying a few groceries would be a simple errand.","When I reached the supermarket, I decided to change my plan for the rest of the afternoon. I bought the things I needed most and left the less urgent tasks for another day. That helped me stop feeling that everything had to happen at once.","The experience wasn't dangerous or dramatic, but it was frustrating. Since then, I've tried to go shopping at a quieter time and leave a little more room in my schedule. It reminded me that a short distance doesn't always mean a short journey."],"keywords":"买菜 → 短途 → 堵车 → 等待 → 耳机替换件","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you were stuck in traffic.","audio":"audio/71d91c81a85aba37.m4a"},{"id":"T070","title":"等待期待已久的东西","category":"经历","masterId":"M24","script":["Something I waited for was a package containing replacement headphones. My original pair had developed a fault, and the shop had agreed to send another pair after checking the problem. I used the headphones for listening practice and work, so I wanted them back quite quickly.","I expected the package by the end of that week, but it took about ten days to arrive. During the wait, I used an older pair which wasn't as comfortable. That wasn't a serious problem, but it reminded me of the replacement whenever I needed to listen to something.","At first, I checked the tracking information several times a day. However, seeing the same update didn't make the delivery any faster. I eventually contacted the shop once, asked for a clearer estimate and then tried to stop checking so often.","When the package arrived, I opened it and tested both sides of the headphones. I was pleased that they worked properly, and I could finally return to my usual listening routine. I also felt relieved that I didn't need another conversation about the fault.","What made the wait frustrating was not knowing exactly when it would end. The experience taught me that a useful update can matter almost as much as a quick delivery. It helped me manage my expectations and spend less time checking."],"keywords":"买菜 → 短途 → 堵车 → 等待 → 耳机替换件","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe something you looked forward to receiving.","audio":"audio/8b4801236fde1183.m4a"},{"id":"T071","title":"帮助别人解决问题","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["A time I helped someone solve a problem was when a colleague had to check the same information repeatedly. It was taking up too much of his day. I asked which part was most difficult and suggested building a simple tool to handle the repeated steps.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was pleased that I could help with a problem that affected his everyday work. The tool didn't remove the need for all checks, but it made the process easier. I also learned that asking careful questions is useful before deciding what kind of help someone needs."],"keywords":"同事困惑 → 我先倾听 → 拆分问题 → 清晰列表 → 减少遗漏","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you helped someone solve a problem.","audio":"audio/6dae6b490a62bf7c.m4a"},{"id":"T072","title":"在公共场所丢失东西","category":"经历","masterId":"M06","script":["One time I lost something was during a visit to a market in the older part of Dubai. I was there with a friend, looking around the small shops and taking a few photographs. The item I lost was my set of keys.","I noticed they were missing when we were about to leave. At first, I thought they must be in another pocket, so I checked my clothes and bag carefully. When I still couldn't find them, I began feeling worried because I needed them to get into my home.","My friend helped me think through where we had been. I remembered taking the keys out while looking for my wallet in one shop. We walked back along the same route and asked a member of staff whether anyone had found them.","Fortunately, someone had noticed the keys on the counter and kept them safely. I described the key ring before the staff member returned them to me. I felt relieved and thanked him, because a small mistake could have caused a much more inconvenient evening.","Afterwards, I put the keys in one specific pocket instead of moving them between my bag and clothes. I also tried to check them before leaving a place. The experience was stressful at the time, but it reminded me that a simple habit can help me avoid the same problem again."],"keywords":"老迪拜市场 → 钥匙不见 → 原路返回 → 店员 → 找回","note":"市场到访、丢钥匙、店员帮忙及找回全部为样例；丢的是钥匙，不是手机。未冒称任何真实商铺的失物流程。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an occasion when you lost something in a public place.","audio":"audio/47a22e37626c06a1.m4a"},{"id":"T073","title":"节约时间的方法","category":"经历","masterId":"M04","script":["A change that helped save time was using a simple tool for a repeated task at work. Before that, my team checked the information manually each time. We still needed to look at the results, but we wanted to avoid repeating every basic step ourselves.","At first, I thought we should create a complete system with lots of features. However, a colleague suggested starting with a simple version. I wasn't fully convinced because I worried it would look unfinished, but we discussed the idea and agreed to test it.","We divided the work between us and focused on the most common problem. I worked on the main function, while another person tested it with a few examples. Our first attempt didn't work properly because we had misunderstood part of the information. We checked the issue together and corrected it.","Eventually, the tool handled the basic task well. It wasn't perfect, but it saved us time and helped us understand what to improve next. Seeing it work was a satisfying moment for me.","I was happy with the decision because we learned something useful without spending weeks on an idea that might not work. The experience changed my opinion about planning. I still think planning matters, but now I prefer to try a small, practical solution before making a bigger commitment."],"keywords":"重复沟通 → 共享列表 → 统一信息 → 减少确认 → 节约时间","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a method you use to save time.","audio":"audio/05cf9f9245e9b0d8.m4a"},{"id":"T074","title":"开心的阅读经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M14","script":["A reading experience that made me happy was finishing an illustrated version of The Tortoise and the Hare by myself in primary school. My father had told me the story before, but reading it without help felt different. I remember sitting beside him and explaining the ending in my own words. He listened patiently, and I felt that I was finally becoming a more independent reader.","The story is about a race between two very different animals. The hare is fast and confident, while the tortoise moves slowly. Because the hare thinks winning will be easy, he stops for a nap. The tortoise keeps going and reaches the finish before him.","As a child, I found the ending funny and surprising. At the beginning, I was certain that the hare would win, so I wanted to turn the pages quickly. I also liked the pictures because they helped me understand what was happening without needing an adult to explain every sentence.","The lesson has stayed with me: steady effort matters, and being good at something doesn't mean you can stop trying. I think of it when I'm learning a skill and comparing myself with people who improve faster. The story reminds me to focus on my own progress. It's simple, but that's probably why I still remember it after so many years."],"keywords":"动物故事 → 故事 → 书（故事集版本） → 开心的阅读经历 → 童年学到的事 → 坚持 → 喜欢的角色","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a reading experience that made you happy.","audio":"audio/a1f81f467de4e652.m4a"},{"id":"T075","title":"在成功公司工作的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["I'd like to talk about Adam, a colleague who works for a successful software company. I've known him for about two years. The company has developed a practical product that helps its customers handle repeated tasks, and Adam works on making the product easier to use.","I think the company has done well because it understands what its customers actually need. It doesn't try to add every possible feature at once. Adam follows the same approach in his own work: he sets a clear goal and keeps the solution simple.","A few months ago, I had to explain a new idea to our team. I knew the details, but I couldn't present them clearly. Adam suggested using one simple example instead of showing everything at once. He also helped me practise and pointed out the parts that were difficult to follow.","The presentation went much better than I expected. People understood the idea, and I felt more confident afterwards. What I appreciate most is that he helped me learn a useful skill rather than just doing the work for me.","Talking to Adam has helped me understand that a successful company needs useful products and people who communicate clearly. I admire his contribution because he pays attention to the person using the product. That is a quality I'd like to develop in my own work."],"keywords":"Adam → 软件公司 → 工作条理 → 服务用户 → 学习","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe someone who works for a successful company.","audio":"audio/4bf724db8153881a.m4a"},{"id":"T076","title":"当地的名人","category":"人物","masterId":"M11","script":["A well-known person in Dubai I'd like to describe is Huda Kattan, the founder of Huda Beauty. I think she's popular because people can connect a recognisable person with the brand. She has shared beauty content as well as built a company, so her public image feels more personal than a business name printed on a shop sign.","Her business began in Dubai in 2013 with false eyelashes. Before that, she worked as a makeup artist and beauty blogger. What interested me was that she didn't begin with a clear plan for a large company. She developed her idea step by step, and the brand eventually expanded beyond Dubai.","I first became interested in her after seeing the brand in a shopping mall. I then read some public articles to learn more. I'm interested in how someone becomes associated with a place through their work, even when the business reaches customers in many other countries.","I'm not especially interested in makeup, but I do enjoy learning how people build businesses. To me, her appeal comes from combining practical knowledge with a way of communicating that people understand. If I had the chance to meet her, I'd ask how she decides which customer suggestions to follow. That's why I find her memorable."],"keywords":"Dubai local celebrity → popular person → successful entrepreneur → overcoming difficulty → ForbesWomen interview → FauxFilter campaign","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a famous person connected with the area where you live.","audio":"audio/1a7144ec0bc1120d.m4a"},{"id":"T077","title":"想购买的科技产品","category":"事物","masterId":"M06","script":["A piece of technology I'd like to buy is a better pair of headphones. I already use a basic pair, but I would like something more comfortable that could reduce distracting background noise. It isn't a phone, and it would serve a clear purpose in my routine.","I often need to concentrate on work or listen to English recordings. When the surroundings are noisy, I find myself repeating the same section because I've missed something. A better pair could make those activities easier, especially in a shared space.","Before buying anything, I would compare a few models and read about their comfort and everyday use. I'd prefer to try them in a shop if possible. The most expensive option wouldn't necessarily be the best one for me.","I plan to save a little money each month instead of buying them immediately. I would also check what help is available if they stop working. My experience with electronic products has taught me that service matters as well as the product itself.","I want them because I expect to use them often, not just because they are new. If they help me work and study with fewer interruptions, I would consider the purchase worthwhile. Until then, I can continue using what I already have."],"keywords":"更好的耳机 → 专注 → 比较性能 → 攒钱 → 计划购买","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a piece of technology you would like to buy.","audio":"audio/0925703942de34c8.m4a"},{"id":"T078","title":"好用的应用或电脑程序","category":"事物","masterId":"M04","script":["A useful app I use at work is a small internal program that our team developed. It brings requests into one shared list, so we can see what needs attention without searching through several different conversations. I helped work on an early version of it.","Before we had the program, requests were spread across messages and emails. It was easy to miss an update or forget who was handling something. Even a simple question could involve looking through old conversations before finding the information we needed.","We started with a basic version instead of trying to build a complete system. The main features were a list of requests, the person responsible for each one and its current status. We tested it with a few examples and corrected the parts that were unclear.","I now use it to check my tasks and update their progress. During team discussions, we can look at the same information rather than explain everything again from memory. It doesn't do the work for us, but it helps us keep track of it.","What I like most is that it solves a problem I actually have. The interface is simple, and I don't need a long explanation each time I open it. For me, useful software makes an ordinary task easier to manage, rather than adding features I rarely need."],"keywords":"内部程序 → 请求列表 → 负责人 → 状态 → 每天使用","note":"团队开发、程序功能和使用效果均为样例。它是目前已在使用的内部程序，不能同时讲成尚未开发或将来想买的App；具体业务功能需与M04实际个人化版本一致。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an application or computer program you find useful.","audio":"audio/9a8a0268e1a88938.m4a"},{"id":"T079","title":"生活必需品（非手机电脑）","category":"事物","masterId":"M06","script":["Something I find difficult to do without is my pair of headphones. They aren't a phone or a computer, but I use them almost every day. They help me concentrate in places with background noise and listen to English recordings without disturbing other people.","I chose a comfortable pair because I knew I would wear them for a while. Before buying them, I compared a few options and saved a little money each month. I wanted something useful, rather than simply buying the most fashionable brand.","When I finally bought them, I was pleased because I had made a deliberate choice rather than buying something on impulse. I started using them regularly for work and language practice.","A few weeks later, one side stopped working properly. I took them back to the shop, expecting a long argument. Instead, the assistant listened carefully, checked the problem and explained the next steps. After confirming the fault, the shop arranged a replacement.","When I couldn't use them, I realised how much they were part of my routine. I could still work and study, but I found it harder to focus and practise listening in a shared space. That's why I think of them as a small but important everyday item."],"keywords":"耳机 → 专注 → 工作学习 → 减少干扰 → 日常需要","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe an essential item in your daily life, other than a phone or computer.","audio":"audio/064de85bc47f69c3.m4a"},{"id":"T080","title":"自己家里放松的角落","category":"地点","masterId":"M20","script":["The place where I like to relax at home is a small corner of my living room. I have a comfortable chair there, with a lamp and a little space beside it for a drink or a book. It isn't a large or impressive area.","I usually sit there after work, once I've finished the things I need to do around the apartment. Sometimes I read a few pages, and sometimes I just sit quietly for a while. I like having an activity that doesn't involve another screen.","I try to keep my work laptop away from that corner. Otherwise, a short break can turn into checking messages and thinking about unfinished tasks. On some evenings, I also leave my phone in another room so that I can properly rest.","One weekend, I spent part of an afternoon there reading a novel. I wasn't following a schedule or trying to finish a certain number of pages. I simply enjoyed being comfortable and having enough time to stay with the story.","What I enjoy most is the feeling of having no urgent task. The space suits the way I relax, even though it is quite simple. Twenty quiet minutes there can make the rest of my evening feel calmer and more separate from work."],"keywords":"自己公寓 → 窗边椅子 → 读书 → 安静 → 休息","note":"","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a spot in your own home where you like to relax.","audio":"audio/a521da2ebdd8964c.m4a"},{"id":"T081","title":"常去但不喜欢的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M24","script":["A place I visit regularly but don't particularly like is the supermarket near my flat in Dubai. I go there about once a week to buy groceries. It's convenient, which is why I keep using it, but the experience is usually quite tiring.","I normally go after work, when quite a few other people have the same idea. The aisles can feel crowded, and there is often a queue at the checkout. I only need a few basic things, but finding them sometimes takes longer than I expect.","The layout is another reason I don't enjoy it. Items occasionally move to a different shelf, so I walk around looking for something I bought easily the previous week. There is also background music and a lot of activity, which makes it hard to relax after a busy day.","I remember one evening when I went in just to buy vegetables, bread and milk. I spent more time waiting to pay than choosing the food. By the time I got home, I felt that a small everyday task had taken up most of my evening.","I still shop there because it is nearby and the prices are reasonable. However, I try to go at quieter times and make a list before I leave. I don't dislike shopping in general; I just prefer an experience where I can find what I need and get home without too much waiting."],"keywords":"附近超市 → 每周买菜 → 拥挤与排队 → 花费时间 → 避开高峰","note":"常去的地点版与不喜欢的短途旅行版分别回答。","scope":"本季汇编训练","prompt_en":"Describe a place you visit regularly but do not particularly like.","audio":"audio/32957cce69237247.m4a"},{"id":"T082","title":"一次观察天空的经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M18","script":["One time I paid close attention to the sky was during an evening visit to Sunset Beach in Dubai. I was there with a friend a few months ago, after a week when we had both spent too much time indoors.","We walked along the sand and found somewhere to sit away from the busier area. At first, we were talking about work, but then we noticed the light beginning to change. We stopped our conversation for a while and looked towards the horizon.","The sky had been quite bright when we arrived. Later, there was orange near the horizon and a little pink above it. The colours were softer than before, and the water reflected some of the light. I liked noticing that change gradually rather than looking up only for a moment.","I took a photograph, but it didn't quite capture what I could see. So I put my phone away and watched for a few more minutes. My friend did the same, and neither of us felt that we needed to speak constantly.","I remember the experience because it was simple and relaxing. It made me realise how often I ignore my surroundings when I'm busy. I'd like to make more time for moments like that, even when I only have a short break."],"keywords":"海边 → 散步 → 傍晚 → 天空 → 放松","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a time you enjoyed looking at the sky.","audio":"audio/1718a3022c036307.m4a"},{"id":"T083","title":"感到特别开心的时刻","category":"经历","masterId":"M08","script":["A moment when I felt extremely happy was near the end of a birthday dinner I organised for my friend Ben. It happened a few months ago at a small restaurant in Dubai. When he saw the cake and heard everyone singing, he looked completely surprised.","I checked when everyone was available and chose a place that was easy for us to reach. Another friend arranged the cake, while I made the reservation and confirmed the time. We also asked him what food he liked so that he would enjoy the meal.","On the evening itself, we arrived a little early and made sure everything was ready. The atmosphere was relaxed. We talked about work, shared some funny stories and took a few photos together.","The most memorable moment was when the cake came out. It was quite simple, but it had a small decoration connected to one of his hobbies. He hadn't expected it, and his reaction made the effort feel worthwhile.","I was pleased that the plan worked and that everyone had a good time. It reminded me that a successful celebration doesn't depend on spending a lot of money. Paying attention to the person and making time for each other can be much more important."],"keywords":"秘密准备 → 朋友生日 → 蛋糕出现 → 大家唱歌 → 看到他的笑容","note":"本题突出开心的具体时刻，其余内容沿用生日主线。","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a moment when you felt especially happy.","audio":"audio/2cefa1a7acc64ba6.m4a"},{"id":"T084","title":"童年值得回忆的学习经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M14","script":["An important lesson I learned as a child was to keep practising instead of comparing myself with other people. My father helped me understand this when I was learning to ride a bicycle in primary school. At the time, I thought I was unusually slow at learning.","Some of my friends could already ride without help, while I kept losing my balance. I became frustrated and wanted to stop trying. My father reminded me of The Tortoise and the Hare, a story he'd told me before. In it, the slow tortoise keeps going and wins while the confident hare takes a nap.","The connection was simple: I didn't have to be the fastest learner to make progress. We practised for a short time each evening on a quiet part of our street. He stayed beside me, and I gradually became more comfortable balancing and turning.","Eventually, I managed to ride a short distance on my own. I was excited, but the bigger change was in how I understood learning. I realised that progress could be slow without being a failure. I still find that lesson useful when I'm studying something difficult or picking up a new skill. It helps me focus on small improvements rather than other people's results."],"keywords":"动物故事 → 故事 → 书（故事集版本） → 开心的阅读经历 → 童年学到的事 → 坚持 → 喜欢的角色","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a memorable learning experience from your childhood.","audio":"audio/9a660ff8792196c9.m4a"},{"id":"T085","title":"感到有信心的时刻","category":"经历","masterId":"M21","script":["A moment when I felt confident was after explaining a new idea to my team in English. It happened a few months ago, during a meeting about a small work project. Before the meeting, I was worried that I would lose my words or confuse people.","I prepared by choosing one main message and a simple example. I also practised saying it aloud, because an explanation that looks clear on a page can still be difficult to say. A colleague helped me notice where I was adding unnecessary details.","When the meeting started, I spoke a little more slowly than usual. I explained the problem first, then used the example to show how the idea could help. I didn't remember every sentence I had practised, but I could still get the main point across.","The change in my confidence came when people began asking useful questions. Their questions showed that they understood the idea, and I could answer without restarting my whole explanation. One colleague also said that the example had made things clearer.","I felt pleased because I had managed something I had been nervous about. The experience didn't mean that speaking English was suddenly easy, but it gave me evidence that preparation and clear language could help me communicate. Since then, I've felt more willing to speak up."],"keywords":"英语 → 长期目标 → 录音 → 表达 → 自信","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a moment when you felt confident.","audio":"audio/adebea3fc893bed4.m4a"},{"id":"T086","title":"改善睡眠或日常作息","category":"经历","masterId":"M05","script":["A change I made to my evening routine was spending less time on my phone before bed. I used to tell myself I was having a short break, but I often kept scrolling until late. The next morning, I sometimes felt rushed and tired.","I decided to make the change small enough to maintain. I chose a time to stop looking at messages and social media, usually about half an hour before I wanted to sleep. I put my phone away from the bed so that it was less tempting to pick it up again.","During that time, I did a few things, such as preparing my clothes for the next day or reading a few pages of a book. I wasn't trying to follow a complicated routine. I mainly wanted the evening to feel as though it was coming to an end.","After a while, I noticed that I was getting into bed earlier more often. On some mornings, I felt more awake and had enough time for breakfast. Those mornings felt less hurried, which made the change feel worthwhile.","I don't manage it perfectly every night, especially when I have something urgent to finish. Still, having a simple stopping point helps me control my time. I like the routine because it gives me a calmer end to the day and a less hurried start the next morning."],"keywords":"刷手机 → 时间过晚 → 提前停 → 早点睡 → 更精神","note":"作息、屏幕时间与第二天状态均为个人感受样例，没有减重、治疗或其他医学断言。它是夜间作息变化，不是把傍晚散步简单改成早起。","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a change that improved your sleeping routine.","audio":"audio/10c97b65751c868a.m4a"},{"id":"T087","title":"一首对你有意义的歌曲","category":"事物","masterId":"M22","script":["A song that has special meaning for me is Happy Birthday to You. It is a familiar song, but I associate it with being remembered and spending time with people I care about. The meaning comes from the occasions rather than a recording.","One evening that stands out was a birthday dinner we arranged for a friend. We had kept the plan simple and met at a place that was convenient for everyone. Towards the end of the meal, someone brought out a cake and we sang.","None of us was a particularly good singer, and we didn't all start at the same moment. However, that made the experience feel relaxed rather than embarrassing. Our friend looked surprised and then started smiling, which made me enjoy the song even more.","What I like about the tune is that it is easy to recognise and join in with. I don't need to concentrate on a complicated performance. I can simply take part and pay attention to the people around me.","I wouldn't put the song on when I'm working or travelling. Still, hearing it at a celebration brings back warm memories. For me, it shows how even a simple piece of music can become meaningful through the experiences connected with it."],"keywords":"熟悉旋律 → 生日晚餐 → 朋友 → 一起唱 → 个人意义","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a song that has a special meaning for you.","audio":"audio/e23efed32999cb3a.m4a"},{"id":"T088","title":"一件喜欢的艺术作品","category":"事物","masterId":"M23","script":["A piece of art I like is a watercolour painting of Dubai Creek that a friend gave me. He enjoys painting in his free time, and he made it after we spent an afternoon walking around the area.","The picture shows a boat on the water, with a row of buildings behind it. The walls are painted in warm, pale colours, while the water has different shades of blue. There are a few soft reflections, which make the scene feel calm rather than completely still.","What caught my attention was that it didn't include every detail. My friend had left out things that weren't important to the scene. That made it easier to notice the boat, the light and the relationship between the colours.","He gave it to me later as a gift. I put it near my desk, where I could see it without it taking up much space. I look at it after a busy day, and it reminds me of our walk and conversation.","I like it partly because of the picture itself, but also because someone I know took the time to make it. I wouldn't try to judge its financial value. For me, its value comes from the memory and the thought behind the gift."],"keywords":"水彩画 → Dubai Creek → 小船 → 暖色 → 朋友礼物","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a piece of art you like.","audio":"audio/1ae689715ef0e538.m4a"},{"id":"T089","title":"一本影响你的书","category":"事物","masterId":"M02","script":["A book that influenced the way I think is The Martian by Andy Weir. It is a science-fiction novel about an astronaut called Mark Watney who is left on Mars and has to find a way to survive. I read it when I wanted something entertaining after work.","The main character is an astronaut called Mark Watney, who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to find ways to stay alive and contact people on Earth. The situation sounds hopeless, but he doesn't give up. He deals with one problem at a time, using whatever resources he has.","What I enjoyed most was the way he thought through his difficulties. The book made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the story enjoyable as well.","I read a little in the evening, and I often continued longer than I had planned because I wanted to know what would happen next. I felt relieved whenever one of his ideas worked.","What influenced me most was his habit of breaking a huge problem into smaller tasks. I sometimes feel overwhelmed by a difficult project, and the story reminds me to work out what I can do next. I don't pretend my problems are as serious as his, but that practical way of thinking has stayed with me."],"keywords":"The Martian → Mark Watney → 生存困境 → 拆小任务 → 工作启发","note":"影响你的书需要讲清个人影响，而不是只复述剧情。","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a book that influenced your thinking.","audio":"audio/485e0012dc779992.m4a"},{"id":"T090","title":"搬家带来的积极变化","category":"经历","masterId":"M20","script":["A change that made my daily life easier was moving into an apartment closer to work. It happened a while ago, when I realised that the time I spent travelling was affecting the rest of my day. I often got home feeling tired.","I compared a few places and tried to think beyond the first impression. The location mattered, but I also needed somewhere within my budget and with enough room for the things I used regularly. I didn't need a particularly large apartment.","Once I had chosen a place, I made a simple plan for moving. I packed the things I didn't use every day first and kept the important items together. A friend helped me carry a few things, which made the day less stressful.","On the first weekend, I unpacked what I needed most and arranged a small place to read. It took a little time before the apartment felt familiar, but I enjoyed deciding how to use the space.","The biggest improvement was having more time in the evening. I could prepare a meal, take a short walk or relax instead of feeling that the whole day had disappeared into work and travel. The move involved some effort, but it suited the routine I wanted to have."],"keywords":"祖母 → 熟悉的家 → 探望 → 距离 → 自己的空间","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a positive change that came from moving home.","audio":"audio/8aa0cb3656cd9037.m4a"},{"id":"T091","title":"有历史感的地方","category":"地点","masterId":"M03","script":["A place with a sense of history that I'd like to describe is Al Fahidi Historical Neighbourhood in old Dubai. I visited it with my friend Adam a few months ago. We wanted a quiet walk somewhere that felt different from the city's newer areas.","The narrow lanes and traditional buildings immediately caught my attention. Instead of rushing between large modern buildings, we could walk slowly and look at small courtyards and the details around us. I liked the feeling of discovering a place one corner at a time.","We spent some time looking around and stopped for a drink at a small cafe. Adam took a few photographs, while I was more interested in how the streets connected. Afterwards, we continued towards the creek and watched the boats crossing the water.","What made the visit enjoyable was the contrast within the same city. I usually associate Dubai with busy roads and tall buildings, but that afternoon gave me a different impression. We didn't need a strict schedule, so there was time to notice things we would normally walk past.","I would like to go back and learn more about the area's history before visiting. I don't know every detail about the buildings, but the neighbourhood made me curious. For me, a historical place is interesting when it helps me imagine how everyday life used to be, rather than simply looking old."],"keywords":"Al Fahidi → 窄巷与庭院 → 慢慢散步 → 迪拜另一面 → 想再了解历史","note":"只使用已核实的历史街区身份；个人参观细节为样例。","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a place that gives you a sense of history.","audio":"audio/e65bf539ae003921.m4a"},{"id":"T092","title":"一次乘坐公共交通的经历","category":"经历","masterId":"M03","script":["A journey I made by public transport was a trip to the area around Dubai Creek with a friend. We used a train for part of the journey and walked the final section. During the outing, we also crossed the creek in a small boat.","I enjoyed being a passenger because I could look around rather than concentrate on driving. We checked the direction before getting on and kept the plan fairly simple. Travelling together made the journey feel like part of the outing, instead of just a way to reach the destination.","The boat crossing was the most memorable part. It was a short journey, but being close to the water gave me a different view of the buildings and the people on the shore. I took a few pictures while my friend pointed out places we could explore next.","We also had a simple drink and talked for a while. The outing didn't cost us much, but I enjoyed it more than some expensive activities I've tried.","I remember feeling relaxed afterwards. It reminded me that I don't always need a complicated plan to have a good day. Sometimes a walk, a friend and a change of surroundings are enough."],"keywords":"Abra → Dubai Creek → 过河 → 看景色 → 实用交通","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a journey you made using public transport.","audio":"audio/e12d04dbe5f8db24.m4a"},{"id":"T093","title":"愿意接纳不同观点的人","category":"人物","masterId":"M01","script":["An open-minded person I know is my colleague Adam. We've worked together for two years, and I appreciate the way he listens when people suggest a different approach. He doesn't seem to feel that he needs to defend his first idea immediately.","One example was a discussion about a small tool our team wanted to build. I was in favour of creating a complete system, while another colleague suggested testing a simple version first. At the beginning, Adam also seemed interested in planning more features in advance.","However, he asked the colleague to explain what we could learn from a small prototype. He listened carefully and asked practical questions about the time involved and how we would check the result. He also made sure that I had a chance to explain my concerns.","After the discussion, he supported trying the smaller version. We agreed on one basic task, tested it with a few examples and used the results to decide what to do next. The approach gave us useful information before we committed more time to the project.","What impressed me was that Adam changed his view after considering the explanation. He didn't simply agree to avoid an argument. His questions showed that he was thinking seriously about the idea. I enjoy working with him because different opinions can become something useful instead of making the conversation uncomfortable."],"keywords":"Adam → 不同意见 → 小原型 → 试验 → 接受结果","note":"Adam、认识方式、团队讨论及原型结果全部为样例。主体是他如何认真听取不同观点，并用具体行为证明思想开放；不只是夸他聪明或乐观。","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a person who is willing to consider different views.","audio":"audio/07721c8310f388d5.m4a"},{"id":"T094","title":"家乡的一处公共场所","category":"地点","masterId":"M17","script":["A public place I like in my hometown is the area around West Lake in Hangzhou. When I am there, I enjoy walking along the paths beside the lake, especially when I want a break from a busy routine.","We spent an afternoon walking along the paths beside the lake. What I remember most is the space around the water. There were trees beside the path, and we could stop whenever we noticed a view we liked. I took a few photos, but I also put my phone away for part of the walk.","At one point, we sat down and watched the light change on the water. We talked about ordinary things and didn't feel that we had to keep moving to another attraction. Afterwards, we found somewhere nearby to have a simple meal.","For me, the lake is important because it gives people a place to enjoy being outdoors while visiting a city. I liked the balance between walking, looking around and having time to talk.","I'd happily go back, especially with someone who enjoys a slower kind of holiday. Next time, I'd leave more time to explore Hangzhou beyond the lake, rather than trying to fit everything into one afternoon."],"keywords":"杭州 → 西湖 → 湖边步道 → 和朋友散步 → 放松","note":"家乡暂以杭州作完整样例；请把整篇地点和经历改成你的真实家乡。","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a public place you like in your hometown.","audio":"audio/b49bc18244f4e716.m4a"},{"id":"T095","title":"喜欢的电影","category":"事物","masterId":"M02","script":["I'd like to talk about a film called The Martian. I watched it at home with a friend a few months ago. Matt Damon plays an astronaut who is accidentally left behind on Mars. The mixture of an unusual setting and practical problem-solving appealed to me.","The main character is an astronaut called Mark Watney, who is accidentally left behind on Mars. He has to find ways to stay alive and contact people on Earth. The situation sounds hopeless, but he doesn't give up. He deals with one problem at a time, using whatever resources he has.","What I enjoyed most was seeing how the character responded to each new difficulty. The film made me feel as if I was following his attempts step by step. Some parts were tense, but his sense of humour made the experience enjoyable as well.","I particularly liked the landscape and the way the acting conveyed his loneliness. My friend and I kept wondering how we would behave in that situation. Afterwards, we talked about which part of the story had made us feel most nervous.","The story also gave me a useful reminder: a big problem becomes less frightening when you focus on the next small action. I think that's why it stayed with me. I'd recommend it to someone who enjoys a hopeful story with a clever main character."],"keywords":"The Martian电影 → Mars → Watney → 解决问题 → 希望","note":"","scope":"补充训练","prompt_en":"Describe a film you enjoyed.","audio":"audio/ccaeca71d83c1f3b.m4a"}],"part1":[{"id":"P101","topic":"工作学习","questions":[{"q":"What takes up most of your time at work?","a":"I'm a software developer, and most of my time goes into building business applications. I enjoy solving practical problems with my team, especially when a small change makes somebody's daily work easier.","q_zh":"你在工作中花时间最多的事情是什么？"},{"q":"What would you like to learn alongside your job?","a":"I'd like to improve my spoken English and learn more about designing useful products. I can already explain technical details, but I want to communicate my ideas more clearly to people outside my field.","q_zh":"在工作之余，你还想学习什么？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/4cad7a13bc110bde.m4a"},{"id":"P102","topic":"住处","questions":[{"q":"Which part of your home do you use the most?","a":"I spend a lot of time in my living room because it's where I read, watch films and occasionally work on my laptop. I keep a comfortable chair by the window.","q_zh":"你在家里最常使用哪个区域？"},{"q":"What would you change about your home if you could?","a":"I'd add a little more storage near the entrance. My shoes and bags sometimes end up on the floor, so a simple cabinet would make the apartment easier to keep tidy.","q_zh":"如果可以，你想对自己的住处做什么改变？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/a3adbf8f6c2b68c8.m4a"},{"id":"P103","topic":"家乡","questions":[{"q":"What would you show a visitor in your hometown?","a":"My hometown is Hangzhou, and I'd take a visitor for a walk near West Lake. It's a pleasant way to see the city, especially if we stop for tea afterwards.","q_zh":"如果有人来你的家乡，你会带他看些什么？"},{"q":"Which memory makes you feel connected to your hometown?","a":"I remember riding my bike around the neighbourhood with my childhood friend Ben. We often stopped at a small shop for snacks, and those ordinary afternoons still make the place feel familiar.","q_zh":"哪段回忆让你觉得自己与家乡有联系？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/9a28031c0cfd3c02.m4a"},{"id":"P104","topic":"生活区域","questions":[{"q":"What makes your neighbourhood convenient for you?","a":"There are a supermarket and a small coffee shop within walking distance of my apartment. I can buy groceries or meet a friend without arranging a long trip, which saves time.","q_zh":"你所在的社区有哪些让生活便利的地方？"},{"q":"Where do you go when you want a break nearby?","a":"I usually walk to a quiet spot near my building or visit a local coffee shop. Getting outside for half an hour helps me relax after spending most of the day indoors.","q_zh":"你想在附近放松一下时，通常会去哪里？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/05170f19f16038e6.m4a"},{"id":"P105","topic":"迪拜","questions":[{"q":"What do you enjoy about living in Dubai?","a":"I enjoy meeting people from different backgrounds. At work and in everyday life, I hear several languages and encounter different habits, so a normal conversation can teach me something new.","q_zh":"住在迪拜，你喜欢哪些方面？"},{"q":"How has living in Dubai changed your routine?","a":"I've become more careful about when I go outside. During hot weather, I prefer walking early in the morning or after sunset, and I plan longer outdoor activities around cooler days.","q_zh":"住在迪拜如何改变了你的日常生活？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/01a59dbf97cb6e40.m4a"},{"id":"P106","topic":"旅行","questions":[{"q":"What sort of trip would you choose for a short holiday?","a":"I'd choose somewhere with interesting streets, good food and a few quiet places to walk. I don't need a packed schedule; I'd rather explore one area properly than rush between attractions.","q_zh":"如果有一个短假期，你会选择什么样的旅行？"},{"q":"What helps you enjoy a long journey?","a":"I download a few podcasts and bring comfortable headphones. If I'm travelling with a friend, we also talk about the places we'd like to visit, which makes the journey feel shorter.","q_zh":"什么能让你更享受一段长途旅程？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/b4882754d3d343d0.m4a"},{"id":"P107","topic":"回收","questions":[{"q":"Which things do you try to recycle at home?","a":"I try to separate cardboard boxes and plastic bottles from other rubbish. Online shopping creates quite a lot of packaging, so I flatten the boxes first to keep the recycling area tidy.","q_zh":"你在家里会尽量回收哪些东西？"},{"q":"What makes recycling difficult in daily life?","a":"The main problem is knowing what each collection point accepts. If the instructions are unclear, I hesitate. Clear labels near the bins would help me sort things correctly and make it a habit.","q_zh":"日常生活中，什么会让回收变得困难？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/460ec1006bf48ac4.m4a"},{"id":"P108","topic":"疲劳","questions":[{"q":"When do you tend to feel mentally tired?","a":"I feel mentally tired after several meetings followed by detailed coding work. Even if I haven't moved much, concentrating for hours can wear me out, so I take a short walk afterwards.","q_zh":"你通常在什么时候会感到精神疲惫？"},{"q":"What helps you recover after a tiring day?","a":"A simple dinner and a quiet evening usually help. I put my phone aside, listen to music and try to sleep at a sensible time instead of staying online late.","q_zh":"忙碌劳累一天后，什么能帮助你恢复精力？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/692ae5c354446ab2.m4a"},{"id":"P109","topic":"鞋","questions":[{"q":"What matters most when you choose a pair of shoes?","a":"Comfort matters most because I often walk when running errands. I prefer simple trainers that match different clothes, and I try them on properly instead of choosing only by appearance.","q_zh":"你挑选鞋子时，最看重什么？"},{"q":"Have your preferences in shoes changed over time?","a":"When I was younger, I paid more attention to the style. Now I think about how my feet feel after a long day, so I usually choose lighter, more comfortable shoes.","q_zh":"随着时间推移，你对鞋子的喜好发生过变化吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/d4d3f97ea8e4b348.m4a"},{"id":"P110","topic":"礼貌","questions":[{"q":"What does being polite look like in your daily life?","a":"For me, it means listening without interrupting, saying thank you and being considerate in shared spaces. Small things, like lowering my voice in a café, can make other people more comfortable.","q_zh":"在你的日常生活中，有礼貌具体表现在哪些方面？"},{"q":"Who helped you develop polite habits as a child?","a":"My parents taught me to greet people and thank them when they helped me. They also reminded me to return borrowed things promptly, which made politeness feel practical rather than formal.","q_zh":"你小时候，谁帮助你养成了礼貌的习惯？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/7aff8303be1b3853.m4a"},{"id":"P111","topic":"蔬果","questions":[{"q":"How do you fit fruit and vegetables into your meals?","a":"I usually add vegetables to dinner and keep easy snacks like apples or bananas at home. If they're already washed and ready, I'm much more likely to eat them during a busy day.","q_zh":"你如何在日常饮食中加入水果和蔬菜？"},{"q":"Were there vegetables you avoided when you were younger?","a":"I disliked carrots when I was a child, especially when they were boiled. Later, I tried them roasted and found the taste much better, so I eat them more often now.","q_zh":"你年纪较小时，有哪些蔬菜是不愿意吃的？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/cb511762d1307a29.m4a"},{"id":"P112","topic":"广告","questions":[{"q":"What kind of advertisement is likely to catch your attention?","a":"I notice advertisements that show a clear use for a product. A short demonstration of how something works is more interesting to me than a famous face with no explanation.","q_zh":"什么样的广告容易吸引你的注意？"},{"q":"How do you react when the same advertisement keeps appearing?","a":"I usually stop paying attention after a while. If it interrupts a video repeatedly, I may skip it immediately, even when the product itself seems useful. Too much repetition becomes annoying.","q_zh":"同一个广告不断出现时，你会有什么反应？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/2061687c6aba9c49.m4a"},{"id":"P113","topic":"纸","questions":[{"q":"When do you still find paper useful?","a":"I find paper useful when I'm planning something complicated. Drawing a rough diagram or making a short list helps me see the whole idea without switching between different windows on a screen.","q_zh":"你在什么情况下仍然觉得纸很有用？"},{"q":"What did you enjoy making with paper as a child?","a":"I used to make paper planes with Ben after school. We tried different shapes and compared how far they flew. It was a cheap activity, but we took the competition quite seriously.","q_zh":"你小时候喜欢用纸做些什么？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/1c360b46c06276d1.m4a"},{"id":"P114","topic":"中学","questions":[{"q":"Which part of secondary school do you remember most clearly?","a":"I remember the lunch breaks because they gave us time to talk without worrying about lessons. Ben and I often discussed films or planned what we'd do together after school.","q_zh":"你对中学生活的哪个部分记得最清楚？"},{"q":"Was there a school subject that became easier with practice?","a":"English became easier once I started reading short articles outside class. At first, I looked up almost every unfamiliar word, but gradually I could follow the meaning without stopping so often.","q_zh":"你上学时，有没有哪门科目是通过练习逐渐学得更轻松的？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/09fed7186fdc623f.m4a"},{"id":"P115","topic":"名字","questions":[{"q":"What do you like about the name you use in English?","a":"I use the English name Marshall. I like that it's easy to introduce myself with it in international settings. It also feels familiar now because colleagues and friends use it regularly.","q_zh":"你喜欢自己所用英文名字的哪些方面？"},{"q":"How do you remember the name of someone you've just met?","a":"I try to use the person's name once during the conversation and connect it with something we discussed. If I'm unsure later, I'd rather ask politely than keep guessing.","q_zh":"你如何记住刚认识的人的名字？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/c2ee54d172a972ee.m4a"},{"id":"P116","topic":"音乐","questions":[{"q":"What kind of music suits your usual working day?","a":"I like quiet instrumental music when I'm doing routine work. Songs with strong lyrics can distract me, so I save those for travelling or relaxing when I can pay more attention.","q_zh":"什么样的音乐适合你平时工作时听？"},{"q":"Has a song ever reminded you of a particular time?","a":"Yes, some songs remind me of journeys with friends. When I hear them again, I remember the conversations and places we visited, even if I haven't thought about that trip for months.","q_zh":"有没有一首歌曾让你想起某段时光？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/6889345c7825bff7.m4a"},{"id":"P117","topic":"老师","questions":[{"q":"What made a teacher memorable to you?","a":"My secondary-school English teacher made lessons feel manageable. She asked us to describe real experiences instead of only memorising rules, and she corrected mistakes in a way that didn't embarrass anyone.","q_zh":"某位老师的什么特点曾让你印象深刻？"},{"q":"Would you enjoy being a teacher yourself?","a":"I'd enjoy teaching a practical skill, such as basic coding, because I like explaining how things work. However, managing a full classroom every day would require more patience and experience than I currently have.","q_zh":"如果你自己当老师，你会喜欢吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/1533c371e9319d44.m4a"},{"id":"P118","topic":"社媒","questions":[{"q":"What do you mainly use social media for?","a":"I mainly use it to keep up with friends and find interesting articles or short videos. I rarely post long updates, but I sometimes share a photograph from a trip.","q_zh":"你主要用社交媒体做什么？"},{"q":"How do you stop social media from taking up too much time?","a":"I try not to open it while I'm working, and I put my phone away before bed. If I keep scrolling without a purpose, I remind myself what I originally wanted to check.","q_zh":"你如何避免社交媒体占用太多时间？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/4726abb54aae6c77.m4a"},{"id":"P119","topic":"整洁","questions":[{"q":"Which area do you make the most effort to keep tidy?","a":"I make the most effort with my desk because clutter distracts me when I'm working. I put cables and small items in a drawer and clear away empty cups before starting.","q_zh":"你最用心保持哪个区域的整洁？"},{"q":"Were you as tidy when you were a child?","a":"Not really. I left books and toys wherever I finished using them. My parents often had to remind me to clean up, but I became more organised when I started sharing space with others.","q_zh":"你小时候也像现在这样爱整洁吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/93fa5e410d60230c.m4a"},{"id":"P120","topic":"网站","questions":[{"q":"What makes a website useful enough for you to revisit?","a":"A useful website gives me clear information without making me search through too many pages. I often return to technical documentation because the examples help me solve problems at work.","q_zh":"一个网站有哪些特点，才会让你觉得有用并再次访问？"},{"q":"Have you learned a practical skill through a website?","a":"Yes, I learned how to prepare a simple dish by following a cooking website. The instructions included photographs at each stage, which helped me understand what the food should look like.","q_zh":"你曾经通过网站学会过一项实用技能吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/4d366c43f6a919c1.m4a"},{"id":"P121","topic":"手表","questions":[{"q":"When is wearing a watch useful for you?","a":"A watch is useful when I'm outside or in a meeting and want to check the time quickly. It saves me from looking at my phone and getting distracted by notifications.","q_zh":"在什么情况下，戴手表对你很有用？"},{"q":"Would you spend a lot of money on a watch?","a":"Probably not. I'd choose something comfortable and reliable rather than very expensive. I can appreciate a well-designed watch, but I would rather spend extra money on travel or a useful device.","q_zh":"你会花很多钱买一块手表吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/00bad63d64b760ce.m4a"},{"id":"P122","topic":"购物","questions":[{"q":"How do you decide whether to buy something online?","a":"I compare the size, price and return conditions before ordering. For things like headphones, I also read a few detailed reviews because photographs alone don't tell me how comfortable a product is.","q_zh":"你如何决定是否在网上购买某件东西？"},{"q":"Do you prefer shopping alone or with someone else?","a":"I prefer going alone when I know exactly what I need. If I'm choosing a gift, I enjoy taking a friend because a second opinion can help me avoid an unsuitable choice.","q_zh":"你喜欢独自购物，还是和别人一起购物？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/90228df439e8c690.m4a"},{"id":"P123","topic":"汽车","questions":[{"q":"What do you enjoy about travelling by car?","a":"I like the flexibility, especially when travelling with friends or carrying several bags. We can leave at a convenient time and stop along the way without following somebody else's schedule.","q_zh":"你喜欢乘车出行的哪些方面？"},{"q":"How do you usually handle being stuck in traffic?","a":"I try to stay patient and listen to a podcast if it's safe to do so. Getting frustrated doesn't help, so I allow extra time when I know a journey may be busy.","q_zh":"遇到堵车时，你通常如何应对？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/a638ad5f2ecb846f.m4a"},{"id":"P124","topic":"公园","questions":[{"q":"What would you do during a quiet afternoon in a park?","a":"I'd walk for a while and then sit somewhere shaded with a book. I enjoy having space around me, and I don't need an organised activity to feel that the visit was worthwhile.","q_zh":"如果在公园度过一个安静的下午，你会做些什么？"},{"q":"Did parks play a part in your childhood?","a":"Yes, I often went to a local park with Ben. We rode our bikes and made up simple games. It was a place where we could spend an afternoon without needing much money.","q_zh":"公园曾是你童年生活的一部分吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/b2d4472b5f94d607.m4a"},{"id":"P125","topic":"科学","questions":[{"q":"Which area of science would you like to understand better?","a":"I'd like to understand astronomy better because I find space fascinating. I know a few basic ideas, but I'd enjoy learning how scientists study objects that are so far away.","q_zh":"你想进一步了解哪个科学领域？"},{"q":"How do you encounter science outside the classroom?","a":"I encounter it through technology, cooking and short documentaries. For example, learning why bread rises makes an ordinary kitchen activity more interesting, and it helps me understand what went wrong when a recipe fails.","q_zh":"你在课堂之外如何接触科学？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/28c68625fb8c47f7.m4a"},{"id":"P126","topic":"镜子","questions":[{"q":"When do you usually use a mirror during the day?","a":"I usually check a mirror before leaving home to make sure my clothes and hair look presentable. I don't spend very long on it, but it's part of getting ready.","q_zh":"你一天中通常在什么时候照镜子？"},{"q":"Would you use mirrors to decorate your home?","a":"Yes, I'd consider a simple mirror near the entrance. It would be useful before going out, and it could make the space feel brighter without taking up much room.","q_zh":"你会用镜子来装饰自己的住处吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/75d480f22a608826.m4a"},{"id":"P127","topic":"星空","questions":[{"q":"What attracts your attention when you look at the night sky?","a":"I notice the moon first because it's easy to see and its shape changes over time. If I'm somewhere darker, I also enjoy trying to recognise a few stars.","q_zh":"你看夜空时，什么会吸引你的注意？"},{"q":"Would you like to learn more about space in the future?","a":"Yes, I'd like to understand how telescopes help scientists study distant objects. A beginner's course or a well-made documentary would suit me because I want clear explanations before going into technical details.","q_zh":"你将来想进一步了解太空吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/76473fce20b58b45.m4a"},{"id":"P128","topic":"唱歌","questions":[{"q":"In what situations do you find yourself singing?","a":"I sometimes sing quietly when I'm cooking or travelling alone. I usually follow a song I already know, and I enjoy it more when I'm not worrying about how I sound.","q_zh":"你通常在什么情况下会不自觉地唱起歌来？"},{"q":"Would you feel comfortable singing in front of friends?","a":"I'd feel comfortable in a relaxed group, especially if everyone joined in. Singing alone in front of an audience would make me nervous, so I'd need some practice before trying that.","q_zh":"在朋友面前唱歌，你会觉得自在吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/c5b6d4e162786f30.m4a"},{"id":"P129","topic":"衣服","questions":[{"q":"How do you choose what to wear on an ordinary day?","a":"I usually choose simple clothes that are comfortable and easy to combine. For work, I want to look presentable, but I don't enjoy spending a long time deciding what to wear.","q_zh":"平常的一天，你如何选择穿什么？"},{"q":"Do you keep clothes that you no longer wear?","a":"I used to keep too many, especially items that didn't fit well. Now I check my wardrobe occasionally and give away things in good condition, which makes it easier to find what I need.","q_zh":"你会保留那些已经不再穿的衣服吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/419321081b44e346.m4a"},{"id":"P130","topic":"喜剧","questions":[{"q":"What kind of humour do you enjoy in a programme?","a":"I enjoy humour based on ordinary situations, like misunderstandings between friends or small problems at work. It feels relatable, and it doesn't need to be loud or cruel to make me laugh.","q_zh":"你喜欢节目中什么样的幽默？"},{"q":"Do you and your friends have a similar sense of humour?","a":"Ben and I often laugh at the same things because we've known each other since childhood. A small comment can remind us of an old situation, even when nobody else understands the joke.","q_zh":"你和朋友的幽默感相似吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/5f048c7cd496e48f.m4a"},{"id":"P131","topic":"耳机","questions":[{"q":"When are headphones especially useful to you?","a":"They're useful when I'm travelling or listening to something while other people are nearby. I can enjoy a podcast without disturbing anyone, and comfortable headphones make a long journey more pleasant.","q_zh":"耳机在什么情况下对你特别有用？"},{"q":"Are there times when you prefer not to wear headphones?","a":"I take them off when somebody is speaking to me or when I need to pay attention to my surroundings. For example, I prefer hearing what's happening when I'm crossing a busy road.","q_zh":"有没有什么时候你更愿意不戴耳机？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/823a9c56ccd1d91e.m4a"},{"id":"P132","topic":"无聊","questions":[{"q":"What sort of activity makes you lose interest quickly?","a":"I get bored when I have to wait with nothing useful to do. If a queue moves slowly, I may read a short article, but I'd still prefer the process to be more efficient.","q_zh":"什么样的活动会让你很快失去兴趣？"},{"q":"What did you do when you felt bored as a child?","a":"I usually called Ben or went outside with my bike. If the weather was bad, we made things from paper or cardboard. Having somebody to share an activity with made a big difference.","q_zh":"你小时候感到无聊时，会做些什么？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/0fca4afea60a2086.m4a"},{"id":"P133","topic":"电脑","questions":[{"q":"What task would be difficult for you without a computer?","a":"My work would be difficult because I use a computer to write code, test applications and communicate with my team. A phone is useful for messages, but it couldn't replace that setup.","q_zh":"如果没有电脑，哪项任务会让你觉得很难完成？"},{"q":"What would you look for when buying your next computer?","a":"I'd look for reliable performance, a comfortable keyboard and a screen that doesn't strain my eyes. Portability would matter too, but I wouldn't choose the lightest model if it made daily work uncomfortable.","q_zh":"下次买电脑时，你会看重哪些方面？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/fbc2800c0be86215.m4a"},{"id":"P134","topic":"收集","questions":[{"q":"Is there anything small that you like keeping over time?","a":"I keep a few postcards and tickets from trips. I don't try to build a valuable collection; I like them because they remind me of places, people and small moments I enjoyed.","q_zh":"有没有什么小物件是你喜欢长期保留的？"},{"q":"Did you collect anything when you were younger?","a":"I collected stickers for a while when I was at school. Ben and I traded the ones we had twice. I eventually lost interest, but comparing our collections was enjoyable at the time.","q_zh":"你年纪较小时收集过什么东西吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/9eae5b496890cc5a.m4a"},{"id":"P135","topic":"市场","questions":[{"q":"What would encourage you to visit a street market?","a":"I'd go for fresh food, small local products and the chance to walk around. I enjoy seeing several stalls together, especially when I'm visiting a place and want to understand its everyday life.","q_zh":"什么会吸引你去逛街头市场？"},{"q":"How does shopping at a market feel different from a supermarket?","a":"A market feels more personal because I can ask the seller about an item directly. A supermarket is usually easier when I'm in a hurry, since the layout and prices are more predictable.","q_zh":"在市场购物和在超市购物，感觉有什么不同？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/531d5878fffc2674.m4a"},{"id":"P136","topic":"抱负","questions":[{"q":"What is a personal goal you're currently working towards?","a":"I'm working towards speaking English more confidently. I practise short answers aloud and record myself occasionally. I'd like to explain my ideas smoothly in conversations, especially when I haven't prepared every sentence.","q_zh":"你目前正在努力实现什么个人目标？"},{"q":"Have your ambitions changed since childhood?","a":"Yes. When I was younger, I mainly imagined having an impressive job title. Now I care more about doing useful work, learning steadily and having enough time for people and activities I enjoy.","q_zh":"你的抱负与小时候相比发生过变化吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/c440c9ff01bfee44.m4a"},{"id":"P137","topic":"历史","questions":[{"q":"What helps you become interested in a historical topic?","a":"A personal story helps me become interested. Ben once showed me his grandfather's old photographs and explained how the neighbourhood had changed. That made history feel connected to real people's lives.","q_zh":"什么会让你对一个历史话题产生兴趣？"},{"q":"Would you choose to learn history through reading or visiting places?","a":"I'd choose a combination. Reading gives me the background, but visiting a museum or an old street makes the details easier to remember. I enjoy comparing what I've read with what I can see.","q_zh":"你会选择通过阅读还是实地参观来学习历史？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/a063d2f90a4096d8.m4a"},{"id":"P138","topic":"电影","questions":[{"q":"What makes you decide to watch a particular film?","a":"I usually look at the story and a few reviews rather than choosing only by the actors. If a friend recommends something and explains why they enjoyed it, I'm more likely to try it.","q_zh":"什么会让你决定看某一部电影？"},{"q":"Do you enjoy watching a film again after some time?","a":"Yes, especially if I enjoyed the characters or didn't fully understand the story the first time. A second viewing lets me notice smaller details without worrying about what will happen next.","q_zh":"隔一段时间后，你喜欢再看一遍同一部电影吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/06a7531066989a66.m4a"},{"id":"P139","topic":"旧建筑","questions":[{"q":"What interests you about an old building?","a":"I like noticing the materials, windows and small details that are different from modern buildings. They make me wonder how people used the space and what everyday life was like at the time.","q_zh":"一栋老建筑的哪些方面会让你感兴趣？"},{"q":"Would you prefer an old home or a modern one?","a":"For living, I'd probably choose a modern home because maintenance and comfort matter to me. I enjoy visiting older buildings, but I wouldn't want to deal with frequent repairs in my own apartment.","q_zh":"你更愿意住在老房子还是现代住宅里？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/824327df7da2c324.m4a"},{"id":"P140","topic":"晚上","questions":[{"q":"What does a pleasant evening at home look like for you?","a":"A pleasant evening usually includes a simple meal, some music and time away from work. I might read or watch a film, but I try not to fill every quiet moment with my phone.","q_zh":"对你来说，一个愉快的居家夜晚是什么样的？"},{"q":"Do your weekend evenings differ from weekday evenings?","a":"Yes, I'm more likely to meet friends or stay out a little later at the weekend. On weekdays, I prefer a calm routine because I need to be ready for work the next morning.","q_zh":"你的周末夜晚和平日夜晚有什么不同吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/d045a34f08efefd2.m4a"},{"id":"P141","topic":"晨间","questions":[{"q":"Which part of your morning routine do you value most?","a":"I value having a few quiet minutes before checking messages. Making breakfast and looking at the day's main tasks helps me feel prepared, instead of starting the morning by reacting to everything at once.","q_zh":"你最重视晨间习惯中的哪个环节？"},{"q":"Was getting up early easy for you when you were younger?","a":"It wasn't always easy, especially after school holidays. I often stayed up later than usual and struggled with the alarm. Having a fixed bedtime helped once the school term started again.","q_zh":"你年纪较小时，早起对你来说容易吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/ee94299834e56753.m4a"},{"id":"P142","topic":"体育节目","questions":[{"q":"What keeps you interested when watching sport on television?","a":"I enjoy a close match when the result is uncertain until the end. Watching with friends makes it more exciting because we discuss the players' decisions and react together to important moments.","q_zh":"在电视上看体育比赛时，什么能让你保持兴趣？"},{"q":"Would you rather watch sport at home or at the venue?","a":"For convenience, I'd choose home because I can see the action clearly and avoid the journey. However, I'd like to attend an important match occasionally to experience the atmosphere in person.","q_zh":"你更愿意在家看体育比赛，还是去现场看？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/a89c6ac7aa1c1efc.m4a"},{"id":"P143","topic":"失物","questions":[{"q":"What would you do first if you realised you'd lost something?","a":"I'd stop and think about where I last used it, then retrace my steps if possible. For something important, I'd contact the place I visited rather than immediately assuming it was stolen.","q_zh":"如果发现自己丢了东西，你首先会做什么？"},{"q":"How would you deal with an item someone else had left behind?","a":"I'd hand it to a responsible member of staff or the appropriate lost-property desk. I'd prefer it to be stored safely where the owner might look, rather than taking it home with me.","q_zh":"如果发现别人遗落的物品，你会如何处理？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/66b168cfb14e1379.m4a"},{"id":"P144","topic":"艺术","questions":[{"q":"What kind of artwork do you find easy to connect with?","a":"I connect most easily with pictures of familiar places or everyday life. I don't need to understand every technique, but I enjoy recognising a mood or detail that reminds me of my own experiences.","q_zh":"什么样的艺术作品容易让你产生共鸣？"},{"q":"Would you like to spend more time making art?","a":"Yes, I'd like to try simple sketching. It would give me something to do away from a screen, and I wouldn't need expensive equipment. I'd start by drawing ordinary objects around my home.","q_zh":"你想花更多时间进行艺术创作吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/a144eb99e5891207.m4a"},{"id":"P145","topic":"机会","questions":[{"q":"What would make you accept a new opportunity?","a":"I'd accept it if it gave me a useful skill or a chance to work with people I could learn from. I'd also check whether I had enough time to take it seriously.","q_zh":"什么会让你决定接受一个新机会？"},{"q":"Have you ever hesitated before trying something new?","a":"Yes, I hesitated before giving a short presentation at work because I was worried about making mistakes. Preparing a few clear points helped, and the experience made the next presentation feel less intimidating.","q_zh":"你在尝试新事物之前，曾经犹豫过吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/146022d62e96d850.m4a"},{"id":"P146","topic":"休息日","questions":[{"q":"How do you usually spend a day with no work planned?","a":"I like starting slowly, having breakfast without rushing and going out for a walk. Later, I might meet a friend or visit Alex's coffee shop, but I leave some time unplanned.","q_zh":"没有安排工作的日子，你通常如何度过？"},{"q":"Would you rather stay home or go out on a day off?","a":"I'd usually do a little of both. Going out helps me feel refreshed, while a quiet afternoon at home gives me time to read or finish small tasks without watching the clock.","q_zh":"休息日，你更愿意待在家里还是外出？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/b81a49d3c25981e0.m4a"},{"id":"P147","topic":"梦境","questions":[{"q":"Do you tend to remember what you dreamed about?","a":"I remember a dream occasionally, usually if I wake up during it. The details often disappear quickly, though, so by breakfast I may only remember a place or a strong feeling.","q_zh":"你通常能记住自己梦到了什么吗？"},{"q":"Would you ever tell a friend about an unusual dream?","a":"Yes, if it was funny or included somebody we both knew. I wouldn't treat it as a prediction, but it could start an entertaining conversation, especially with a close friend like Ben.","q_zh":"如果做了一个不寻常的梦，你会告诉朋友吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/69f7fb9782fc8d98.m4a"},{"id":"P148","topic":"钥匙","questions":[{"q":"What helps you keep track of your keys?","a":"I keep them in the same small tray near the entrance when I get home. That simple habit saves me from searching through bags or pockets when I'm trying to leave quickly.","q_zh":"什么能帮助你记住钥匙放在哪里？"},{"q":"Have you ever had an inconvenient experience involving keys?","a":"Once, I thought I'd lost my keys just before leaving home. I checked several places and eventually found them in yesterday's jacket. Since then, I've tried to put them away immediately.","q_zh":"你曾经遇到过与钥匙有关的麻烦吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/d3d8b63eed6157a9.m4a"},{"id":"P149","topic":"花草","questions":[{"q":"Would you like to have plants where you live?","a":"Yes, I'd like a couple of easy plants near the window. They would make the room feel more pleasant, but I'd choose something manageable because I sometimes forget small household tasks during busy weeks.","q_zh":"你想在自己的住处养些植物吗？"},{"q":"What would make flowers a suitable gift for you?","a":"Flowers would be a nice gift for a celebration or when visiting someone's home. I'd choose a simple arrangement rather than something enormous, especially if the person had limited space to display it.","q_zh":"在什么情况下，鲜花会是适合送给你的礼物？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/c704f8ac3cd6421f.m4a"},{"id":"P150","topic":"亲戚","questions":[{"q":"Which relative do you enjoy talking with?","a":"I enjoy talking with my cousin Sara because she's thoughtful and curious. She's interested in becoming a nurse, so our conversations often include her plans, volunteer experiences and what she's learning.","q_zh":"你喜欢和哪位亲戚聊天？"},{"q":"How do you keep in touch with relatives who live far away?","a":"We mainly use messages and occasional video calls. A quick photograph or short update helps us stay connected between longer conversations, and we try to make time for family gatherings when possible.","q_zh":"你如何与住得很远的亲戚保持联系？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/71caf20bd06a1a51.m4a"},{"id":"P151","topic":"颜色","questions":[{"q":"Which colours do you tend to choose for everyday things?","a":"I often choose blue, grey or other simple colours for clothes and bags. They combine easily, so I don't have to spend much time thinking about whether different items match.","q_zh":"你为日常用品挑选颜色时，通常会选哪些颜色？"},{"q":"Would you use a bright colour anywhere in your home?","a":"I'd use a bright colour in a small detail, like a cushion or a picture. I prefer calm colours for large surfaces, but one colourful item can make a room feel more lively.","q_zh":"你会在家中某个地方使用鲜艳的颜色吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/580da1d099e9a8c2.m4a"},{"id":"P152","topic":"地理","questions":[{"q":"What kind of geographical information do you find useful?","a":"I find information about distance, climate and transport useful when planning a trip. It helps me choose where to stay, what to pack and whether I can comfortably explore a place on foot.","q_zh":"你觉得哪类地理信息有用？"},{"q":"Did you enjoy using maps when you were at school?","a":"Yes, I liked comparing places on a map and seeing how far apart they were. It made unfamiliar countries feel easier to imagine, especially when a teacher connected the map with a real story.","q_zh":"你上学时喜欢使用地图吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/eeb34dba008c7864.m4a"},{"id":"P153","topic":"守时","questions":[{"q":"How do you make sure you arrive at an appointment on time?","a":"I check the route in advance and leave a little extra time for unexpected delays. For an important appointment, I also set a reminder so I don't become absorbed in another task.","q_zh":"你如何确保自己准时赴约？"},{"q":"How do you feel when somebody keeps you waiting?","a":"A short delay doesn't bother me if the person lets me know. What frustrates me is having no update, because I can't decide whether to keep waiting or change my plans.","q_zh":"别人一直让你等时，你会有什么感受？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/c82021191105fc79.m4a"},{"id":"P154","topic":"手写","questions":[{"q":"When would you choose handwriting instead of typing?","a":"I'd choose handwriting for a short personal note or a rough plan. It feels more direct, and I can add arrows or small drawings without worrying about how the page is formatted.","q_zh":"你会在什么情况下选择手写，而不是打字？"},{"q":"Has your handwriting changed since your school days?","a":"Yes, it has become less neat because I type much more than I write by hand. If I slow down, I can still write clearly, but quick notes sometimes look quite untidy.","q_zh":"与学生时期相比，你的字迹发生过变化吗？"}],"tags":["本季与基础补充","可修改样例"],"example_notice":"所有第一人称答案均为可修改练习样例；杭州家乡、迪拜生活、软件开发工作、Marshall名字及Ben/Sara/Alex经历均不代表已核实的用户事实。问句为自行表述的训练题，不是官方完整题库。","audio":"audio/053f87978e956bc9.m4a"}],"part3":[{"id":"P301","topic":"决策","questions":[{"q":"Why do people sometimes ask others to help them make decisions?","a":"Other people can notice risks that we overlook, especially when we feel excited or anxious. Someone considering a new job might ask a friend about the working hours rather than focus only on salary. However, advice should support the decision, not replace it, because the person making the choice has to live with the consequences.","q_zh":"为什么人们有时会请别人帮助自己做决定？"},{"q":"Do people make decisions differently now than in the past?","a":"I think people often have more information available now, but that doesn't always make choosing easier. When booking a hotel, for example, hundreds of reviews may create new doubts instead of resolving them. Earlier decisions might have relied more on personal recommendations. The difference also depends on the decision; family matters still require judgement that an online search cannot provide.","q_zh":"与过去相比，人们现在做决定的方式是否有所不同？"}],"audio":"audio/2efe06913f29e729.m4a"},{"id":"P302","topic":"成功","questions":[{"q":"Is hard work enough to make someone successful?","a":"Hard work matters, but I wouldn't say it guarantees success. A small business owner can work long hours and still struggle if customers don't need the product. They also need sound decisions, useful skills and some opportunities. Effort is valuable because it improves what someone can control, although the final result may depend on circumstances outside their control.","q_zh":"单靠努力就足以让一个人成功吗？"},{"q":"How might a young person's idea of success differ from an older person's?","a":"A younger person might connect success with getting a desirable job or proving their ability. Someone with more experience may value control over their time, such as being able to leave work for a family event. These priorities can overlap, of course. Age may influence what people want, but their responsibilities and personal values probably matter just as much.","q_zh":"年轻人和年长者对成功的理解可能有哪些不同？"}],"audio":"audio/a3b033e53dd116f9.m4a"},{"id":"P303","topic":"快乐","questions":[{"q":"Can buying things make people happy?","a":"Yes, particularly when a purchase solves a problem or supports something they enjoy. A comfortable chair could make working at home more pleasant, for instance. The excitement of owning something new may fade, though. I think purchases contribute more lasting satisfaction when they have a clear purpose, rather than being used to fill every moment of boredom.","q_zh":"买东西能让人快乐吗？"},{"q":"Do children and adults find happiness in different things?","a":"Children may enjoy immediate experiences, like playing a game with a friend, while adults can appreciate something less visible, such as finishing a difficult responsibility. However, I don't think the difference is complete. An adult can still love a simple game, and a child can feel proud of an achievement. Happiness depends on the meaning an experience has for someone.","q_zh":"孩子和成年人会从不同的事物中获得快乐吗？"}],"audio":"audio/4b41a740757c7534.m4a"},{"id":"P304","topic":"名人采访","questions":[{"q":"Why do people enjoy watching interviews with famous people?","a":"An interview can reveal how someone thinks, rather than showing only their public performance. A musician explaining how a song developed may help listeners appreciate it more. Some viewers are simply curious about the person's life. I find interviews more worthwhile when the questions explore their work or choices, although entertainment is a perfectly reasonable reason to watch.","q_zh":"为什么人们喜欢看名人访谈？"},{"q":"Should interviewers treat celebrities differently from ordinary guests?","a":"They may need to prepare differently because a celebrity's work is already familiar to the audience, but basic respect should remain the same. An interviewer can ask a challenging question about a public statement without demanding private family details. Fame shouldn't remove personal boundaries. Equally, an ordinary guest deserves proper research and thoughtful questions, rather than being treated as less interesting.","q_zh":"采访者应该区别对待名人和普通受访者吗？"}],"audio":"audio/77ea05931fd6e023.m4a"},{"id":"P305","topic":"条理","questions":[{"q":"Why do some people find it difficult to stay organised?","a":"Sometimes the problem is an unrealistic system rather than a lack of effort. A person might create a detailed weekly schedule that leaves no room for unexpected tasks, then stop using it after one busy day. I think organisation works better when it fits someone's actual routine. Frequent interruptions can also make maintaining even a simple plan difficult.","q_zh":"为什么有些人觉得保持条理很难？"},{"q":"Is being organised at home the same as being organised at work?","a":"The basic aim is similar: making things easier to find and tasks easier to manage. At work, though, the system usually needs to make sense to other people. A shared folder requires clear names, while a personal drawer can follow someone's own preferences. Home organisation may be more flexible, unless several family members depend on the same arrangement.","q_zh":"在家里做事有条理，与在工作中做事有条理是一回事吗？"}],"audio":"audio/ce085530cc5b22d1.m4a"},{"id":"P306","topic":"噪音","questions":[{"q":"Why can the same noise annoy one person but not another?","a":"People may attach different meanings to a sound. Music from a neighbour's party could feel enjoyable to a guest but frustrating to someone trying to finish an assignment. The timing and the person's activity matter too. A sound doesn't have to be extremely loud to interrupt concentration, although tolerance varies and some people can work comfortably with background noise.","q_zh":"为什么同一种噪音会让某个人烦恼，却不会影响另一个人？"},{"q":"Would you expect noise problems to be different in a city and a village?","a":"I would expect different sources rather than complete silence in one place. A city resident might be disturbed by traffic, while someone in a village could hear machinery or barking dogs. People may also have different expectations of quiet. The important comparison is probably between particular locations and times, since a quiet city street can be calmer than a busy village centre.","q_zh":"你认为城市和乡村遇到的噪音问题会有所不同吗？"}],"audio":"audio/745a5a417dff8838.m4a"},{"id":"P307","topic":"自然空间","questions":[{"q":"Why should cities include parks and other green spaces?","a":"They give residents places to spend time outside without needing to leave the city. A small park can offer somewhere to sit, walk or meet a friend after work. I think that makes neighbourhood life more enjoyable. However, creating a park isn't enough by itself; it needs to be accessible and maintained so people actually feel comfortable using it.","q_zh":"为什么城市应该有公园和其他绿地？"},{"q":"How does visiting a city park differ from visiting a remote natural area?","a":"A city park is usually easier to fit into an ordinary day, while a remote area can offer a stronger sense of getting away. Someone might take a short walk in a park during lunch but plan a whole weekend around a mountain visit. Neither experience is automatically better. The choice depends on available time and what the visitor wants.","q_zh":"去城市公园和去偏远的自然地区有什么不同？"}],"audio":"audio/87d28b05da5f49a2.m4a"},{"id":"P308","topic":"金钱储蓄","questions":[{"q":"Why do some people find it hard to save money?","a":"For some people, essential expenses leave very little to save, so it would be unfair to blame every case on poor discipline. Others may struggle because small purchases are easy to overlook. Ordering extra food several evenings a week, for example, can reduce what remains. The reasons differ, and practical advice needs to match the person's actual situation.","q_zh":"为什么有些人觉得存钱很难？"},{"q":"Should children learn about saving in the same way as adults?","a":"The principle can be similar, but the examples should suit their responsibilities. A child might save pocket money for a toy and learn that choosing one thing means waiting for another. Adults need to think about larger commitments and unexpected expenses. I would introduce the idea gradually, without making children feel responsible for financial pressures that belong to their parents.","q_zh":"孩子应该和成年人用同样的方式学习储蓄吗？"}],"audio":"audio/686dbd658358d9ca.m4a"},{"id":"P309","topic":"儿童学技能","questions":[{"q":"Should schools spend time teaching practical skills?","a":"Yes, because practical tasks can connect classroom learning with everyday life. Preparing a simple meal, for instance, involves following instructions, measuring and working carefully. I wouldn't replace core academic subjects with these activities, though. Schools have limited time, so the most useful approach may be to include practical applications within existing lessons rather than add too many separate courses.","q_zh":"学校应该花时间教授实用技能吗？"},{"q":"How does learning a skill from a parent differ from learning it from a teacher?","a":"A parent may have more opportunities to practise a skill during daily routines, like showing a child how to care for a plant. A teacher can provide a more structured sequence and experience with different learners. Neither is always better. What matters is whether the adult explains clearly, gives useful feedback and allows the child to try independently.","q_zh":"向父母学习一项技能，与向老师学习有什么不同？"}],"audio":"audio/33455594594a7288.m4a"},{"id":"P310","topic":"摄影","questions":[{"q":"Why do people take photographs of ordinary daily activities?","a":"Ordinary moments can become meaningful later, even if they don't seem remarkable at the time. A photograph of friends cooking together may bring back details that a formal group portrait misses. People also use pictures to share their day with others. I think this is understandable, provided taking the photograph doesn't distract everyone from enjoying the actual experience.","q_zh":"为什么人们会拍摄普通的日常活动？"},{"q":"Has phone photography changed the value of professional photography?","a":"It has made taking everyday pictures much easier, but I don't think it removes the need for professional work. At a wedding, for example, guests can capture casual moments while a professional takes responsibility for recording the main events. The difference is partly about reliability and judgement. Some phone users are very skilled, so equipment alone doesn't define quality.","q_zh":"手机摄影是否改变了专业摄影的价值？"}],"audio":"audio/991a0e5b5a06b9ea.m4a"},{"id":"P311","topic":"代际关系","questions":[{"q":"Why can communication between different generations be difficult?","a":"People may assume their own experiences are the normal starting point. A parent could see a stable job as the safest choice, while their child values trying different roles. If neither explains the reasons behind their preference, the discussion can turn into an argument. Different ages don't automatically create conflict, but unspoken expectations can make understanding harder.","q_zh":"为什么不同代际之间的沟通可能比较困难？"},{"q":"Do you think relationships between grandparents and grandchildren are changing?","a":"They can change when families live farther apart or follow different daily routines. A grandparent might now join a birthday through a video call instead of visiting in person. That helps maintain contact, but it doesn't replace every part of spending time together. Some families remain very close, so the change depends more on their circumstances than on age alone.","q_zh":"你认为祖父母与孙辈之间的关系正在变化吗？"}],"audio":"audio/6a9495071d3fb769.m4a"},{"id":"P312","topic":"礼貌倾听","questions":[{"q":"Why is listening an important part of being polite?","a":"Listening shows that you consider the other person's contribution worth your attention. If a colleague explains a problem and you immediately change the subject, they may feel dismissed, even without an insulting word. I think good listening includes asking relevant questions. It doesn't require agreeing with everything, but disagreement is easier to discuss after both people feel understood.","q_zh":"为什么倾听是礼貌的重要组成部分？"},{"q":"Is it ever acceptable to interrupt someone?","a":"Yes, when there is a clear reason, such as preventing a misunderstanding before it affects a decision. In a meeting, someone might politely interrupt to correct a date that everyone is about to use. However, the interruption should be brief and relevant. Repeatedly taking over because you prefer your own ideas is different from helping the conversation stay accurate.","q_zh":"在某些情况下，打断别人说话是否可以接受？"}],"audio":"audio/707483233569fede.m4a"},{"id":"P313","topic":"客户服务","questions":[{"q":"Why do customers sometimes care more about service than price?","a":"Good service can reduce uncertainty and save people time. Someone buying a complicated appliance may value a clear explanation and dependable help if something goes wrong. A slightly lower price may feel less attractive without that support. This won't apply to every purchase, though; for a simple product that customers already understand, price can remain the main concern.","q_zh":"为什么顾客有时更看重服务而非价格？"},{"q":"How does good online customer service differ from good service in a shop?","a":"Online service needs especially clear written information because customers can't easily point to the product or read the assistant's expression. In a shop, an employee can demonstrate a solution immediately. For example, showing how a button works may take seconds in person. Both settings still require listening carefully, but the way an explanation is delivered needs to fit the channel.","q_zh":"优质的线上客服与实体店里的优质服务有什么不同？"}],"audio":"audio/6bb8e47c9c316071.m4a"},{"id":"P314","topic":"手工与机器","questions":[{"q":"Why do some people prefer handmade products?","a":"They may appreciate small differences that show someone worked directly on the object. A handmade bowl can feel personal because its shape or decoration isn't identical to every other one. The maker's story may add meaning too. I wouldn't assume handmade products are always better, though; customers still need to consider whether the item is suitable for its intended use.","q_zh":"为什么有些人更喜欢手工制品？"},{"q":"When are machine-made products a better choice than handmade ones?","a":"They can be a better choice when consistency and large quantities matter. A café buying hundreds of matching cups may prefer products with predictable sizes and prices. A handmade cup might be more appealing as a personal gift. I think the comparison depends on the purpose: efficiency is valuable in one situation, while individuality adds value in another.","q_zh":"在什么情况下，机器生产的产品比手工制品更合适？"}],"audio":"audio/b313ae89e3ed0c35.m4a"},{"id":"P315","topic":"朋友聚会","questions":[{"q":"Why do people enjoy organising gatherings for their friends?","a":"A gathering creates time together that might otherwise be postponed. Busy friends can keep saying they'll meet soon without choosing a date. Organising a simple dinner gives everyone a clear opportunity to reconnect. Some people also enjoy making others feel welcome. However, I think hosting is more enjoyable when the organiser doesn't feel pressured to make every detail perfect.","q_zh":"为什么人们喜欢为朋友组织聚会？"},{"q":"How might a small gathering differ from a large party?","a":"A small gathering makes it easier to have a proper conversation with each person. At a large party, there may be more energy and more opportunities to meet someone new. For a friend who has been going through a difficult week, a quiet dinner might be preferable. The ideal size depends on the purpose and the guests' personalities.","q_zh":"小型聚会与大型派对可能有哪些不同？"}],"audio":"audio/4ed6ef838d35db3c.m4a"},{"id":"P316","topic":"屏幕时间","questions":[{"q":"Why do people sometimes spend longer on their phones than they intended?","a":"There's often no clear finishing point. Someone opens an app to check one message, then sees a video or another conversation and continues. Unlike finishing a chapter, they may not notice a natural place to stop. I think the purpose of using the phone matters too; talking to a friend is different from scrolling without much interest.","q_zh":"为什么人们有时会玩手机超过原本打算的时间？"},{"q":"Should adults and children follow the same rules about screen use?","a":"The rules shouldn't be identical because their responsibilities and independence differ. An adult may need a screen for work, while a child might need guidance about choosing content and balancing activities. However, shared family expectations can help. For example, putting phones away during dinner can apply to everyone, rather than making children follow a rule that adults ignore.","q_zh":"成年人和孩子应该遵守同样的屏幕使用规则吗？"}],"audio":"audio/c7bce18b29f3caa8.m4a"},{"id":"P317","topic":"历史文化","questions":[{"q":"Why is it useful to preserve historic buildings?","a":"They can help people understand how a place developed, beyond what a written description can show. Walking through an old market may reveal its layout and the way people once traded. Historic buildings can also contribute to a neighbourhood's identity. Preservation still requires judgement, though; the building's significance, condition and possible future use all deserve consideration.","q_zh":"保护历史建筑为什么有价值？"},{"q":"Is visiting a historic place better than learning about it online?","a":"Visiting can make the scale and atmosphere more memorable, while online material can explain details that aren't obvious on site. Someone looking at an old fort may enjoy the setting but need a video or guide to understand its purpose. I'd see the two methods as complementary. Travel isn't always possible, and a thoughtful online resource can still teach a great deal.","q_zh":"实地参观历史遗址，比在网上了解它更好吗？"}],"audio":"audio/4973b689cf5c63b7.m4a"},{"id":"P318","topic":"阅读影视","questions":[{"q":"Why do some people prefer a film adaptation to the original book?","a":"A film can make a story easier to enter, especially for someone who finds the book's language demanding. Actors, music and visual details create an immediate impression. Others may simply have less time for reading. I don't think preferring the film means someone appreciates stories less, although an adaptation may leave out parts that readers consider important.","q_zh":"为什么有些人更喜欢改编电影而不是原著？"},{"q":"How does reading a story differ from watching it on screen?","a":"Reading leaves more of the setting and characters' appearance to the reader's imagination. A screen version makes those choices visible and controls the pace more directly. For example, a reader can pause over a character's thoughts, while a film may communicate the same feeling through an expression. Both can be powerful, but they invite the audience to participate differently.","q_zh":"阅读一个故事与在屏幕上观看它有什么不同？"}],"audio":"audio/bec274770d556f02.m4a"},{"id":"P319","topic":"城市交通","questions":[{"q":"Why might people continue driving even when public transport is available?","a":"Availability doesn't always mean convenience. A bus may exist, but it might require a long walk or several transfers for someone's particular journey. A parent collecting children and carrying shopping could find driving easier. I think people compare the whole trip, rather than just the fare. Better connections may encourage change, but individual needs still have to be considered.","q_zh":"即使有公共交通，为什么人们可能仍然选择开车？"},{"q":"Should a city prioritise faster journeys or more comfortable journeys?","a":"I'd try to balance them, but predictable journey times would be my first priority for daily commuting. A comfortable bus is less useful if passengers can't estimate when they'll arrive. For longer trips, seating and space become more important. The best investment therefore depends on the journey and the users, rather than treating speed as the only measure of quality.","q_zh":"城市应该优先让出行更快，还是让出行更舒适？"}],"audio":"audio/95171dd9a195c404.m4a"},{"id":"P320","topic":"运动健康","questions":[{"q":"Why do some people struggle to make time for physical activities?","a":"The difficulty may be fitting an activity into an unpredictable routine. Someone working changing shifts might find it hard to join a class at the same time each week. Others may choose an activity they don't really enjoy, so it becomes another obligation. I think participation is more sustainable when the activity matches the person's interests and available time.","q_zh":"为什么有些人很难抽出时间参加体育活动？"},{"q":"How is taking part in sport different from watching it?","a":"Taking part requires you to make decisions and experience the effort yourself, while watching lets you appreciate other people's skill without that responsibility. Someone playing tennis might be focused on returning the next shot; a spectator can notice the wider pattern of the match. Both can be enjoyable, but the experience of participating depends on finding a suitable level.","q_zh":"参与运动与观看运动比赛有什么不同？"}],"audio":"audio/38099a1d51662299.m4a"},{"id":"P321","topic":"法律环保","questions":[{"q":"Are rules necessary to encourage environmentally responsible behaviour?","a":"Rules can be useful because they set a shared expectation, but they work better alongside practical support. Asking residents to separate rubbish makes more sense when the containers are clearly labelled and easy to reach. I wouldn't expect a rule alone to solve every problem. People also need to understand what to do and why it matters.","q_zh":"鼓励人们采取对环境负责的行为，是否需要规则？"},{"q":"Should environmental policies focus more on individuals or businesses?","a":"I'd focus on both, but give each group responsibilities it can realistically control. A shopper can choose how much to buy, while a company decides how a product is packaged. Asking the shopper to solve the packaging problem alone seems unfair. The balance will vary by issue, and policies should connect the different parts rather than treat them separately.","q_zh":"环保政策应该更侧重个人，还是企业？"}],"audio":"audio/783bacaa66937657.m4a"},{"id":"P322","topic":"语言学习","questions":[{"q":"Why do some language learners understand more than they can say?","a":"Recognising language and producing it are different tasks. A learner may follow a familiar conversation but need extra time to choose words when replying. For example, watching a travel video doesn't require answering an unexpected question. I think speaking practice helps connect knowledge with use, although confidence and familiarity with the topic can also affect what someone manages to say.","q_zh":"为什么有些语言学习者的理解能力强于口头表达能力？"},{"q":"How does learning a language in a classroom differ from using it abroad?","a":"A classroom can provide explanations and a planned sequence, while using the language abroad brings less predictable situations. Ordering food may involve a question the learner hasn't practised. That can reveal useful gaps, but living abroad doesn't automatically produce progress. Someone who rarely speaks outside their own language group may still need deliberate practice and feedback.","q_zh":"在课堂上学一门语言，与在国外使用它有什么不同？"}],"audio":"audio/ed010b9f1269734b.m4a"},{"id":"P323","topic":"科技效率","questions":[{"q":"Does technology always help people work more efficiently?","a":"No, because a tool can create extra steps as well as remove them. A team might adopt a planning app but spend more time updating it than discussing the actual work. I think technology helps when it addresses a clear problem. The useful question is whether the task becomes easier or more reliable, rather than whether the tool looks advanced.","q_zh":"科技总能帮助人们提高工作效率吗？"},{"q":"How might technology change the skills employees need?","a":"If a tool handles routine parts of a task, employees may spend more time checking results and deciding what to do next. For example, software can organise customer messages, but someone still needs to judge which problem is urgent. New skills won't replace every existing one. Understanding the work itself remains important when a tool produces an unexpected answer.","q_zh":"科技可能如何改变员工需要掌握的技能？"}],"audio":"audio/3bd965555b65af70.m4a"},{"id":"P324","topic":"住房建筑","questions":[{"q":"Why do people value different features when choosing a home?","a":"Their routines create different needs. Someone working from home may want a quiet room, while someone commuting every day might prioritise being near a station. A family could place more weight on space for children. I don't think one feature is best for everyone, and the same person's priorities can change when their work or household situation changes.","q_zh":"为什么人们选房时看重的因素不同？"},{"q":"Should new buildings copy traditional styles or use modern designs?","a":"I'd prefer designs that respond to their surroundings without copying the past exactly. A new building in a historic street could use a similar scale while including a modern layout inside. In another location, a more distinct design might fit well. The aim should be a useful building that belongs in its setting, rather than choosing appearance before considering people's needs.","q_zh":"新建筑应该沿用传统风格，还是采用现代设计？"}],"audio":"audio/0bae80ad5002d1e0.m4a"}],"sources":[{"title":"新航道 · 2026年9–12月口语汇编（9月9日）","url":"https://wx.xhd.cn/ielts/yskouyu/968749.html"},{"title":"新东方 · 本季海外题目补充（9月11日）","url":"https://ielts.xdf.cn/202609/15384038.html"},{"title":"老烤鸭 · 本季题目汇编（9月15日）","url":"https://www.laokaoya.com/60391.html"},{"title":"Joe Speaking · 本季海外题目汇编（9月21日）","url":"https://joespeaking.com/ielts-speaking-questions/2026-sep-dec"},{"title":"Lingua Practice · 补充练习主题（9月14日）","url":"https://linguapractice.com/ielts/speaking/recent-questions/2026-september-december"},{"title":"IELTS官方 · 口语考试形式","url":"https://ielts.org/take-a-test/test-types/ielts-academic-test/ielts-academic-format-speaking"},{"title":"IELTS官方 · 口语准备建议","url":"https://ielts.org/news-and-insights/dont-overdo-it-how-to-ace-your-ielts-speaking-test"}]};
